    skos:definition "This U.S. industry comprises establishments primarily engaged in operating hydroelectric power generation facilities. These facilities use water power to drive a turbine and produce electric energy. The electric energy produced in these establishments is provided to electric power transmission systems or to electric power distribution systems." .

<Hnpg2Vu7QY6s1o0LsVrwPw> a owl:Class ;
