        "Priory"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Monastery is a religious house in which members of a religious institute, traditionally monks or nuns, live a common life ordered primarily toward prayer, contemplation, and stability. A monastery embodies a rhythm of liturgical prayer, work, and community according to an approved rule."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "A cloistered monastery dedicates itself primarily to contemplative life."^^xsd:string,
        "A monastery gathers monks for a life centered on liturgical prayer and manual labor."^^xsd:string,
        "A priory serves as a dependent monastic house under an abbey."^^xsd:string,
        "An abbey functions as a monastery with an abbot exercising community leadership."^^xsd:string .

