    skos:definition "Guillain-Barré Syndrome (GBS) is a rare neurological disorder in which the body's immune system mistakenly attacks the peripheral nerves, leading to muscle weakness, numbness, and paralysis. This condition often begins with tingling and weakness in the extremities and can progress rapidly, sometimes affecting respiratory muscles and requiring medical intervention." .

