<R2Ocimo6ph9ym7bvUywOEb> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Residuary Bequest" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R3OI7nrib1LEPtUfn5G5CH> ;
    skos:altLabel "Remainder Bequest",
        "Residual Bequest",
        "Residual Testamentary Gift" ;
    skos:definition "A Residuary Bequest is a provision in a will or trust that designates the distribution of the remainder of an estate after all specific, general, and demonstrative bequests have been fulfilled. This type of bequest ensures that any leftover assets are passed to the named beneficiary or beneficiaries." .

<R2OkACCnZv4q8qWirQKXvs> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Contrition" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RD3Y189V579xUOPZVOl4bdH> ;
    skos:altLabel "Penitential Sorrow"^^xsd:string,
        "Repentance"^^xsd:string,
        "Sorrow for Sin"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Contrition is heartfelt sorrow for sins committed, together with the firm resolve not to sin again. It arises from love of God above all things or, in an imperfect form, from recognition of sin’s gravity and fear of its consequences."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Contrition disposes the penitent to receive forgiveness."^^xsd:string,
        "Perfect contrition arises from love of God above all else."^^xsd:string,
        "True contrition includes the resolve to avoid future sin."^^xsd:string .

<R2QZLqIr6hAvXA4YhEnCVT> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Labor Shortage Verification" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RKY2B2HNSx5K82dgVN6Qn7> ;
    skos:altLabel "PERM Labor Certification" ;
    skos:definition "A Labor Shortage Verification (in the U.S., a PERM labor certification) is a process where employers demonstrate that there are no qualified destination-country (e.g., U.S.) workers available to fill a specific job position and that hiring a foreign worker will not negatively impact the destination country's job market. In the United States, It's a crucial step in the employment-based immigration process, often required for certain employment-based green card applications (EB-2 and EB-3 categories). Employers must go through a series of recruitment efforts and file a Form ETA-9089 with the U.S. Department of Labor to obtain PERM labor certification before proceeding with the green card application for the foreign worker" .

