        "Financial Regulator" ;
    skos:definition "The UK Financial Conduct Authority is an independent regulatory body responsible for overseeing the conduct of financial markets, firms, and individuals in the United Kingdom to ensure consumer protection and market integrity. The FCA regulates financial services providers and enforces rules to maintain fair, transparent, and competitive markets." .

