<R4mSfvmS03kmmWa1Jj5tEm> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Comity Clause Claim" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RC5bITZZ0taJOXwcwS314VU> ;
    skos:altLabel "Comity-Klausel-Anspruch"@de-de,
        "Comity Clause Claim"@en-gb,
        "Reclamación de la Cláusula de Comidad"@es-es,
        "Reclamación de la Cláusula de Comidad"@es-mx,
        "Demande de clause de comité"@fr-fr,
        "תביעת סעיף קומיטי"@he-il,
        "कोमिटी क्लॉज क्लेम"@hi-in,
        "コミティ条項請求"@ja-jp,
        "Reivindicação de cláusula de comitê"@pt-br,
        "礼让条款索赔"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A Comity Clause claim refers to a legal argument based on the Comity Clause of the United States Constitution, asserting that one state must give full faith and credit to the public acts, records, and judicial proceedings of another state. It aims to ensure interstate cooperation and prevent discrimination against individuals or entities based on their out-of-state status." .

<R4t2di94RLtuPT7YOnLoI4> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Sabbath Law Establishment Events" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <ROgocFufRBHZKkFfPDYyYh> ;
    skos:altLabel "Sabbath Observance Establishment"^^xsd:string,
        "Sabbath Regulation Institution Occasions"^^xsd:string,
        "Seventh-Day Rest Law Events"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Sabbath Law Establishment Events comprise the occasions when God instituted and elaborated regulations governing the seventh-day rest, establishing a weekly rhythm of work and worship. These events span from Creation's seventh day through Sinai's commandments to Jesus's authoritative reinterpretation, marking the Sabbath as both memorial of divine creativity and covenant sign between God and Israel."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Biblical scholars analyze Sabbath law establishment events to discern layers of legal development from narrative origins to prophetic reform."^^xsd:string,
        "Catechetical materials use Sabbath law establishment events to teach about rest's spiritual necessity and work's proper limits."^^xsd:string,
        "Catholic liturgical theology traces Sabbath law establishment events to understand how Sunday worship fulfills and transcends Jewish Sabbath observance."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:note """God's Seventh-Day Rest (Genesis 2:2-3)
Sabbath Day Blessing and Sanctification (Genesis 2:3)
Manna and Double-Portion Friday (Exodus 16:22-30)
Fourth Commandment Declaration (Exodus 20:8-11)
Sabbath as Covenant Sign (Exodus 31:13-17)
Death Penalty for Sabbath Violation (Exodus 31:14-15)
Deuteronomic Sabbath Restatement (Deuteronomy 5:12-15)
Sabbath Year and Jubilee Extensions (Leviticus 25)
Prophetic Sabbath Restoration Calls (Isaiah 58:13-14)
Jesus's "Lord of the Sabbath" Declaration (Mark 2:27-28)
Apostolic Sunday Worship Transition (Acts 20:7)"""^^xsd:string .

