<R74zuvPdysbm8JDf0v5JU4n> a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "folio:docketed" ;
    skos:altLabel "docketed",
        "folio:recorded",
        "recorded" ;
    skos:definition "In legal procedures, \"docketed\" refers to the act of formally recording an document (e.g., application, motion) or proceeding (e.g., case, appeal, license proceeding), or other legal matter in the official registry or list of a government agency or court. This signifies that the matter has been officially entered into the system and is scheduled for consideration. A document may be \"filed\" but not \"docketed,\" often because the clerk of court rejected the filing." .

