<R7KQJqS4Z6XfPFkmtMmLE1y> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Schism" ;
    rdfs:comment "In a global Catholic ontology, Schism represents a formal rupture of ecclesiastical union and a rejection of the \"tranquillity of order\" within the Church. It is distinguished from heresy by focusing on the refusal of submission to the Supreme Pontiff or of communion with the members of the Church subject to him, rather than the denial of a specific dogma."^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RDlItdnVxvODqT0Waa9XBcg> ;
    skos:altLabel "Break in Communion"^^xsd:string,
        "Ecclisial Rupture"^^xsd:string,
        "Religious Division"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Schism is the formal withdrawal of submission to the Supreme Pontiff or the refusal of communion with the members of the Church subject to him. This event constitutes a grave wound to the mystical body of Christ and triggers the application of canonical principles to preserve the unity of the faithful."^^xsd:string .

