<R7On4VWw10rNMziVMsyhnz9> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Narrative Objection" ;
    dc:source "Fed. R. Evid. 611" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R7NB9WJzAFK6tIIGmfIj5Ay> ;
    skos:altLabel "Narrative Response Objection",
        "No question before witness",
        "Objection to Overbroad Testimony" ;
    skos:definition "An objection to a narrative is raised when a party in a legal proceeding believes that a witness's response or a question posed by the opposing counsel is too lengthy, lacks focus, or provides information beyond what was requested. This objection aims to prevent the introduction of irrelevant or prejudicial details into the record." .

<R7OsK77qJzadZwNwV39v2XX> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Faithfully Executed Clause Claim" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RDdZDW8VIPVbM8gI4n7Ippf> ;
    skos:altLabel "Anspruch auf treue Ausführungsklausel"@de-de,
        "Faithfully Executed Clause Claim"@en-gb,
        "Reclamación de Cláusula de Ejecución Fiel"@es-es,
        "Reclamación de Cláusula de Ejecución Fiel"@es-mx,
        "Réclamation de clause d'exécution fidèle"@fr-fr,
        "תביעת סעיף ביצוע נאמן"@he-il,
        "ईमानदारी से अंजामित शर्त दावा"@hi-in,
        "忠実に実行された条項の請求"@ja-jp,
        "Reivindicação de cláusula de execução fiel"@pt-br,
        "忠实执行条款索赔"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A Faithfully Executed Clause claim is a legal argument asserting that a government official, typically the President, has failed to faithfully execute the laws as required by the Faithfully Executed Clause of the United States Constitution. This claim contends that the official's actions or omissions in implementing or enforcing the laws are in violation of the constitutional duty to faithfully execute the laws, potentially rendering their actions unconstitutional or invalid." .

