    skos:altLabel "Compulsive Disorder",
        "Compulsive-Obsessive Disorder",
        "OCD",
        "Obsessive Disorder" ;
    skos:definition "Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder (OCD) is a chronic mental health condition characterized by uncontrollable, recurring thoughts (obsessions) and behaviors (compulsions) that the individual feels driven to perform. These obsessions and compulsions can significantly interfere with daily activities and cause distress." .

