        "Sacramental Confession"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Confession of Sins is the act by which the penitent verbally acknowledges sins committed after baptism to a priest in the Sacrament of Penance. Through honest and integral confession, the sinner opens himself or herself to God’s mercy and ecclesial reconciliation."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Confession of sins requires honesty and completeness."^^xsd:string,
        "Through confession, the penitent seeks reconciliation with God."^^xsd:string .

