    skos:definition "A Parishioner is a member of the Christian faithful who belongs to a parish by domicile, quasi-domicile, or stable participation in its sacramental and communal life. A Parishioner participates in the parish’s worship, pastoral care, and mission under the authority of the parish pastor."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "A parishioner regularly attends Sunday Mass at the local parish."^^xsd:string,
        "A parishioner transfers membership after moving to a new parish."^^xsd:string,
        "A parishioner volunteers in parish outreach and charitable programs."^^xsd:string,
        "Parishioners support the parish through prayer, service, and stewardship."^^xsd:string,
        "The parishioner receives the sacraments through the parish community."^^xsd:string ;
