        "עד חומרי"@he-il,
        "पदार्थ साक्षी"@hi-in,
        "物的証人"@ja-jp,
        "Testemunha material"@pt-br,
        "物证证人"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A person who prosecutors believe has evidence of a material fact in a criminal investigation." .

<R7Xnvf9ThDb99RM1dpQnH2L> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Reasonable Act or Omission to Correct" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RCHbjppawvAlt5WcUyfjeN8> ;
    skos:altLabel "Angemessene Handlung oder Unterlassung zur Korrektur"@de-de,
        "Reasonable Act or Omission to Correct"@en-gb,
        "Acto o Omisión Razonable para Corregir"@es-es,
        "Acto u Omisión Razonable para Corregir"@es-mx,
        "Acte ou omission raisonnable pour corriger"@fr-fr,
        "פעולה או התעלמות סבירה לתיקון"@he-il,
        "सुविधाजनक कार्य या सुधार के लिए अनुमोदन या अनुपस्थिति"@hi-in,
        "合理な行為または過失の修正"@ja-jp,
        "Ato ou omissão razoável para correção"@pt-br,
        "合理行为或不作为以纠正"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A \"Reasonable Act or Omission to Correct\" refers to a legal concept within the larger framework of \"Governmental Immunity for Condition of Public Property,\" which allows a government entity to avoid liability for injuries caused by a dangerous condition on public property if they can show that they acted reasonably in attempting to correct the condition or that their decision not to correct the condition was also reasonable." .

<R7Xopvf7NTf5ffUwdT34zFE> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Sappony" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RC1ceWXE3emNHpYlrOvvmxG> .

<R7XpYe4Rz8RjUeP6NgDxbQ> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Corporal Punishment Claims" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R8A3IWnCF4w7p6lvVLLqAQa> ;
    skos:altLabel "Ansprüche wegen körperlicher Züchtigung"@de-de,
        "Corporal Punishment Claims"@en-gb,
        "Reclamaciones de Castigo Corporal"@es-es,
        "Reclamaciones de Castigo Corporal"@es-mx,
        "Réclamations de châtiments corporels"@fr-fr,
        "תביעות על עונש גופני"@he-il,
        "शारीरिक दंड दावे"@hi-in,
        "体罰請求"@ja-jp,
        "Reivindicações de punição corporal"@pt-br,
        "体罚索赔"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A claim made against an educational institution or its staff for the use of physical discipline on a student, falling under the category of Education Liability and specifically related to Corporal Punishment." .

<R7XyscaXi5Cnm09a2Eu2TyI> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Existing Mental, Emotional, Physical Condition" ;
    dc:source "Fed. R. Evid. 803(3)" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R1EbxjQwzgikspixQygdfK> ;
    skos:altLabel "Present State of Mind or Body",
        "Then-Existing Mental, Emotional, or Physical Condition" ;
    skos:definition "Existing Mental, Emotional, or Physical Condition is a hearsay exception that allows the admission of statements that describe the declarant's then-existing state of mind, feeling, sensation, or bodily health. This exception is based on the belief that such statements are reliable because they are made in the moment and are unlikely to be fabricated." .

<R7YShSuPBbr8Gd8UZEmZb8d> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Economic Loss Doctrine" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RuDAbRiNW105SQoqb1XZ4c> ],
        <RCfunX4u69LUQ3gbhckE0oI>,
        <RCzs34uEQI9f4cuWp3bQO0P> ;
    skos:altLabel "Economic Loss Rule",
        "Wirtschaftlicher Verlustgrundsatz"@de-de,
        "Economic Loss Doctrine"@en-gb,
        "Doctrina de la Pérdida Económica"@es-es,
        "Doctrina de la Pérdida Económica"@es-mx,
        "Doctrine des pertes économiques"@fr-fr,
        "תאוריה של הפסד כלכלי"@he-il,
        "आर्थिक हानि डॉक्ट्रिन"@hi-in,
        "経済損失原則"@ja-jp,
        "Doutrina de Perda Econômica"@pt-br,
        "经济损失原则"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "The Economic Loss Doctrine is a legal principle that limits recovery in negligence claims to only economic losses, such as lost profits or property damage, and excludes recovery for personal injury or other non-economic losses." .

<R7YToQxzuXojCNWk2g0gIk8> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Second-Degree Murder" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <R7bP5vwpnavvW5pPJutIvq8> ],
        <R7Ttdyo4FsvaupPKT35Qry0> ;
    skos:altLabel "Depraved Heart Murder",
        "Mord zweiten Grades"@de-de,
        "Second-Degree Murder"@en-gb,
        "Asesinato en segundo grado"@es-es,
        "Homicidio en segundo grado"@es-mx,
        "Meurtre au deuxième degré"@fr-fr,
        "רצח ממעולה שנייה"@he-il,
        "द्वितीय डिग्री हत्या"@hi-in,
        "二度殺人"@ja-jp,
        "Assassinato de segundo grau"@pt-br,
        "二级谋杀"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "The concept of Second-Degree Murder, also known as Depraved Heart Murder, refers to the intentional killing of another person with malice aforethought, but without premeditation or deliberation, and with a reckless disregard for human life." .

<R7YXMd6n1Pa9dmpBWmbf7tI> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Manufacturing Defect" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R8p15egW5el3Go9V1L4obop> ;
    skos:altLabel "Herstellungsfehler"@de-de,
        "Manufacturing Defect"@en-gb,
        "Defecto de fabricación"@es-es,
        "Defecto de fabricación"@es-mx,
        "Défaut de fabrication"@fr-fr,
        "פגם ייצור"@he-il,
        "विनिर्माण दोष"@hi-in,
        "製造上の欠陥"@ja-jp,
        "Defeito de fabricação"@pt-br,
        "制造缺陷"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A manufacturing defect is a type of product defect that occurs when a product is not made according to its intended design, resulting in a dangerous or defective product." .

<R7YZiYE6y1mjgMaElmtVAGl> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Single Asset Real Estate Debtor" ;
    dc:source <https://www.uscourts.gov/services-forms/bankruptcy/bankruptcy-basics/chapter-11-bankruptcy-basics> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R77pHybcEdlO9OmqSuiyWi1> ;
    skos:definition "A Single Asset Real Estate Debtor (SARE Debtor) refers to a specific classification in bankruptcy proceedings for debtors whose primary business involves a single real estate property. This classification impacts how bankruptcy cases are handled, particularly by expediting the process and applying unique rules concerning automatic stays and reorganization plans." .

<R7YZtYSCWULuIY1kc2Nn8Dg> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Contact Name Suffix - J.D. (Juris Doctor)" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RcTA2iQmrtqOnX3WrjJIp8> ],
        <RCOYxInIdB2hOEl2dAlgQQH> ;
    skos:altLabel "Esq.",
        "Esquire",
        "Juris Doctor" ;
    skos:definition "The suffix \"J.D.\" stands for \"Juris Doctor\" and is used after a person's name to signify that they have earned the professional graduate degree in law. This designation indicates the individual's qualifications to practice law in a particular jurisdiction, provided they have passed the bar exam, and is commonly used in legal settings, academic environments, and formal documents." ;
    skos:prefLabel "J.D." .

