    rdfs:subClassOf <R7hDCTMLoPZrFgIFAMlNHvf> ;
    skos:definition "A Stop Sign Violation Claim involves a legal allegation that a driver has failed to make a complete stop at a stop sign as required by traffic regulations, potentially leading to administrative or legal penalties. Such claims are integral to traffic law enforcement and often necessitate evidence review and legal proceedings to resolve." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Failure to Stop Claim" .

