        "ニロ・サハラ語族"@ja-jp,
        "Línguas nilo-saarianas"@pt-br,
        "尼罗-撒哈拉语系"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "Nilo-Saharan languages are a group of languages spoken in parts of Africa, including Sudan, Chad, and Ethiopia." .

<R7mdFwKA6SgDr4v5jLlBWjS> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Uncontested Adoption" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RCw8IC5TbjkV1rxNruwttNL> ;
    skos:definition "An Uncontested Adoption is when all relevant parties agree on the adoption of a child without any opposition. Typically, the biological parents have either voluntarily relinquished their parental rights or have had them legally terminated, allowing the adoption process to proceed smoothly and without legal disputes." .

<R7mf7oh5KrYlGVqeLGW2Hb4> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Birth of Jesus at Bethlehem" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RBlfLOh5T3hwTWxMPyHfXBx> ],
        <R8Q2ik3utpYM1LNPjwbkF4A>,
        <RBcdN3ccRk1SftZVzCrFRw0> ;
    skos:altLabel "Birth of Christ at Bethlehem"^^xsd:string,
        "Birth of the Lord in Bethlehem"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Birth of Jesus at Bethlehem means the historical event in which Jesus Christ was born in Bethlehem of Judea to the Virgin Mary, as narrated in the Gospels. Birth of Jesus at Bethlehem constitutes the concrete historical realization of the Incarnation within salvation history."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Christian tradition commemorates the birth of Jesus at Bethlehem during the celebration of Christmas."^^xsd:string,
        """She gave birth to her first-born Son and wrapped Him in swaddling clothes and laid Him in a manger, because there was no room for them in the place where travelers lodged.
(Luke 2:7)"""^^xsd:string,
        "The Gospel of Luke states that Jesus was born in Bethlehem and laid in a manger."^^xsd:string,
        "The Gospel of Matthew situates Jesus’ birth in Bethlehem during the reign of King Herod."^^xsd:string .

<R7mhIW2MLv6G8EokmXgn4vL> a owl:Class ;
