    skos:definition "Pilgrimage Grounds are sacred places designated or recognized as destinations for pilgrimage due to their association with significant events of faith, saints, relics, apparitions, or enduring devotional practice. Pilgrimage Grounds foster conversion, prayer, penance, and communal worship through intentional sacred travel."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Marian Pilgrimage Grounds"^^xsd:string,
