        "Privileges & Immunities Clause Claim"@en-gb,
        "Reclamo de la Cláusula de Privilegios e Inmunidades"@es-es,
        "Reclamo de la Cláusula de Privilegios e Inmunidades"@es-mx,
        "Réclamation de la clause des privilèges et immunités"@fr-fr,
        "תביעת סעיף הזכויות והחריגים"@he-il,
        "विशेषाधिकार और अवरोधों धारा दावा"@hi-in,
        "特権および免除条項の主張"@ja-jp,
        "Reivindicação da Cláusula de Privilégios e Imunidades"@pt-br,
        "特权和豁免条款索赔"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A Privileges & Immunities Clause claim refers to a legal argument based on the Privileges and Immunities Clause of the United States Constitution, asserting that states cannot discriminate against citizens of other states by denying them fundamental rights and privileges. It aims to protect the rights and equal treatment of individuals traveling or residing in different states within the United States." .

