    skos:definition "Turkeys are large domesticated birds belonging to the species Meleagris gallopavo, commonly raised for their meat. Known for their distinctive fan-shaped tail and wattled neck, turkeys are an important source of poultry, particularly in North America, where they play a central role in traditional meals like Thanksgiving." .

<R7orA1Zzk6GEaKf69iWtbT8> a owl:Class ;
