    skos:definition "Jesus’ Multiplication of the Loaves and Fishes means the miraculous act by which Jesus Christ fed a large multitude by multiplying a small amount of bread and fish. Jesus’ Multiplication of the Loaves and Fishes reveals Christ’s compassion, divine providence, and prefigures the Eucharist."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "The Gospel narratives describe baskets of leftover fragments gathered after the crowd was fed."^^xsd:string,
        "The Gospels recount Jesus feeding five thousand people with five loaves and two fish."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel "Feeding of the Multitude"^^xsd:string .

<R7ov944p22Oy99uqJIz5uvK> a owl:Class ;
