        "Prison Ministry"^^xsd:string,
        "Prison Visitation"^^xsd:string,
        "Reentry Support Ministry"^^xsd:string,
        "Spiritual Support for the Incarcerated"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Visit the Imprisoned is a corporal work of mercy that consists in offering presence, compassion, and support to persons who are incarcerated. Visit the Imprisoned affirms human dignity by recognizing the imprisoned as persons capable of repentance, hope, and restoration."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "A chaplain celebrates liturgy and offers pastoral counsel within a correctional facility."^^xsd:string,
        "A community supports families of the imprisoned through visitation and accompaniment."^^xsd:string,
        "A faith-based organization assists incarcerated persons in preparing for reintegration into society."^^xsd:string,
        "A parish prison ministry visits incarcerated individuals to offer prayer and conversation."^^xsd:string,
        "A volunteer regularly meets with prisoners to provide spiritual encouragement."^^xsd:string .

