<R7qIxdwQJremplPz5qw2WYj> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Commandment 07: You shall not steal." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RDJPdWE32ZF0O3QeYJi5uc> ;
    skos:altLabel "Property Protection Commandment"^^xsd:string,
        "Theft Prohibition Commandment"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "You Shall Not Steal represents the seventh commandment prohibiting the wrongful taking of another's property, protecting rightful ownership and economic justice. This decree establishes respect for legitimate possessions as moral obligation, extending beyond theft to encompass fraud, exploitation, wage theft, and any unjust deprivation of another's goods or labor."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Business ethicists have interpreted this commandment as prohibiting fraudulent accounting, tax evasion, and deceptive business practices."^^xsd:string,
        "Catechists have taught this commandment as requiring restitution and repayment when stolen goods could be returned or compensated."^^xsd:string,
        "Moral theologians have extended this commandment to intellectual property violations including plagiarism and copyright infringement."^^xsd:string,
        "Social justice advocates have applied this commandment to systemic wage theft where employers withheld earned compensation from workers."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:note """Prohibition Statement (Exodus 20:15)
Deuteronomic Restatement (Deuteronomy 5:19)
Theft Restitution Laws (Exodus 22:1-15)
Kidnapping Death Penalty (Exodus 21:16)
Gleaning Rights for Poor (Leviticus 19:9-10, Deuteronomy 24:19-22)
Wage Payment Requirements (Leviticus 19:13, Deuteronomy 24:14-15)
False Weights Prohibition (Leviticus 19:35-36, Deuteronomy 25:13-16)
Landmark Moving Prohibition (Deuteronomy 19:14)
Paul's Work Command (2 Thessalonians 3:10)
Zacchaeus's Fourfold Restitution (Luke 19:8)"""^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel "Seventh Commandment"^^xsd:string .

<R7qJ0ILexZuBxTnTk94Q658> a owl:Class ;
