    skos:altLabel "Parable of the Foolish Rich Man"^^xsd:string,
        "Parable of the Hoarding Landowner"^^xsd:string,
        "Rich Fool Parable"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Parable of the Rich Fool means the teaching in which Jesus Christ describes a wealthy man who stores up earthly goods but dies without regard for God. Parable of the Rich Fool warns against greed and teaches the necessity of being rich toward God rather than relying on material security."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Accumulation of Earthly Wealth"^^xsd:string,
        "Call to Be Rich Toward God"^^xsd:string,
        "Christian moral teaching interprets the parable of the rich fool as a warning against placing trust in possessions rather than God."^^xsd:string,
        "Divine Judgment on Greed"^^xsd:string,
        "The Gospel of Luke recounts a wealthy man planning to store surplus grain only to die that very night."^^xsd:string .

