<R7qjvUfvWoLEUPk8i4rR3Sz> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Collective Work" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R7mMPoEuA9Ja4rODr1LGXcR> ;
    skos:definition "Collective Work in copyright law refers to a work consisting of individual contributions assembled into a collective whole, where each contribution retains its individual copyright but the collection as a whole is also protected. This concept is common in anthologies, encyclopedias, and periodicals, where the collective arrangement is subject to copyright, separate from the individual works." .

