    skos:definition "Calling of the Apostles means the act by which Jesus Christ chose and summoned specific disciples to follow him and share in his mission. Calling of the Apostles establishes the foundational group entrusted with preaching, authority, and leadership in the Church."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Jesus’ selection of the Twelve establishes the apostolic foundation of the Church."^^xsd:string,
        "The Gospels recount Jesus calling Peter and Andrew while they were fishing."^^xsd:string .

