<R7vg1IJx3GqdQTRK269CRUg> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Sin of Thought" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RbxVEZPis7iHhky06utRnR> ;
    skos:altLabel "Mental Sin"^^xsd:string,
        "Sinful Thought"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Sin of Thought is a form of interior sin committed when a person freely consents to a morally disordered thought, desire, or intention. Sin of Thought becomes sinful not by the mere appearance of an idea, but by deliberate acceptance or indulgence of it against right reason and divine law."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "A person consents to prideful thoughts that exalt self over God or neighbor."^^xsd:string,
        "A person cultivates envy by repeatedly comparing himself to others with resentment."^^xsd:string,
        "A person freely entertains lustful thoughts rather than rejecting them."^^xsd:string,
        "A person knowingly dwells on thoughts of harming another and consents to them."^^xsd:string .

