<R7yOhaPNOcL5bh0ZFbKTbOD> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Prayer of St. Francis of Assisi" ;
    dc:source <https://www.xavier.edu/jesuitresource/online-resources/prayer-index/catholic-prayers> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RyTfHxUQPVMUQrtIt1Mycz> ;
    skos:altLabel "Franciscan Prayer for Peace"^^xsd:string,
        "Make Me an Instrument of Your Peace"^^xsd:string,
        "Prayer for Peace"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Prayer of St. Francis of Assisi is a devotional prayer that asks God to make the petitioner an instrument of peace through love, forgiveness, faith, hope, and joy. It expresses the Franciscan call to self-giving charity, reconciliation, and trust in God through humble service."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "At the conclusion of a retreat, the director invited participants to pray the Prayer of St. Francis of Assisi as a commitment to service."^^xsd:string,
        "During a service for reconciliation, the assembly prayed the Prayer of St. Francis of Assisi together."^^xsd:string,
        "In times of conflict, she recited the Prayer of St. Francis of Assisi to seek peace and humility."^^xsd:string,
        """Lord, make me a channel of thy peace,
that where there is hatred, I may bring love;
that where there is wrong,
I may bring the spirit of forgiveness;
that where there is discord, I may bring harmony;
that where there is error, I may bring truth;
that where there is doubt, I may bring faith;
that where there is despair, I may bring hope;
that where there are shadows, I may bring light;
that where there is sadness, I may bring joy.
Lord, grant that I may seek rather to
comfort than to be comforted;
to understand, than to be understood;
to love, than to be loved.
For it is by self-forgetting that one finds.
It is by forgiving that one is forgiven.
It is by dying that one awakens to Eternal Life."""^^xsd:string,
        """Lord, make me an instrument of your peace. 
Where there is hatred, let me sow love.
Where there is injury, pardon.
Where there is doubt, faith.
Where there is despair, hope.
Where there is darkness, light.
Where there is sadness, joy.

O Divine Master,
grant that I may not so much seek to be consoled, as to console;
to be understood, as to understand;
to be loved, as to love.
For it is in giving that we receive.
It is in pardoning that we are pardoned,
and it is in dying that we are born to Eternal Life."""^^xsd:string .

