<R84O5MFBD4yVpz5EoTditqc> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Systemic Vasculitis" ;
    dc:source <https://www.ssa.gov/disability/professionals/bluebook/14.00-Immune-Adult.htm#14_03> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RBJ0dgV4Z2Xk7aGfJt2nSj7> ;
    skos:altLabel "Multi-Organ Vascular Inflammation",
        "Systemic Vasculitic Syndrome",
        "Vascular Inflammatory Disease" ;
    skos:definition "Vasculitis is an inflammation of blood vessels. It may occur acutely in association with adverse drug reactions, certain chronic infections, and occasionally, malignancies. More often, it is chronic and the cause is unknown. Symptoms vary depending on which blood vessels are involved. Systemic vasculitis may also be associated with other autoimmune disorders; for example, SLE or dermatomyositis." .

<R84Rns2UsbgWnMnQCnF0VpU> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Seizure" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R73Uo5x4VyfiOXt6i4R256t> ;
    skos:altLabel "Expropriation",
        "Taking" ;
    skos:definition "Seizure, within the legal domain, refers to the act of legally taking possession of persons or property by law enforcement or other authorities, typically because the persons or property are suspected of being involved in, or evidence of, illegal activity." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Confiscation" .

<R84VgtWYZcnGVQFEdADLhxu> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Granulocytopenia" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R7WKt0VAzs1NaH3XvbaWYIZ> ;
    skos:altLabel "Granulocyte Deficiency",
        "Low Granulocyte Count",
        "Neutropenia" ;
    skos:definition "Granulocytopenia is a condition characterized by an abnormally low level of granulocytes, a type of white blood cell crucial for fighting infections. This deficiency can lead to increased susceptibility to infections, delayed wound healing, and other complications due to the impaired immune response." .

<R84WSMY4efMvESQh729h2Kp> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Involuntary Intoxication" ;
    dc:source "New Mexico Criminal Jury Instruction 14-5106",
        "Oklahoma Jury Instructions, Ouji-cr 8-42",
        "State v. Davis, 2021 Ohio 237 (Ohio Ct. App. Jan. 29, 2021)." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R8mREFTbCVNHGAdqneLSd0d> ;
    skos:definition "Involuntary intoxication is a legal defense where the defendant claims they were forced or unknowingly induced to consume intoxicating substances, rendering them unable to understand the nature of their actions. This defense can negate criminal liability if the intoxication prevented the formation of intent or awareness necessary to commit the crime." .

