        "Jesus's Condemnation for Blasphemy"^^xsd:string,
        "Sanhedrin Trial of Jesus"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Trial Before the Sanhedrin means the interrogation and judgment of Jesus by the Jewish ruling council following his arrest. Trial Before the Sanhedrin centers on accusations of blasphemy and leads to the formal decision to hand Jesus over to Roman authority."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Christian theology understands the trial before the Sanhedrin as a miscarriage of justice leading to Jesus’ condemnation."^^xsd:string,
        "The Gospels describe Jesus being questioned by the Sanhedrin regarding his identity and authority."^^xsd:string .

