        "Moderation of Appetite"^^xsd:string,
        "Self-Control"^^xsd:string,
        "Self-Mastery"^^xsd:string,
        "Sobriety"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Temperance is the cardinal virtue that moderates attraction to pleasure and provides balance in the use of created goods. Temperance orders desires according to right reason, preserving freedom and fostering self-mastery."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Temperance helps a person resist compulsive or addictive behavior."^^xsd:string,
        "Temperance moderates eating and drinking to preserve health and freedom."^^xsd:string,
        "Temperance orders enjoyment so that it serves human flourishing."^^xsd:string,
        "Temperance restrains excess in the pursuit of pleasure."^^xsd:string,
        "Temperance supports balanced use of technology and entertainment."^^xsd:string .

