    skos:definition "Atheism is the belief or doctrine that asserts the non-existence of deities or a supreme being. In legal contexts, it may pertain to the protection of non-religious individuals' rights, ensuring freedom from religious impositions, or the recognition of atheism as a legitimate philosophical stance." ;
    skos:example "Secular morality" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Humanism" .

<R8DuzCmVDKzwxCeemVcTUU0> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "This is My Body" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R83qv1lc6haj7YdVbcf75oC> ;
    skos:altLabel "Consecratory Words Over the Bread"^^xsd:string,
        "Hoc Est Corpus Meum"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "“This Is My Body” is the declarative phrase spoken by Jesus over the bread at the Last Supper, identifying it with his body. It functions as the central formula within the institution narrative that grounds the Eucharist’s sacramental meaning."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "A catechetical lesson connected “This Is My Body” to the memorial character of the Eucharist."^^xsd:string,
        "A theology course analyzed “This Is My Body” as the core phrase of the institution narrative."^^xsd:string,
        "During the Eucharistic Prayer, the celebrant pronounced “This Is My Body” over the bread."^^xsd:string .

