<R8VTnoSkN2YchcU4wYNmqp7> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Blessed Are Those Who Mourn" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RDS4ZvoTuxk7hu7zuyJRyoR> ;
    skos:altLabel "Second Beatitude"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Blessed Are Those Who Mourn means the beatitude in which Jesus Christ declares blessed those who grieve, whether for personal loss, sin, or the brokenness of the world. Blessed Are Those Who Mourn promises divine consolation and reveals God’s nearness to human suffering."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Christian theology interprets this beatitude as God’s promise of consolation to those who suffer and repent."^^xsd:string,
        "The Gospel of Matthew records Jesus proclaiming, “Blessed are those who mourn, for they shall be comforted.”"^^xsd:string .

<R8VWI7MXtnSXaP6rHFs1Tbh> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Environmental Permit Violation Claim" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RBeZkopwGsxt3K5BXOgNBNF> ;
    skos:definition "An Environmental Permit Violation Claim is a legal action alleging that an individual, company, or entity has failed to comply with the terms and conditions of an environmental permit issued by a regulatory authority. Such claims typically assert that the permit holder has exceeded allowed emission levels, discharged prohibited substances, or failed to implement required environmental protection measures." .

