<R8XEIPN0gdrO2Fgwj05iPvs> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Myelofibrosis" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R7WKt0VAzs1NaH3XvbaWYIZ> ;
    skos:altLabel "Myelofibrotic Syndrome" ;
    skos:definition "Myelofibrosis is a rare type of bone marrow disorder characterized by the replacement of normal bone marrow tissue with fibrous scar tissue. This leads to the impaired production of blood cells and can result in anemia, enlarged spleen (splenomegaly), and other systemic symptoms." .

<R8XFIHIjOcoXRc5EiJhgBok> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Prayer to Our Lady Guadalupe Apostolate" ;
    dc:source <https://www.xavier.edu/jesuitresource/online-resources/prayer-index/catholic-prayers> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RCA6zlBfTqVXfLM0xipUkZf>,
        <RyTfHxUQPVMUQrtIt1Mycz> ;
    skos:altLabel "Guadalupe Consecration Prayer"^^xsd:string,
        "Our Lady of Guadalupe Apostolate Prayer"^^xsd:string,
        "Prayer to Our Lady of Guadalupe"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Prayer to Our Lady Guadalupe Apostolate is a Marian prayer that entrusts individuals and communities to Our Lady of Guadalupe, seeking faithfulness, justice, charity, and growth in Christ. It consecrates hearts to Mary’s Immaculate Heart and commits efforts to the building of God’s Kingdom among the Americas and all nations."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example """Our Lady of Guadalupe, Mother of the Americas and all Nations.
Look in compassion on your children.
We need your help to keep the faith, to preserve the family,
to work for justice with forbearance and forgiveness, to live and grow in charity.

With our whole heart we consecrate ourselves to Your Immaculate Heart.
Direct our abilities, our efforts, to the furthering of the Kingdom of God on earth.

May we do our part to make ourselves, the Americas and all Nations more worthy of the love you show us. Looking on your image, may we grow in the likeness of your son, our Lord Jesus Christ. Amen."""^^xsd:string .

<R8XI2NPtg7ZMadfULv2SLS0> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Cultural Rights" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RBJlYzE4ZY14dTEghzbbMHg> ;
    skos:definition "Cultural rights pertain to the freedom and ability of individuals or groups to maintain, develop, and share their culture, language, and heritage. These rights are often protected by international law and may include access to cultural and educational resources, protection of cultural heritage, and freedom to engage in cultural practices" .

