    skos:altLabel "Countervailing Tariff Payment",
        "Trade Remedy Duty Payment",
        "Trade Subsidy Duty Payment" ;
    skos:definition "A Countervailing Duty (CVD) Payment refers to the payment made by importers to the government as a result of countervailing duties imposed on imported goods that benefit from foreign government subsidies. These payments aim to counteract the effects of such subsidies, ensuring fair competition for domestic producers." ;
    skos:prefLabel "CVD Payment" .

