<R8hMLiAtJxKxraEG4xHqW1w> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Immigration Lottery" ;
    dc:description "An immigration lottery is a system used by some countries, including the United States, to allocate visas or permits to foreign nationals based on a random selection process. In the U.S., the H1B lottery is a well-known example, where a limited number of H1B visas for skilled workers are distributed through a random selection process due to high demand exceeding the annual cap." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RBEXxc9B6kR2p0BMwGjhWGW> ;
    skos:example "Diversity Lottery",
        "H1B Visa Lottery",
        "Visa Lottery" .

