    skos:definition "The \"Right to be Forgotten\" refers to an individual's legal ability to request the removal of personal information from digital platforms or search engine results. Originating in the European Union, this right aims to allow people to control their digital footprint by deleting or delisting information that is outdated, irrelevant, or no longer applicable." .

