    skos:definition "A Roman Curia Dicastery is a central administrative body through which the Roman Pontiff exercises his supreme pastoral and governing authority over the universal Church. Each dicastery carries out specific functions of governance, doctrine, discipline, or service in the pope’s name."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Curial dicasteries act with authority delegated by the Roman Pontiff."^^xsd:string,
        "Dicasteries assist the pope in governing the universal Church."^^xsd:string,
        "The Dicastery for the Doctrine of the Faith safeguards Catholic doctrine."^^xsd:string .

