<R8nMXQ6k46QexNTIdUvvr4k> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Condition" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R9abezigCOxFsNH1QItgXgB>,
        <RClhbl4E1TJp9LygIXewIhn> ;
    skos:altLabel "Applicability Criterion"^^xsd:string,
        "Circumstance"^^xsd:string,
        "Criterion"^^xsd:string,
        "IF/THEN"^^xsd:string,
        "Precondition"^^xsd:string,
        "Prerequisite"^^xsd:string,
        "Qualification"^^xsd:string,
        "Requirement"^^xsd:string,
        "Stipulation"^^xsd:string,
        "Triggering Fact"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "A condition is a stated requirement or circumstance that must hold true for a moral norm, ecclesial directive, or canonical rule to apply in a particular case. A condition limits, triggers, or modifies an obligation, permission, prohibition, or right by specifying when, to whom, and in what circumstances the norm binds."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "\"If X then Y\" — the \"X\" is the Condition"^^xsd:string,
        "If a Catholic has a serious medical reason, then the Catholic does not fast on the required day."^^xsd:string,
        "If a parish’s policy requires parental consent, then the parish must request the parent’s signature before enrolling a minor."^^xsd:string,
        "If a penitent expresses sincere contrition, then the confessor may grant absolution."^^xsd:string,
        "If a person lacks the use of reason, then the person does not incur a canonical penalty that requires imputability."^^xsd:string .

