<R8rGoAgxS9Chat0iImC4Y1d> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Crowning with Thorns" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RD0JfBltrTwUJkeYjw8iN1P>,
        <RDxAHb6WWxvwiBtuiLOfgfr> ;
    skos:altLabel "Crown of Thorns"^^xsd:string,
        "Mock Coronation of Christ"^^xsd:string,
        "Mockery of Jesus as King"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Crowning with Thorns means the act by which Roman soldiers mocked Jesus Christ by placing a crown of thorns on his head and treating him as a false king. Crowning with Thorns reveals both the depth of Christ’s humiliation and the paradoxical truth of his kingship."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Christian devotion reflects on the crowning with thorns as a revelation of Christ’s suffering kingship."^^xsd:string,
        "The Gospels describe soldiers placing a crown of thorns on Jesus’ head and mocking him."^^xsd:string,
        """They stripped off His clothes and wrapped Him in a scarlet military cloak. Weaving a crown out of thorns they fixed it on His head, and stuck a reed in His right hand …
(Matthew 27:28-29)"""^^xsd:string .

<R8rIjfy8ZkiLZ0gcCDwtdYc> a owl:Class ;
