    skos:definition "Arthropods are a diverse phylum of invertebrate animals known as Arthropoda, characterized by their exoskeleton, segmented bodies, and jointed appendages. This group includes insects, arachnids, crustaceans, and myriapods, and they are found in virtually every habitat on Earth, playing crucial ecological roles." ;
