    rdfs:subClassOf <R79ZRcChNA1jEORJLsPWYSv> ;
    skos:definition "Public Benefit Diversion Objective refers to policy goals aimed at reducing dependency on long-term public assistance by encouraging alternative means of support, such as employment or private aid. Methods can include offering lump-sum payments, vouchers, or services like job training and placement to encourage individuals to transition away from ongoing public benefit programs." .

