<R9CPDrfJ7JlM6AylZm3RngF> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Not Work Authorized" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R8N4pMIOhTNbqcmDczSephq> ;
    skos:definition "In the context of immigration law, \"Not Work Authorized\" refers to an individual who does not have the legal permission to be employed in a specific country. Under U.S. law, individuals in certain visa categories or those without legal status are considered \"not work authorized,\" and employers could face penalties for employing such individuals." .

<R9CPTzQXRonakaswNB7cgH9> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Audiobook" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R9r2XYxmAiksCgeIwOht0sP> ;
    skos:altLabel "Audio Literature",
        "Narrated Book",
        "Recorded Book",
        "Spoken Book" ;
    skos:definition "An Audiobook is a spoken word recording of a book or other written material, narrated and often enhanced with sound effects or music, intended for playback on digital devices, CDs, or other media. Protected under copyright law, audiobooks grant the narrators and producers exclusive rights to reproduce, distribute, and publicly perform the recorded content." .

<R9CVPHajerdkWrt3R77smqg> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Interjurisdictional Child Custody and Jurisdiction Claim" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RZm4akQHkbU4y4YWTSSjrO> ;
    skos:altLabel "UCCJEA Claim" ;
    skos:definition "An Interjurisdictional Child Custody and Jurisdiction Claim pertains to legal proceedings in cases involving child custody and which state's court has authority to make custody decisions. When parents live in different states, jurisdictional rules defined by the Uniform Child Custody Jurisdiction and Enforcement Act (UCCJEA) or other relevant laws determine which state's court can handle the custody case. These claims are essential in ensuring that custody disputes are resolved appropriately and in compliance with interstate legal frameworks." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Interstate Child Custody and Jurisdiction Claim" .

