<R9Cj1A31dy70CbB8b6Uzqh9> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Entrepreneurial Buyer" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RhUwaBjg0AFfnJkZgYorpG> ;
    skos:altLabel "Unternehmerischer Käufer"@de-de,
        "Entrepreneurial Buyer"@en-gb,
        "Comprador Emprendedor"@es-es,
        "Comprador Emprendedor"@es-mx,
        "Acheteur entrepreneur"@fr-fr,
        "קונה יזמותי"@he-il,
        "उद्यमी खरीदार"@hi-in,
        "起業家バイヤー"@ja-jp,
        "Comprador empreendedor"@pt-br,
        "创业买家"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "An entrepreneurial buyer is an individual or entity that engages in mergers and acquisitions with the primary goal of acquiring a business to actively manage and grow. These buyers often possess industry-specific knowledge, skills, or experience that enable them to identify opportunities and add value to the target company. Unlike financially driven buyers who focus mainly on generating financial returns, entrepreneurial buyers are more likely to take a hands-on approach, seeking to build and develop the acquired business for the long term, often driven by a strategic vision or passion for the industry." .

<R9CjPGdKf66GPkEst2jYGk8> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "New York City Court - Yonkers" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RCz0OhGJQscjwPvw2jQBP63> ;
    skos:definition "A court located in Yonkers, New York that operates under the jurisdiction of the New York City Court." .

<R9CkwL8sW1mOa5qWVeJb7i3> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Travel Document Number" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <ROEhQluRR7rfqDyDYvJ3Dd> ;
    skos:definition "A Travel Document Number refers to a unique identifier assigned to a travel document, such as a visa or refugee travel document, by the issuing authority. This number is used for verification and identification purposes during international travel and border crossings, and it is required for various legal and administrative processes related to travel." .

<R9CppF8ctgc9584B4NEsb7Y> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Hodgkin Lymphoma" ;
    dc:source <https://www.ssa.gov/disability/professionals/bluebook/13.00-NeoplasticDiseases-Malignant-Adult.htm#13_05> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RCkVEfL4H41pColicGhkXJb> ;
    skos:altLabel "Reed-Sternberg Cell Lymphoma" ;
    skos:definition "Hodgkin lymphoma is a type of cancer that originates in the lymphatic system, characterized by the presence of Reed-Sternberg cells. It typically begins in the lymph nodes and can spread to other organs, requiring specific treatment approaches distinct from those for non-Hodgkin lymphomas." .

<R9CsDr2C4jiZvVKIrb12R4A> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "New Mexico Magistrate Court - Eddy County" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RDSK8CbOPdmMwMyMIlw8pdO> ;
    skos:definition "A court located in Eddy County, New Mexico that has limited jurisdiction over certain types of cases." .

<R9CviKLACLe1HEP2cShDoPW> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Non-Hearsay Document Objective" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R4nwMYlRLa9aP9pKWIZEE> ;
    skos:altLabel "Document Reliability Principle" ;
    skos:definition "The non-hearsay document objective is the legal principle that certain documents are admissible as evidence in court without being considered hearsay, due to their inherent reliability. These documents, such as business records, public records, and learned treatises, are deemed trustworthy because they are created and maintained in the regular course of activities and are used for important purposes." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Reliable Document Standard" .

<R9Cw8CmXhnaMRuej3PNXdDA> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Presentment Clause Claim" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RDkqXQLaqeFlhG4isnkHJuv> ;
    skos:altLabel "Anspruch aus der Vorlageklausel"@de-de,
        "Presentment Clause Claim"@en-gb,
        "Reclamo de la Cláusula de Presentación"@es-es,
        "Reclamo de la Cláusula de Presentación"@es-mx,
        "Réclamation de la clause de présentation"@fr-fr,
        "תביעת סעיף ההצגה"@he-il,
        "प्रस्तुति धारा दावा"@hi-in,
        "提示条項請求"@ja-jp,
        "Reivindicação da Cláusula de Apresentação"@pt-br,
        "呈现条款索赔"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A Presentment Clause claim refers to a legal argument challenging the constitutionality of a law based on the requirements outlined in the Presentment Clause of the United States Constitution. This claim asserts that a law is invalid because it was not properly presented to the President for signature or veto, violating the constitutional process for enacting legislation and potentially rendering it unconstitutional." .

<R9Cy2HyrxJFo8tk0VgAkLKi> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Friedreich’s Ataxia" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RkvRD1NfpM4aO12DEEarGf> ;
    skos:altLabel "Friedreich Ataxia",
        "Hereditary Spinocerebellar Degeneration" ;
    skos:definition "Friedreich’s ataxia is a rare, inherited degenerative disorder that primarily affects the nervous system and the spinal cord. It is characterized by progressive loss of coordination, muscle weakness, and gait disturbances due to the degeneration of spinal cord pathways and cerebellum." .

<R9D00mxrkbEo2ZeuWmb92Aw> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Corporate President" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RCwdLsWxoa7TqpUv5hIYwzW> ;
    skos:altLabel "President" ;
    skos:definition "A Corporate President is a senior executive often responsible for overseeing the day-to-day operations of a company and implementing strategic initiatives set by the board of directors. The President often acts as the second-highest-ranking officer in a company, reporting directly to the Chief Executive Officer (CEO) or, in some cases, the board." .

