<R9GZaacP4QJQYO4MD3zSnCm> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Tithing Law Institution Events" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <ROgocFufRBHZKkFfPDYyYh> ;
    skos:altLabel "Tenth-Offering Law Establishment Events"^^xsd:string,
        "Tenth-Portion Commandment Events"^^xsd:string,
        "Tithe Regulation Institution"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Tithing Law Institution Events encompass the occasions when God established regulations requiring the contribution of one-tenth of produce, livestock, and income to support worship and the poor. These events span from patriarchal voluntary offerings through Mosaic mandatory requirements to prophetic critiques and Jesus's affirmation of justice alongside tithing, defining the community's material obligations toward God and neighbor."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Biblical scholars analyze tithing law institution events to trace economic support systems for priests, Levites, widows, orphans, and strangers."^^xsd:string,
        "Catholic stewardship programs reference tithing law institution events to encourage proportional giving while acknowledging Christian freedom from legal obligation."^^xsd:string,
        "Homilies connect tithing law institution events to contemporary discussions about charitable giving and supporting Church ministries."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:note """Abraham's Tithe to Melchizedek (Genesis 14:18-20)
Jacob's Tithe Vow at Bethel (Genesis 28:20-22)
Levitical Tithe Institution (Leviticus 27:30-33)
Annual Festival Tithe (Deuteronomy 14:22-27)
Triennial Poor Tithe (Deuteronomy 14:28-29)
Tithe of Livestock Regulations (Leviticus 27:32)
Numbers' Priestly Tithe (Numbers 18:21-32)
Nehemiah's Tithe Restoration (Nehemiah 10:37-39)
Malachi's Tithe Rebuke (Malachi 3:8-10)
Jesus's Tithe and Justice Teaching (Matthew 23:23)
Pharisee's Tithing Boast (Luke 18:12)"""^^xsd:string .

<R9GaS9pNRiLf8ucevJN7bih> a owl:Class ;
