        "Pastors oversee parish staff and ministries."^^xsd:string,
        "The bishop appoints a pastor for a defined term or indefinitely."^^xsd:string,
        "The pastor governs the parish under the authority of the diocesan bishop."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel "Parish Priest"^^xsd:string .

<R9MEf8HjgrmW3baeXYLpox6> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Jesus' Calming of the Storm" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R8eB4tGcIUItbvkSlnjfbOw> ;
    skos:altLabel "Calming of the Storm by Jesus"^^xsd:string,
        "Miracle on the Sea of Galilee"^^xsd:string,
        "Still­ing of the Storm"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Jesus’ Calming of the Storm means the miraculous act by which Jesus Christ rebuked the wind and the sea, bringing sudden calm during a storm on the Sea of Galilee. Jesus’ Calming of the Storm reveals Christ’s divine authority over creation and calls his disciples to faith amid fear."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Christian theology interprets the calming of the storm as a sign of Christ’s lordship over creation and fear."^^xsd:string,
        "Questioning of the Disciples’ Faith"^^xsd:string,
        "Rebuke of the Wind and Sea"^^xsd:string,
        "The Gospels recount Jesus calming a violent storm while his disciples were in a boat."^^xsd:string .

