<R9NnIby2ar5BVIQCuaM9oP1> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Tearing of the Temple Veil" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RBIF8SqULlcUju99hpRYHBh> ;
    skos:altLabel "Opening of Access to the Holy of Holies"^^xsd:string,
        "Rending of the Temple Veil"^^xsd:string,
        "Sign of the New Covenant"^^xsd:string,
        "The Gospel of Matthew reports that the veil of the Temple was torn in two from top to bottom at Jesus’ death."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Tearing of the Temple Veil means the rending of the veil of the Jerusalem Temple at the moment of Jesus Christ’s death on the cross, as recorded in the Synoptic Gospels. Tearing of the Temple Veil signifies the definitive access to the Father opened through Christ’s sacrifice and the fulfillment and transformation of the Old Covenant."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Christian theology interprets the tearing of the Temple veil as a sign that Christ’s sacrifice grants direct access to God."^^xsd:string .

