<R9TPU4OEQMZKml3qNqYtB8E> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "From the Breastplate of St. Patrick" ;
    dc:source <https://www.xavier.edu/jesuitresource/online-resources/prayer-index/catholic-prayers> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RyTfHxUQPVMUQrtIt1Mycz> ;
    skos:altLabel "Christ Be With Me Prayer"^^xsd:string,
        "Lorica of St. Patrick"^^xsd:string,
        "St. Patrick’s Breastplate"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "From the Breastplate of St. Patrick is an excerpted prayer invoking Christ’s abiding presence in every dimension of life, drawing from the ancient Irish hymn traditionally attributed to Saint Patrick. It expresses trust in Christ’s protection, guidance, and indwelling presence amid peace and danger."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "At morning prayer, he recited From the Breastplate of St. Patrick to seek Christ’s protection throughout the day."^^xsd:string,
        """Christ be with me, Christ within me,
Christ behind me, Christ before me,
Christ beside me, Christ to win me,
Christ to comfort and restore me.
Christ beneath me, Christ above me,
Christ in quiet, Christ in danger,
Christ in hearts of all that love me,
Christ in mouth of friend and stranger."""^^xsd:string,
        "During a retreat on Celtic spirituality, the group prayed From the Breastplate of St. Patrick together."^^xsd:string,
        "In a moment of fear, she repeated lines from From the Breastplate of St. Patrick for reassurance.e"^^xsd:string .

