<R9Uhwom9TKZx0L9euy4pyZ8> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Just Compensation Clause Claim" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RDwajUPdKVdK5tlwiUjmNzG> ;
    skos:altLabel "Takings Clause Claim",
        "Anspruch auf gerechte Entschädigungsklausel"@de-de,
        "Just Compensation Clause Claim"@en-gb,
        "Reclamación de Cláusula de Compensación Justa"@es-es,
        "Reclamación de Cláusula de Compensación Justa"@es-mx,
        "Réclamation de clause de juste indemnisation"@fr-fr,
        "תביעת סעיף פיצוי הוגן"@he-il,
        "बस्तित्वाधिकार धारा दावा"@hi-in,
        "公正な補償条項の請求"@ja-jp,
        "Reivindicação de cláusula de compensação justa"@pt-br,
        "公正补偿条款索赔"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A Just Compensation Clause claim is a legal assertion related to the Fifth Amendment of the United States Constitution, which states that private property cannot be taken for public use without just compensation. If the government takes private property for public use and the property owner believes they have not received fair market value or other appropriate compensation, they may file a Just Compensation Clause claim to seek additional compensation or challenge the taking." .

