        "Amount in Controversy - expressed as \"up to\""@en-gb,
        "Cantidad en controversia - expresada como \"hasta\""@es-es,
        "Monto en controversia - expresado como \"hasta\""@es-mx,
        "Montant en litige - exprimé comme \"jusqu'à\""@fr-fr,
        "סכום בסכסוך - מובא כ\"עד\""@he-il,
        "विवाद में राशि - \"तक\" के रूप में व्यक्त की गई"@hi-in,
        "争議金額 - 「最大で」表現される"@ja-jp,
        "Valor da controvérsia - expresso como \"até\""@pt-br,
        "争议金额 - 表示为“最高”"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "The maximum amount in controversy, where the actual amount in dispute is below that maximum. Example: Small-claims courts (also known as \"conciliation courts\" frequently have a maximum amount of controversy (e.g., $1,000 or $10,000) — over which the case must be argued in a higher court (e.g., state district court)." .

