    skos:definition "A positive youth development activity is an action or program designed to promote the healthy development and well-being of young people, particularly in areas such as education, social skills, and emotional regulation. This concept is specifically related to the conditions that parents must meet as part of a criminal disposition." .

<R9W9JEOuk0H3iu0X5kmhYoi> a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "folio:overruled" ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf <RdpSPh3bFHYrQ3vYPDwJYB> ;
    skos:altLabel "disavowed",
        "overruled" ;
    skos:definition "In legal practice, \"overruled\" refers to the action of a higher court setting aside or nullifying the decision of a lower court or an earlier court. Or it could apply to a judge overruling an evidentiary objection. This denotes a rejection of the previous decision or objection based on legal grounds, signaling a different interpretation or application of the law." ;
    skos:example "Appellate Court overruled Trial Court",
        "Trial Court overruled Plaintiff's evidentiary objection" ;
    skos:prefLabel "folio:disavowed" .

