<R9WQHjLVPhDY3cjrrzxxeq2> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Prayer for the Year of Faith" ;
    dc:source <https://www.xavier.edu/jesuitresource/online-resources/prayer-index/catholic-prayers> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RyTfHxUQPVMUQrtIt1Mycz> ;
    skos:altLabel "Faith Renewal Prayer"^^xsd:string,
        "Prayer for Renewal of Faith"^^xsd:string,
        "Year of Faith Prayer"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Prayer for the Year of Faith is a prayer promulgated to support the Church’s celebration of the Year of Faith, asking for renewal of belief, deeper conversion, and joyful witness to the Gospel. It emphasizes growth in faith through Scripture, the sacraments, charity, and communion with the Church."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "At the opening of catechetical sessions, the parish recited the Prayer for the Year of Faith together."^^xsd:string,
        "During a diocesan celebration, the bishop led the Prayer for the Year of Faith to encourage renewed belief."^^xsd:string,
        """Eternal God, you called your Church at the Second Vatican Council to
stir into flame afresh riches of grace that abide in her heart, and bid
us seek from you a new and fiery Pentecost. In fidelity to this call,
sanctify your Church by a new outpouring of the Holy Spirit, that we
might set the world ablaze with liberating truth and radiant beauty of
your beloved Son, Jesus Christ; for you, O Father, are the
lover of mankind. Amen."""^^xsd:string .

