<R9eUTTuVTES2GrcOItLuuj4> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Act of Faith" ;
    dc:source <https://www.xavier.edu/jesuitresource/online-resources/prayer-index/catholic-prayers> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RyTfHxUQPVMUQrtIt1Mycz> ;
    skos:definition "Act of Faith is a Catholic prayer in which a person explicitly professes belief in God and in the truths God has revealed through divine revelation and the teaching authority of the Church. Act of Faith affirms assent to doctrines such as the Trinity, the Incarnation, and divine judgment because God is truthful and trustworthy."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Before receiving the Eucharist, he prayed an Act of Faith to reaffirm belief in Christ’s real presence."^^xsd:string,
        "Each morning, she prayed an Act of Faith to ground the day in trust in God’s revealed truth."^^xsd:string,
        "O my God, I firmly believe that Thou art one God, in three Divine Persons, the Father, the Son and the Holy Ghost; I believe that Thy Divine Son became man and died for our sins and that He will come to judge the living and the dead. I believe these and all the truths which the holy Catholic Church teaches, because Thou hast revealed them, Who canst neither deceive nor be deceived."^^xsd:string,
        "While preparing for confirmation, the candidate memorized the Act of Faith as part of formation."^^xsd:string .

