<R9gTq4hbqoSHGcTZ2HXPAsL> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Commandment 02: You shall not take the name of the Lord your God in vain." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RDJPdWE32ZF0O3QeYJi5uc> ;
    skos:altLabel "Prohibition Against Blasphemy"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "You Shall Not Take the Name of the Lord Your God in Vain represents the second commandment prohibiting misuse, abuse, or empty invocation of God's holy name. This decree protects divine reverence by forbidding false oaths, blasphemy, casual invocation, and any frivolous or manipulative use of God's name that diminishes its sacred character."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Catholic moral theologians have distinguished between blasphemy (direct violation) and profanity (indirect disrespect) under this commandment."^^xsd:string,
        "Contemporary spiritual writers applied this commandment to advertising and entertainment that trivialize religious language."^^xsd:string,
        "Interfaith scholars noted parallels between this commandment and Islamic prohibitions against dishonoring Allah's names."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:note """Prohibition Statement (Exodus 20:7)
Divine Punishment Warning ("will not hold guiltless")
Deuteronomic Restatement (Deuteronomy 5:11)
Levitical Death Penalty for Blasphemy (Leviticus 24:10-16)
False Oath Prohibition (Leviticus 19:12)
Jesus's Teaching Against Oaths (Matthew 5:33-37)
James's Warning About Swearing (James 5:12)"""^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel "Second Commandment"^^xsd:string .

<R9gVbCYmeRMGmrOAJNjtcRr> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Criminal Lineup" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RBV3MQlbGLIUVo5fSiBZ2V4> ;
    skos:definition "A criminal lineup is a procedure used by law enforcement in which a witness or victim of a crime is presented with a series of individuals, one of whom is the suspect, to determine if the witness can identify the perpetrator. The lineup can be live, with individuals standing in person, or photo-based, using pictures of potential suspects. Proper protocols are essential to ensure fairness and avoid unintentional suggestion or bias." .

