<R9ha5Zbl8m0uLHHAJObkO9H> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Treaty Clause Claim" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RDdZDW8VIPVbM8gI4n7Ippf> ;
    skos:altLabel "Anspruch aus Vertragsklausel"@de-de,
        "Treaty Clause Claim"@en-gb,
        "Reclamación de Cláusula de Tratado"@es-es,
        "Reclamación de Cláusula de Tratado"@es-mx,
        "Réclamation de clause de traité"@fr-fr,
        "תביעת סעיף הסכם"@he-il,
        "संधि धारा दावा"@hi-in,
        "条約条項クレーム"@ja-jp,
        "Reivindicação de cláusula de tratado"@pt-br,
        "条约条款索赔"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A Treaty Clause claim is a legal argument asserting that a particular action or law violates the Treaty Clause of the United States Constitution. This claim contends that the action or law undermines or contradicts the authority granted to the President and the Senate in making and implementing treaties, which requires Senate approval and compliance with the constitutional procedures outlined in the Treaty Clause." .

