    skos:definition "A president is the elected head of state and, in many systems, also the head of government, responsible for executing laws, directing foreign and domestic policy, and representing the nation both domestically and internationally. The specific powers and duties of a president vary by country and are usually defined by a constitution or similar foundational legal document." .

