<R9jqLlNd6kMQydNdIlwyEJS> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Wedding at Cana" ;
    dc:source <https://marian.org/mary/rosary/luminous-mysteries> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RPq5X7NPLuzbWzt3kLIhkw>,
        <RvsGnqbpH0lHwlXuGAmIqD> ;
    skos:altLabel "A homily explained the Wedding at Cana as revealing Jesus’s glory through transformation and abundance."^^xsd:string,
        "A theology class discussed the Wedding at Cana as a sign pointing toward the Eucharist."^^xsd:string,
        "Cana Wedding"^^xsd:string,
        "First Sign of Jesus"^^xsd:string,
        "Marriage Feast at Cana"^^xsd:string,
        "Miracle at Cana"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "The Wedding at Cana is the event in which Jesus transformed water into wine at a wedding feast in Cana of Galilee. It is understood as the first public sign through which Jesus manifested his glory and revealed the inauguration of his saving mission."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "An icon depicted Mary speaking to Jesus before the water was changed into wine at Cana."^^xsd:string,
        """His mother said to the servants, "Do whatever He tells you." … Jesus said to them, "Fill the jars with water." And they filled them up to the brim.
(John 2:5-7)"""^^xsd:string,
        "The Gospel of John presents the Wedding at Cana as the first sign performed by Jesus."^^xsd:string .

