        "Novitiate Candidate"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "A Novice is a person formally admitted to the novitiate of an institute of consecrated life, undertaking an initial period of formation and discernment before first profession. A Novice lives under a novice master’s guidance and follows the institute’s rule and constitutions to test a vocation and grow in the institute’s spiritual and communal life."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "A novice begins the novitiate after admission by the institute’s competent authority."^^xsd:string,
        "A novice discerns readiness for first vows during the canonical novitiate period."^^xsd:string,
        "A novice in a monastic community follows the monastery’s horarium while learning the rule."^^xsd:string,
        "A novice in an apostolic institute receives formation in the institute’s charism and mission."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel "Novice"^^xsd:string .

