<R9od3LRzsXe7sYDBzsaxPno> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Annunciation" ;
    rdfs:comment "In a worldwide Catholic ontology, the Annunciation serves as the precise moment of the Incarnation, where eternity entered time through a human \"yes.\" The Church celebrates this event as the pinnacle of cooperation between divine grace and human freedom."^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RBOrw0GX3E0xD5DuimNLYnD> ],
        <R7oT3qg4wZmB5K3qC79EVID>,
        <R8Q2ik3utpYM1LNPjwbkF4A> ;
    skos:altLabel "Angelic Salutation"^^xsd:string,
        "Mary’s Fiat"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "The Annunciation is the visit of the Archangel Gabriel to the Virgin Mary to announce that she would conceive the Son of God by the power of the Holy Spirit. This event marks the definitive fulfillment of God's promises to Israel and the beginning of the New Covenant in the person of Jesus Christ."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example """And when the angel had come to her, he said, "Hail, full of grace, the Lord is with thee. Blessed art thou among women."
(Luke 1:28)"""^^xsd:string,
        "Painting a lily in a work of sacred art often serves as a symbol of the purity of the Virgin at the moment of the Annunciation."^^xsd:string,
        "Praying the first Joyful Mystery of the Rosary allows the faithful to meditate on the humility of Mary during the Annunciation."^^xsd:string,
        "Setting the date of the Annunciation exactly nine months before Christmas emphasizes the biological and theological reality of Christ's gestation."^^xsd:string .

