<R9sokcA9oHRbgtRmCOsUCY2> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Balance" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <ROYaKdqmAn8EdjV8wNsXdc> ;
    skos:definition "In the context of a balance sheet, \"balance\" refers to the value assigned to an asset, liability, or equity account at a specific point in time. The balance sheet itself is based on the accounting equation \"Assets = Liabilities + Equity,\" and individual balances should sum up to satisfy this equation. This is related to several legal areas (e.g., Tax Law, Bankruptcy Law).",
        "In the context of a claim table, \"balance\" refers to the outstanding amount that remains to be paid or settled on a specific claim. It represents the difference between the total claim amount and any payments or adjustments that have been made against that claim.",
        "In the context of an executory contract, \"balance\" refers to the unfulfilled obligations that each party has yet to perform under the agreement. It signifies the remaining actions, payments, or deliverables that are pending to fully satisfy the terms of the contract.",
        "In the context of bankruptcy, \"balance\" refers to the remaining amount of money or assets that a debtor has after discharging their financial obligations. This term can also relate to the outstanding amount owed by the debtor to the creditors after bankruptcy proceedings." .

