    skos:definition "In civil law jurisdictions, the Right of Property Habitation refers to a real right that allows an individual to reside in a dwelling for life or a specified period, without owning the property outright. This right is personal in nature and typically cannot be transferred, leased, or inherited, distinguishing it from more complete forms of ownership like fee simple or leasehold",
        "Right of Habitation" .

