<R9t8WXRLn7pookX0bFcOwqo> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Petition for Skilled Worker and Specialty Occupation Visa" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty <RN3mWlXZUAt07dYsu6tls2> ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <R76UTCrg8DDzlFkZCPjrdqe> ],
        <RKY2B2HNSx5K82dgVN6Qn7> ;
    skos:altLabel "H1B Petition" ;
    skos:definition "The \"Petition for Specialty Occupation Visa\" generally refers to the H-1B visa petition in the United States. The H-1B visa is a non-immigrant visa category that allows U.S. employers to hire foreign workers in specialty occupations that require specialized knowledge and skills. The employer must file a Form I-129 petition with U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services (USCIS), demonstrating that the position meets the criteria of a specialty occupation and that the beneficiary (the foreign worker) has the necessary qualifications. If approved, the beneficiary can work in the U.S. for the sponsoring employer for a specified period, typically up to three years with the possibility of extension" .

