    skos:altLabel "Fifth Beatitude"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Blessed Are the Merciful means the beatitude in which Jesus Christ declares blessed those who show compassion, forgiveness, and active mercy toward others. Blessed Are the Merciful promises that those who practice mercy will themselves receive mercy from God."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Christian theology interprets mercy as concrete love expressed through forgiveness and compassionate action."^^xsd:string,
