<RB6dePqdjyRdHLTnTyOcFAH> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Anointing of the Sick" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <Rmh26VkWP4ZFcOPX4XE3oA> ;
    skos:altLabel "Anointing of the Infirm"^^xsd:string,
        "Holy Anointing"^^xsd:string,
        "Last Anointing"^^xsd:string,
        "Sacrament of the Anointing of the Sick"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Anointing of the Sick is the sacrament by which the Church commends the faithful who are seriously ill or frail to the suffering and glorified Lord. Through prayer and anointing with blessed oil, the Holy Spirit grants strength, peace, forgiveness of sins, and, if God wills, bodily healing."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "A priest anoints the sick with blessed oil."^^xsd:string,
        "Anointing of the sick strengthens those facing serious illness."^^xsd:string,
        "The Church encourages the faithful to receive this sacrament of Anointing of the Sick before surgery or grave illness."^^xsd:string .

<RB6dekjtZI0W9W2K6JJ2jcO> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Retirement Plan Disclosure" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RmCERXtzdqIJcW9mdbk0Bb> ;
    skos:altLabel "Employee Pension Report" ;
    skos:definition "A Retirement Plan Disclosure, known in the U.S. as a Form 11-K, is an annual report detailing the financial statements and other information regarding an employee benefit plan sponsored by a publicly traded company. The 11-K provides transparency into the assets, liabilities, income, expenses, and operations of the retirement plan. Form 11-K is a specialized financial disclosure document filed with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC), detailing the financial status of a company's employee benefit plans, such as 401(k) plans. It is an American regulatory requirement aimed at providing transparency concerning the financial health of these plans." ;
    skos:prefLabel "11-K" .

