<RB6uy8F0eTdrXT1PxaFeBje> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Jesus' Healing of the Deaf and Mute" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RBpseS3fO7sq2jPuFJjJRzq> ;
    skos:altLabel "Healing of the Deaf and Mute by Jesus"^^xsd:string,
        "Miracle of the Deaf-Mute Healed"^^xsd:string,
        "Restoration of Hearing and Speech by Christ"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Jesus’ Healing of the Deaf and Mute means the miraculous acts by which Jesus Christ restored hearing and speech to those afflicted with deafness or speech impediments. Jesus’ Healing of the Deaf and Mute reveals Christ’s authority over bodily infirmity and his power to open both physical senses and spiritual understanding."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Christian tradition reflects on the healing of the deaf and mute as a sign of Christ opening humanity to God’s word."^^xsd:string,
        "Ephphatha Command"^^xsd:string,
        "Healing of the Deaf-Mute in the Decapolis"^^xsd:string,
        "The Gospel of Mark recounts Jesus healing a deaf man with a speech impediment in the Decapolis."^^xsd:string .

