<RB7s65L4gymOdYbTVr3onXt> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Right to a Jury Trial" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso "The right to a jury trial is a legal principle that guarantees an individual facing criminal charges the opportunity to have their case decided by a group of impartial citizens, typically selected from the community. In the United States, this right is protected by the Sixth Amendment to the Constitution and applies to federal cases, as well as state cases under the Fourteenth Amendment's due process clause." ;
