    skos:definition "Amphibians are a class of vertebrate animals characterized by their ability to live both in water and on land, undergoing metamorphosis from a larval stage with gills to an adult stage with lungs. Amphibians include frogs, salamanders, and caecilians, and are known for their moist skin, which plays a role in respiration." ;
