        "Reivindicação de cláusula ex post facto"@pt-br,
        "事后法律条款索赔"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "An Ex Post Facto Clause claim is a legal argument asserting that a law or action violates the Ex Post Facto Clause of the United States Constitution. This claim contends that the law or action retroactively imposes punishment or changes the legal consequences of an act, which is prohibited by the Ex Post Facto Clause." .

