        "Advice & Consent Clause Claim"@en-gb,
        "Reclamo de la Cláusula de Consejo y Consentimiento"@es-es,
        "Reclamo de la Cláusula de Consejo y Consentimiento"@es-mx,
        "Revendication de la clause de conseil et de consentement"@fr-fr,
        "תביעת סעיף ייעוץ והסכמה"@he-il,
        "सलाह और सहमति धारा दावा"@hi-in,
        "助言と同意条項の主張"@ja-jp,
        "Reivindicação da Cláusula de Conselho e Consentimento"@pt-br,
        "建议和同意条款索赔"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "An Advice & Consent Clause claim is a legal argument asserting that a particular appointment or nomination made by a government official violates the Advice and Consent Clause of the United States Constitution. This claim contends that the appointment or nomination was made without obtaining the necessary advice and consent of a legislative body, typically the Senate, as required by the constitutional provision." .

