    skos:definition "Continuation coverage plans, such as the Consolidated Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act (COBRA) in the U.S., allow former employees to continue their employer-sponsored health insurance for a limited period after employment ends. The individual is generally responsible for the full premium cost plus an administrative fee." ;
    skos:prefLabel "COBRA Coverage Policy" .

<RBPHnblcRUUtZ6l4HOluR9u> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Golden Rule" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RB00C43eWpZ3eGhqNnziJXg> ;
    skos:altLabel "Ethic of Mutual Treatment"^^xsd:string,
        "Rule of Reciprocity"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Golden Rule means the ethical teaching of Jesus Christ that commands treating others as one would wish to be treated. Golden Rule summarizes the moral demands of love of neighbor and expresses the heart of the Law and the Prophets."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Christian moral theology interprets the golden rule as a concise expression of charity and justice in daily life."^^xsd:string,
        "Do unto others as you would have them do unto you."^^xsd:string,
        "The Gospel of Matthew records Jesus teaching, “Do to others what you would have them do to you.”"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel "Do Unto Others"^^xsd:string .

