        "Baptism by Pouring"^^xsd:string,
        "Pouring Baptism"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Baptism by Affusion is a mode of Baptism by Water in which natural water is poured over the person’s head while the Trinitarian formula is pronounced. It validly confers the sacrament and signifies cleansing from sin and rebirth in Christ."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Baptism by affusion is the most common form used in parish celebrations."^^xsd:string,
        "During baptism by affusion, the minister pours water three times while invoking the Trinity."^^xsd:string,
        "Infants are frequently baptized by affusion."^^xsd:string .

