        "Restoration of the Covenant"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "A divine act or ceremony where God reaffirms or restores the covenant relationship with His people, often following periods of unfaithfulness or exile. This renewal reestablishes the binding agreement between God and the faithful, restoring them to their proper covenantal status."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Ezra read the Law to the returned exiles, and the people renewed their covenant with God."^^xsd:string,
        "Josiah renewed the covenant after discovering the Book of the Law in the temple."^^xsd:string,
        "Moses renewed the covenant with Israel on the plains of Moab before they entered the Promised Land."^^xsd:string .

