<RBZn0IX2NtrfPkzFcRdMLwg> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Primary Lateral Sclerosis" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RKBlQ2mgZn3CTwBfUYIM7s> ;
    skos:definition "Primary lateral sclerosis (PLS) is a rare neurodegenerative disorder characterized by the gradual degeneration of upper motor neurons in the brain and spinal cord. This condition leads to progressive muscle stiffness, spasticity, and weakness, primarily affecting voluntary movements while sparing lower motor neurons." .

<RBZyQS180oRBbk6avg3889Y> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Riparian Rights" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RCzQzQSPRAB9cLkvDtBJFn> ;
    skos:definition "Rooted in common law, riparian rights refer to the rights of landowners whose property borders a natural watercourse. Under riparian doctrine, these landowners have the right to make reasonable use of the water adjacent to or flowing over their land, provided they don't unreasonably interfere with the rights of downstream users." .

<RBa1FTthyTBoMYhUi0m4mrN> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Pope Benedict XVI's Prayer for Vocations" ;
    dc:source <https://www.xavier.edu/jesuitresource/online-resources/prayer-index/catholic-prayers> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RyTfHxUQPVMUQrtIt1Mycz> ;
    skos:altLabel "Prayer for Priestly and Religious Vocations"^^xsd:string,
        "Prayer for Vocations by Pope Benedict XVI"^^xsd:string,
        "Vocations Prayer of Benedict XVI"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Pope Benedict XVI’s Prayer for Vocations is a prayer composed to ask God to call and sustain vocations to the priesthood, consecrated life, and holy Christian service. It emphasizes attentive listening to God’s voice, generous response, and faithful perseverance in the Church’s mission."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "At a diocesan gathering, the bishop led Pope Benedict XVI’s Prayer for Vocations to encourage openness to God’s call."^^xsd:string,
        "During adoration, the community prayed Pope Benedict XVI’s Prayer for Vocations for an increase in priestly vocations."^^xsd:string,
        """O Father, raise up among Christians
abundant and holy vocations to the priesthood,
who keep the faith alive
and guard the blessed memory of your Son Jesus
through the preaching of his word
and the administration of the Sacraments,
with which you continually renew your faithful.

Grant us holy ministers of your altar,
who are careful and fervent guardians of the Eucharist,
the sacrament of the supreme gift of Christ
for the redemption of the world.

Call ministers of your mercy,
who, through the sacrament of Reconciliation,
spread the joy of your forgiveness.

Grant, O Father, that the Church may welcome with joy
the numerous inspirations of the Spirit of your Son
and, docile to His teachings,
may she care for vocations to the ministerial priesthood
and to the consecrated life.

Sustain the Bishops, priests and deacons,
consecrated men and women, and all the baptized in Christ,
so that they may faithfully fulfill their mission
at the service of the Gospel.

This we pray through Christ our Lord. Amen.
Mary, Queen of Apostles, pray for us."""^^xsd:string,
        "On the World Day of Prayer for Vocations, the parish recited Pope Benedict XVI’s Prayer for Vocations together."^^xsd:string .

