    skos:definition "The temperate market segment refers to consumers or businesses located in regions characterized by moderate temperatures, typically experiencing distinct seasonal changes. This segmentation allows businesses to cater to the needs of individuals living in areas with a temperate climate, offering products and services suitable for varying weather conditions throughout the year." .

