    rdfs:subClassOf <R83qv1lc6haj7YdVbcf75oC> ;
    skos:altLabel "Consecratory Words Over the Cup"^^xsd:string,
        "Hoc Est Sanguis Meus"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "“This Is My Blood” is the declarative phrase spoken by Jesus over the cup at the Last Supper, identifying the wine with his blood. It functions as a central formula within the institution narrative that establishes the sacramental meaning of the cup and the covenantal dimension of the meal."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "A catechetical session connected “This Is My Blood” to themes of covenant and sacrifice."^^xsd:string,
        "A theology lecture examined “This Is My Blood” as the covenantal declaration of the institution narrative."^^xsd:string,
        "During the Eucharistic Prayer, the celebrant pronounced “This Is My Blood” over the chalice."^^xsd:string .

<RBr6bDd1I5S2sHmzWzkVbes> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "International Organization Visa - Employees and Their Families" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RD1oQDMlC6FytjOndhJTMy8> ;
    skos:altLabel "G-4 Visa"@en-us ;
    skos:definition "An International Organization Visa for employees and their families is a specialized visa category that allows staff members of international organizations, as well as their immediate family members, to reside in a host country for the duration of their assignment. This visa often comes with certain privileges and immunities to facilitate the employees' work and may allow family members to engage in limited employment or educational activities, depending on the host country's regulations." .

<RBrCMBCJ37yUCC4SY0OHund> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Council of Jerusalem" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <ROaU08jUOgsbTbTXXNTIXX> ;
    skos:altLabel "Apostolic Council of Jerusalem"^^xsd:string,
        "First Church Council"^^xsd:string,
        "Jerusalem Council"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Council of Jerusalem means the apostolic assembly described in the Acts of the Apostles in which Church leaders discerned the requirements for Gentile converts to Christianity. Council of Jerusalem establishes the Church’s authority to resolve doctrinal and disciplinary questions through communal discernment guided by the Holy Spirit."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Christian theology regards the council of Jerusalem as the model for conciliar decision-making in the Church."^^xsd:string,
        "The Acts of the Apostles describes the apostles and elders meeting in Jerusalem to decide whether Gentile converts must follow Mosaic Law."^^xsd:string .

