    skos:altLabel "Visitation of Mary"^^xsd:string,
        "Visitation of the Blessed Virgin Mary"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Visitation is a biblical event in which the Blessed Virgin Mary visits her kinswoman Elizabeth, who is pregnant with John the Baptist, and Christ’s presence sanctifies and brings joy. Visitation reveals the work of the Holy Spirit, confirms Mary’s blessedness, and elicits Elizabeth’s inspired proclamation."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Elizabeth was filled with the Holy Spirit and cried out in a loud voice: \"Blest are you among women and blest is the fruit of your womb.\""^^xsd:string,
        "In Advent prayer, she reflected on the Visitation as a model of charity and service."^^xsd:string,
        "The homily highlighted the Visitation as a meeting filled with the Holy Spirit and joy."^^xsd:string,
        "While praying the Rosary, the group meditated on the Visitation as the second Joyful Mystery."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel "The Visitation" .

