        "General Principle"^^xsd:string,
        "Universal Premise"^^xsd:string,
        "Whatever God reveals is true."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Major Premise is the general or universal proposition in an argument that states a principle, rule, or law. It provides the broad foundation from which a conclusion follows when combined with a minor premise."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "All contingent beings require a cause."^^xsd:string .

