<RC0pOXr7Np5vCRZ00mrLema> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Quadriplegia" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R9eX3Auj16MgFGGYWRmhns8> ;
    skos:altLabel "Tetraplegia",
        "Total Body Paralysis" ;
    skos:definition "Quadriplegia, also known as tetraplegia, is a type of mobility disability characterized by the partial or complete paralysis of all four limbs and the torso. This condition typically results from a spinal cord injury or disease affecting the cervical region of the spine, leading to a loss of motor and sensory function below the level of injury." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Quadriplegic Condition" .

<RC0s8HLecR700A0q7jKTfS0> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Blood Prohibition Declaration Events" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RuuXgrWsjANd7N8EBCrGeO> ;
    skos:altLabel "Blood Consumption Prohibition Events"^^xsd:string,
        "Lifeblood Restriction Declaration Occasions"^^xsd:string,
        "Sanguinary Prohibition Establishment Events"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Biblical scholars analyze blood prohibition declaration events across covenants to trace continuity in how Scripture regards life's sanctity."^^xsd:string,
        "Blood Prohibition Declaration Events encompass the specific occasions when God forbade the consumption of blood, establishing blood's sacred status as representing life itself. These events span from the Noahic covenant through Mosaic legislation to the Jerusalem Council's apostolic decree, maintaining blood's special reverence across covenant dispensations."^^xsd:string,
        "Catholic moral theologians study blood prohibition declaration events to understand the theological foundations for reverence toward human life."^^xsd:string,
        "Liturgical theology connects blood prohibition declaration events to Eucharistic doctrine, where Christ's blood becomes spiritual nourishment."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:note """Noahic Blood Prohibition (Genesis 9:4)
Levitical Blood Consumption Ban (Leviticus 17:10-14)
Blood as Atonement Declaration (Leviticus 17:11)
Deuteronomic Blood Pouring Requirements (Deuteronomy 12:23-25)
Jerusalem Council Blood Restriction (Acts 15:20, 29)
Blood Draining Mandates for Sacrifices
Life-Force Theology Statements
Blood and Altar Connection Events"""^^xsd:string .

