<RC6PjawbC2j2bUJ6mt3ZRKc> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Undifferentiated and Mixed Connective Tissue Disease" ;
    dc:source <https://www.ssa.gov/disability/professionals/bluebook/14.00-Immune-Adult.htm#14_00D5>,
        <https://www.ssa.gov/disability/professionals/bluebook/14.00-Immune-Adult.htm#14_06> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RBJ0dgV4Z2Xk7aGfJt2nSj7> ;
    skos:altLabel "Undifferentiated Connective Tissue Disease" ;
    skos:definition "Undifferentiated and mixed connective tissue disease encompasses syndromes with clinical and immunologic features of multiple autoimmune disorders, but which do not meet the criteria for any specific disorder. These conditions may present with clinical manifestations of systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE), systemic vasculitis, and serologic findings characteristic of rheumatoid arthritis, among others." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Autoimmune Overlap Disorder" .

<RC6SNzsct97dNur2jmCJwg0> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Passport Number" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RB8gtCBLdNnUSfnwwQZSVhG> ;
    skos:definition "A passport number is a unique alphanumeric identifier assigned to an individual's passport by the issuing government. This number is used for verification and identification purposes during international travel, border crossings, and various official procedures. It is an essential component of the passport and is often required for legal and administrative purposes." .

