<RCC6qZKk4vInl0VVZfVhnNp> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Bus Lane Violation Claim" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R7hDCTMLoPZrFgIFAMlNHvf>,
        <RBuYThXwp8tJjNWkTeuFvAZ> ;
    skos:altLabel "Bus-Only Lane Infringement Claim",
        "Mass Transit Violation Claim" ;
    skos:definition "A Bus Lane Violation Claim involves allegations that a driver has unlawfully used a bus lane designated solely for buses, potentially impeding public transport efficiency and violating traffic regulations. These claims aim to uphold the integrity of public transit lanes and typically result in fines or other penalties to enforce compliance." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Mass Transit Lane Violation Claim" .

<RCC7p40tc21kf22JJDdEwbC> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Government Contract Labor Standards Claim" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R9UYGSnWQz2MvNsWUofGb6J> ;
    skos:definition "A Government Contract Labor Standards Claim (in the U.S., a Service Contract Act claim) is a legal assertion that an employer has failed to pay prevailing wages and benefits to employees working on federal service contracts. In the U.S., those are required by the McNamara-O'Hara Service Contract Act. Such claims typically seek compensation for underpaid wages and benefits, as well as enforcement of labor standards." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Service Contract Act Claim" .

