    skos:definition "Agnosticism is a philosophical position that asserts the uncertainty or impossibility of knowing the existence or non-existence of deities or other metaphysical entities. In legal contexts, it may refer to a neutral stance regarding religious beliefs or practices in matters such as oaths, testimonies, or religious accommodations." ;
