    skos:altLabel "dismissed",
        "folio:terminated",
        "terminated" ;
    skos:definition "In legal practice, \"dismissed\" refers to the action taken by a court or judicial panel to terminate a case, claim, or appeal. This decision can be based on procedural grounds, lack of jurisdiction, non-compliance with legal requirements, or other reasons that render the case unsuitable for continuation." ;
    skos:example "Appellate panel dismissed the appeal",
        "Judge dismissed claim" .

