<RCGuxQKbNtQSucZOzNQWYQ4> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Catechism Paragraph" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RCve9Byd0sPTUxFRAugXTrX> ;
    skos:definition "Catechism Paragraph is a numbered textual unit within the Catechism of the Catholic Church that authoritatively presents doctrine, moral teaching, or sacramental theology. It serves as a stable reference for instruction, citation, and normative catechesis."^^xsd:string .

<RCGzY6GxWecmgsg39XP6QMG> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Voluntary Commitment to a Mental Health Facility" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RDmZbwmBBKWQ3vGof1sh1kB> ;
    skos:definition "Voluntary commitment to a mental health facility occurs when an individual willingly and knowingly agrees to be admitted to a psychiatric hospital or clinic for treatment. This decision is made without external coercion, and the individual retains the right to request discharge, though there might be conditions or procedures to follow before release." .

<RCH9bm46SJokYFChlK01xIX> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Business License" ;
    rdfs:comment "From LIST: Legal Issues Taxonomy — https://taxonomy.legal/" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RCKrakJNv6b1oTTMhd4c5DU> ;
    skos:definition "A business license is a permit or certification issued by a governmental authority that allows an individual or company to operate a business within a specific jurisdiction. The license serves as proof of compliance with local, state, or federal regulations and is often required for tax purposes." .

<RCHEH9WuYl4sNbdfqEDZgmN> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Right to Confront Witnesses" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <R9tZFXPrXQJWHbqSgtCQxJF> ],
        <RBQRg4Bv481hOyPBNKLCj8m> ;
    skos:altLabel "Recht auf Konfrontation von Zeugen"@de-de,
        "Right to Confront Witnesses"@en-gb,
        "Derecho a Confrontar Testigos"@es-es,
        "Derecho a Confrontar Testigos"@es-mx,
        "Droit de confronter les témoins"@fr-fr,
        "זכות למעמד עדים"@he-il,
        "गवाहों के सामने अधिकार"@hi-in,
        "証人尋問権"@ja-jp,
        "Direito de confrontar testemunhas"@pt-br,
        "与证人对抗的权利"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "The right to confront witnesses is a fundamental aspect of a fair trial, ensuring that a defendant in a criminal case has the opportunity to question or cross-examine the witnesses testifying against them. Protected by the Sixth Amendment of the United States Constitution, this right enables the defense to challenge the credibility, accuracy, and reliability of the witnesses' testimony, and helps ensure that the trial process is transparent and adversarial." .

