<RCN12H3Ong9RPr1qtQ2VDl3> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Act of Love" ;
    dc:source <https://www.xavier.edu/jesuitresource/online-resources/prayer-index/catholic-prayers> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RyTfHxUQPVMUQrtIt1Mycz> ;
    skos:definition "Act of Love is a Catholic prayer in which a person professes love for God above all things and commits to love of neighbor for God’s sake. It unites devotion to God with forgiveness and charity as concrete expressions of divine love."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "After receiving Communion, she prayed an Act of Love in thanksgiving and devotion."^^xsd:string,
        "O my God, I love Thee above all things with my whole heart and soul, because Thou art all good and worthy of all love. I love my neighbor as myself for love of Thee. I forgive all who have injured me, and I ask pardon for all whom I have injured."^^xsd:string,
        "The catechist taught the Act of Love alongside the Acts of Faith, Hope, and Charity."^^xsd:string,
        "While examining his conscience, he recited an Act of Love to renew forgiveness and charity."^^xsd:string .

