<RCPDM2C4dWtlL1XVLpJoe7m> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Sacrifice Regulation Events" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R7hUqSzjreR3vfFZVZniVs4>,
        <ROgocFufRBHZKkFfPDYyYh> ;
    skos:altLabel "Ritual Sacrifice Regulation"^^xsd:string,
        "Sacrificial Code Institution"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Sacrifice Regulation Events encompass the occasions when God established and refined the rules governing offerings, sacrifices, and ritual worship practices. These events span from the earliest altars through detailed Levitical prescriptions to prophetic critiques and Christ's ultimate self-offering, defining how humanity approaches God through prayer and worship."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Biblical commentaries analyze sacrifice regulation events to discern ancient Israel's understanding of atonement, thanksgiving, and covenant renewal."^^xsd:string,
        "Catholic sacramental theology studies sacrifice regulation events to understand how Christ fulfills and perfects Old Testament sacrificial systems."^^xsd:string,
        "Liturgical scholars trace sacrifice regulation events to explain the Mass's sacrificial character and Eucharistic theology."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:note """Cain and Abel's Offerings (Genesis 4:3-5)
Noah's Post-Flood Altar (Genesis 8:20-21)
Patriarchal Altar Building Events
Passover Lamb Institution (Exodus 12)
Burnt Offering Regulations (Leviticus 1)
Grain Offering Prescriptions (Leviticus 2)
Peace Offering Instructions (Leviticus 3)
Sin Offering Requirements (Leviticus 4)
Guilt Offering Laws (Leviticus 5-6)
Day of Atonement Sacrifices (Leviticus 16)
Daily Tamid Offerings (Numbers 28:1-8)
Prophetic Critique of Empty Sacrifice (Isaiah 1:11-17)
Christ's Last Supper Institution (Luke 22:19-20)
Christ's Calvary Sacrifice (Hebrews 9:11-14)"""^^xsd:string .

