    skos:definition "A Vicar Forane is a priest appointed by the diocesan bishop to coordinate and support pastoral ministry within a defined group of neighboring parishes, known as a vicariate or deanery. He exercises limited supervisory and consultative functions on the bishop’s behalf without governing authority over pastors."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "A vicar forane supports collaboration among neighboring parishes."^^xsd:string,
        "Canon law assigns defined responsibilities to the vicar forane."^^xsd:string,
        "The bishop appoints a vicar forane to oversee a deanery."^^xsd:string,
        "The vicar forane assists pastors while respecting their authority."^^xsd:string .

