    skos:definition "Friary is a religious house in which members of a mendicant religious order live in common according to their rule and charism. A friary is ordered toward communal life, prayer, and active apostolic ministry, often marked by itinerant service and engagement with the wider community."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "A Dominican friary functions as a center for preaching, study, and teaching."^^xsd:string,
        "A Franciscan friary supports communal life marked by poverty and service to the poor."^^xsd:string,
