        <RKKRGOkIme6pnG2BSePt1Z> ;
    skos:definition "An Intellectual Property License Agreement grants a party the right to use a specific intellectual property owned by another party under specified conditions. It doesn't transfer ownership but allows for certain usages, often in exchange for compensation." .

