        "Teaching to Be Held Definitively"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Definitively Proposed Doctrine is a teaching of the Catholic Church set forth as to be held firmly and irrevocably, even if not solemnly defined as divinely revealed. The faithful owe it definitive assent because it is necessarily connected to divine revelation or required to safeguard and faithfully expound the deposit of faith."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "A doctrine may be definitively proposed even if not formally defined as revealed."^^xsd:string,
        "Definitively proposed doctrine requires firm and definitive assent."^^xsd:string,
        "The Magisterium proposes some doctrines definitively to protect the integrity of the faith."^^xsd:string .

