        "Moral Instruction"^^xsd:string,
        "Moral Teaching"^^xsd:string,
        "Teach the Uninformed"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Instruct the Ignorant is a spiritual work of mercy that consists in teaching those who lack necessary knowledge, especially in matters of faith, morals, or practical wisdom. Instruct the Ignorant serves truth and charity by correcting misunderstanding and enabling informed, free moral judgment."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "A catechist explains the basic teachings of the faith to new inquirers."^^xsd:string,
        "A mentor explains ethical obligations to someone unfamiliar with them."^^xsd:string,
        "A parent teaches a child right and wrong through patient instruction."^^xsd:string,
        "A parish volunteer helps adults understand the sacraments and their meaning."^^xsd:string,
        "A teacher clarifies moral principles to correct a serious misunderstanding."^^xsd:string .

