<RD3AsL6dIQwlCnaA8Rezj3B> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Excessive Bail Claim" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RKj3panTdxsJ7nFn11CPGT> ;
    skos:altLabel "Anspruch auf unangemessen hohe Kaution"@de-de,
        "Excessive Bail Claim"@en-gb,
        "Reclamo de fianza excesiva"@es-es,
        "Reclamo de fianza excesiva"@es-mx,
        "Réclamation de caution excessive"@fr-fr,
        "תביעת ערבות מופקרת"@he-il,
        "अत्यधिक जमानत दावा"@hi-in,
        "過剰保釈請求"@ja-jp,
        "Reivindicação de fiança excessiva"@pt-br,
        "过度保释要求"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "An excessive bail claim is a legal action initiated by an individual alleging that their Eighth Amendment right to be free from excessive bail has been violated by the government or a government actor. The Eighth Amendment prohibits the government from imposing excessive bail, which is a monetary sum set by a court to ensure that an individual shows up for trial or other legal proceedings. An excessive bail claim may arise in various contexts, such as when a court sets an unreasonably high bail amount that is beyond the individual's ability to pay, or when a court sets bail at a level that is disproportionate to the offense committed." .

