        "Ethics of the Environment"^^xsd:string,
        "Sustainability Ethics"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Environmental Ethics is the field of applied ethics that examines moral duties toward the natural environment and the proper relationship between humanity and creation. Environmental Ethics orders human stewardship of the earth toward respect for creation, human dignity, and the common good."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Environmental ethics addresses environmental harm that disproportionately affects the poor."^^xsd:string,
        "Environmental ethics evaluates policies that affect the integrity of ecosystems."^^xsd:string,
        "Environmental ethics guides responsible use of natural resources for future generations."^^xsd:string .

