    rdfs:subClassOf <RDETD6YVYGhLGZbM1fBnsfj> ;
    skos:altLabel "Emotionale Unfähigkeit"@de-de,
        "Emotional Incapacity"@en-gb,
        "Incapacidad emocional"@es-es,
        "Incapacidad emocional"@es-mx,
        "Incapacité émotionnelle"@fr-fr,
        "אי יכולת רגשית"@he-il,
        "भावनात्मक अशक्तता"@hi-in,
        "感情的な無力"@ja-jp,
        "Incapacidade emocional"@pt-br,
        "情感无能力"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "Emotional incapacity refers to an individual's inability to manage or cope with their emotions effectively, often resulting in difficulty forming or maintaining relationships, making decisions, or participating in daily activities. Emotional incapacity may be considered in certain legal contexts, such as family law or mental health-related cases, to assess a person's competence or decision-making abilities." .

