<RDJNj1oxGk7LGj6OusI7Uv> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Hail, Holy Queen"^^xsd:string ;
    dc:source <https://www.xavier.edu/jesuitresource/online-resources/prayer-index/catholic-prayers> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RCA6zlBfTqVXfLM0xipUkZf>,
        <RyTfHxUQPVMUQrtIt1Mycz> ;
    skos:altLabel "Antiphon of Our Lady"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Hail, Holy Queen is a Marian antiphon that invokes the Blessed Virgin Mary as Mother of Mercy and asks for her intercession during earthly exile. It expresses hope in Mary’s advocacy and longing for the vision of Christ at life’s end."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "At the conclusion of the Rosary, the group prayed Hail, Holy Queen together."^^xsd:string,
        "During Night Prayer, the choir sang the Salve Regina in Gregorian chant."^^xsd:string,
        """Hail, holy Queen, mother of Mercy.
Hail, our life, our sweetness and our hope.
To thee do we cry,
poor banished children of Eve;
to thee do we send up our sighs,
mourning and weeping,
in this vale of tears.
Turn then, most gracious advocate,
thine eyes of mercy toward us;
and after this our exile, show unto us
the blessed fruit of thy womb, Jesus.
O clement, O loving,
O sweet virgin Mary."""^^xsd:string,
        "On pilgrimage, the faithful ended the day by praying Hail, Holy Queen."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel "Salve Regina"^^xsd:string .

<RDJPhq9RjJu1rvptoQKqbbI> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Airplane" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R9HTLbEXSzD7fXO9Hu6mTmb> ;
    skos:altLabel "Fixed-Wing Air Vehicle",
        "Fixed-Wing Aircraft",
        "Jet",
        "Plane",
        "Aeroplane"@en-gb ;
    skos:definition "An Airplane is a powered fixed-wing aircraft that achieves flight through the use of forward thrust and aerodynamic lift. It typically has a fuselage, wings, and one or more engines, and is designed for transporting passengers, cargo, or both." .

<RDJUDQGYk9rhdIFXzTyv11u> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Substantive Due Process Claim" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RfP04tDTTpn4LDvwAxAqkh> ;
    skos:altLabel "Anspruch auf materielle Rechtsstaatlichkeit"@de-de,
        "Substantive Due Process Claim"@en-gb,
        "Reclamo de debido proceso sustantivo"@es-es,
        "Reclamo de debido proceso sustantivo"@es-mx,
        "Revendication de procédure régulière"@fr-fr,
        "תביעת תהליך דיון משמעותי"@he-il,
        "वास्तविक दंड प्रक्रिया दावा"@hi-in,
        "実質的な正当な手続きの主張"@ja-jp,
        "Reivindicação de devido processo legal material"@pt-br,
        "实体正当程序主张"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A substantive due process claim is a legal action initiated by an individual or entity alleging that their fundamental rights, as protected by the Due Process Clauses of the Fifth and Fourteenth Amendments of the United States Constitution, have been violated by the government or a government actor. Substantive due process protects individuals from arbitrary or unreasonable government actions that infringe on fundamental rights, even if proper procedures were followed. A substantive due process claim may arise in various contexts, such as when a government body enacts a law or regulation that unduly restricts a fundamental right (e.g., the right to privacy, the right to marry, or the right to make decisions about family matters) or when a government actor takes an arbitrary or irrational action that infringes on an individual's rights." .

<RDJWZSnQkLCRb0PTCafsUD9> a owl:Class ;
