    skos:definition "Foreign National Identifier refers to a unique identification number or code assigned to non-citizens by a country's immigration or governmental agency. In the United States, this is commonly known as the Alien Number or A-Number, which is used to track immigration cases and statuses. These identifiers appear on official documents such as green cards, visas, and employment authorization documents." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Alien Number" .

