    skos:definition "Chaldean Rites are the liturgical, theological, and spiritual expressions of the Catholic Church rooted in the East Syriac Christian tradition of Mesopotamia. They are marked by an ancient euchological heritage, the use of Syriac language, and a theology shaped by the Church of the East."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Chaldean rites preserve the East Syriac liturgical tradition."^^xsd:string,
        "The Chaldean Catholic Church celebrates the sacraments according to this rite."^^xsd:string,
