        "Misleading",
        "Objection to Indefinite Question",
        "Unintelligible",
        "Vague" ;
    skos:definition "A Vague and Ambiguous Objection is raised when a party in a legal proceeding believes that a question posed by the opposing counsel is unclear, lacks specificity, or could be interpreted in multiple ways. This objection aims to ensure that questions are precise and understandable, facilitating accurate and relevant responses." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Objection to Unclear Question" .

