    skos:altLabel "Droit de Prendre" ;
    skos:definition "In civil law systems, the Right to Profit (\"droit de prendre\") refers to a real right that allows an individual or entity to enter another's land to extract resources like minerals, timber, or fish. This right is usually granted through a contract or license and is subject to the terms and conditions specified therein, as well as overarching legal regulations." .

