<RDknkUgvOz8oQItOWa7Y9Av> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Retention Agreement" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <Rhpdjd9p358e9Rkel80dvQ> ;
    skos:definition "A Retention Related Agreement is a legally binding contract between an employer and an employee, often a key or high-value employee, with the aim of retaining the employee within the company for a specified period. This type of agreement typically includes provisions for financial incentives, such as bonuses or stock options, and may also outline conditions or obligations the employee must meet to receive these incentives. The primary goal is to encourage employee loyalty and discourage them from leaving the organization during a critical period." .

<RDkxy1u3kzfwPuVV7mW0nv7> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Private Attorneys General Act Claim" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R9UYGSnWQz2MvNsWUofGb6J> ;
    skos:altLabel "PAGA Claim",
        "Klage nach dem Gesetz über private Staatsanwälte"@de-de,
        "Private Attorneys General Act Claim"@en-gb,
        "Reclamación de la Ley de Abogados Generales Privados"@es-es,
        "Reclamación de la Ley de Abogados Generales Privados"@es-mx,
        "Action en vertu de la loi sur les procureurs généraux privés"@fr-fr,
        "תביעה על פי חוק עורכי דין כלליים פרטיים"@he-il,
        "निजी वकील महानियांकन अधिनियम दावा"@hi-in,
        "プライベート・アトーニーゼネラル法クレーム"@ja-jp,
        "Reivindicação da Lei de Procuradores Gerais Privados"@pt-br,
        "私人检察官法案索赔"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "The Private Attorneys General Act (PAGA) is a California law that allows employees to bring claims on behalf of the state against their employers for labor code violations. By acting as private attorneys general, employees can seek penalties for themselves and their co-workers, thereby helping to enforce labor laws when government agencies may lack the resources to do so." .

