        "Tempestade em progresso"@pt-br,
        "正在进行的风暴"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A \"Storm in Progress\" is a legal concept within the context of civil defenses and litigation, referring to a situation where a legal matter is currently ongoing and actively being pursued." .

<RDldaaRtY0mfXfmbn43Kfm6> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Patience" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <R8ifazW1D1PDee0OGJlWVpG> ],
        <RBAHGQZblh8cggdiTJggZfv> ;
    skos:altLabel "Calm Perseverance"^^xsd:string,
        "Forbearance"^^xsd:string,
        "Long-Suffering"^^xsd:string,
        "Steadfast Endurance"^^xsd:string,
        "Tolerance of Delay"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Patience is the moral virtue that disposes a person to endure difficulty, delay, or suffering without undue anger, discouragement, or resentment. Patience sustains charity and perseverance by moderating sorrow and frustration in the face of trial."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Patience enables a person to endure illness without losing hope or charity."^^xsd:string,
        "Patience restrains anger when confronted with repeated frustration."^^xsd:string,
        "Patience supports steady effort during long and demanding responsibilities."^^xsd:string .

<RDlhbcek4X5EXc5Oz0vWnOi> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Pleura or Mediastinum Cancer" ;
    dc:source <https://www.ssa.gov/disability/professionals/bluebook/13.00-NeoplasticDiseases-Malignant-Adult.htm#13_15> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RDF3VrmH1eapfkrSQstevLs> ;
    skos:altLabel "Thoracic Cavity Cancer" ;
    skos:definition "Pleura or mediastinum cancer refers to malignant tumors originating in the pleura, the thin tissue covering the lungs and lining the chest cavity, or in the mediastinum, the central compartment of the thoracic cavity. These cancers can significantly affect respiratory function and often require complex diagnostic and therapeutic approaches due to their proximity to vital structures." ;
    skos:example "Mediastinal Cancer",
        "Pleural Cancer" .

