<RDn0b6dDytXqi3nEm99XM4O> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Bipolar Disorder" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R8ly82UzT3qEXtZR0pcZq8L> ;
    skos:altLabel "Bipolar Condition",
        "Bipolar Mental Disorder",
        "Bipolar Mood Disorder",
        "Manic-Depressive Illness" ;
    skos:definition "Bipolar Disorder is a psychiatric condition characterized by extreme mood swings that include emotional highs (mania or hypomania) and lows (depression). These mood swings can affect energy levels, activity, behavior, and the ability to carry out daily tasks, often requiring long-term treatment to manage symptoms." .

<RDnD2fvOdZErNFUzPEokIYM> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "International Organization Visa - Attendants, Servants, and Personal Employees" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RCT9Ji3xwVRmaAm7oP74vvB> ],
        <R7vlavFi9wyzEzNgp9zjkE> ;
    skos:altLabel "G-5 Visa"@en-us ;
    skos:definition "An International Organization Visa for attendants, servants, and personal employees is a specialized visa category that allows individuals to accompany representatives or officials of international organizations while they are stationed in a host country for official duties. This visa is generally subject to specific conditions and may require the sponsoring international organization or official to assume certain responsibilities for the employee's welfare and legal status in the host country." .

<RDnEuJ1VsP5Slnusvfyyt5f> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Peaches" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R8WhsyEOse5TvMLfnHDYfTY> ;
    skos:altLabel "Prunus Persica" ;
    skos:definition "Peaches are juicy, sweet stone fruits from the Prunus persica species, characterized by their fuzzy skin and aromatic flesh. They are consumed fresh, canned, or used in culinary applications such as desserts, jams, and beverages, valued for their vitamins, antioxidants, and dietary fiber." .

<RDnIuhbbvS0zCuqfgntnzRW> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Rice" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R9WRFGVqE913fnyJVUGR8Xg> ;
    skos:altLabel "Oryza" ;
    skos:definition "Rice is a cereal crop belonging to the species Oryza sativa (Asian rice) or Oryza glaberrima (African rice), known for its edible starchy grains that are a staple food for more than half of the world's population. Cultivated primarily in flooded fields called paddies, rice provides essential carbohydrates, proteins, and vitamins, and is used in a variety of culinary dishes." .

