    rdfs:subClassOf <R7g26D3ngRM7ylTT72MlAUW> ;
    skos:altLabel "Umgekehrtes Recht"@de-de,
        "Droit inversé"@fr-fr,
        "逆法"@ja-jp,
        "Lei Reversa"@pt-br,
        "反向法"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "The previously effective law has been reversed by some authority (e.g., appellate court, judge, regulator)." .

<RDoRNl7czYxqWXYmY66AXlB> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "The Magnificat" ;
    dc:source <https://www.xavier.edu/jesuitresource/online-resources/prayer-index/catholic-prayers> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RyTfHxUQPVMUQrtIt1Mycz> ;
    skos:altLabel "Magnificat Anima Mea Dominum"^^xsd:string,
        "Song of Mary"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "The Magnificat is Mary’s canticle of praise proclaimed during the Visitation, in which she glorifies God for his mighty deeds and saving mercy. The Magnificat expresses joy in God’s fidelity, exalts divine justice, and proclaims the reversal of human pride through God’s action."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Each evening, the Church proclaims the Magnificat during Vespers in the Liturgy of the Hours."^^xsd:string,
        "In personal prayer, he recited the Magnificat to give thanks for God’s mercy."^^xsd:string,
        """My soul proclaims the greatness of the Lord, 
my spirit rejoices in God my Savior
for he has looked with favor on his lowly servant.
From this day all generations will call me blessed:
the Almighty has done great things for me,
and holy is his Name.

He has mercy on those who fear him
in every generation.
He has shown the strength of his arm,
he has scattered the proud in their conceit.

He has cast down the mighty from their thrones,
and has lifted up the lowly.
He has filled the hungry with good things,
and the rich he has sent away empty.

He has come to the help of his servant Israel
for he remembered his promise of mercy,
the promise he made to our fathers,
to Abraham and his children forever."""^^xsd:string,
        "The choir sang a choral setting of the Magnificat during the feast of the Assumption."^^xsd:string,
        "While meditating on the Visitation, she reflected on the Magnificat as Mary’s response of praise."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel "Canticle of Mary"^^xsd:string .

