<RDoc5fkIs4N79QVKf9t11jt> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Defensive Asylum" ;
    dc:source <https://help.unhcr.org/usa/applying-for-asylum/types-of-asylum/> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RCjaPxLpNSWz91c3fJzxweU> ;
    skos:definition "Defensive asylum is a form of asylum claimed by individuals who are in removal proceedings before an immigration court. Unlike affirmative asylum, defensive asylum is raised as a defense against being removed from the destination country (e.g., United States) and requires the applicant to present their case before an immigration judge." .

