<RDtGL89WprtWamR7WEh5tqg> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Petition for Treaty Investor Visa" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty <RN3mWlXZUAt07dYsu6tls2> ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <Rt0JqQ9ENDi6hglqbWBbJe> ],
        <RKY2B2HNSx5K82dgVN6Qn7> ;
    skos:altLabel "E-2 Petition" ;
    skos:definition "An E-2 petition refers to the application process for obtaining an E-2 Treaty Investor Visa in the United States. The E-2 visa is available to individuals from countries that have a qualifying treaty with the U.S. It allows foreign nationals who are making a substantial investment in a U.S. enterprise to enter the U.S. for the purpose of developing and managing that investment. The E-2 visa can be applied for by investors, employees of the investor's enterprise, or the enterprise itself. The petition involves demonstrating the substantiality of the investment and meeting other eligibility criteria as outlined by U.S. immigration laws and regulations" .

<RDtGwjcx99cEgGWhK2DvpNq> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "General Ticket (Party Block) Electoral System" ;
    dc:source <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_ticket> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RV8mJWGZnQhe2gDARKvAiF> ;
    skos:altLabel "PBV",
        "Ticket Voting" ;
    skos:definition "The general ticket, also known as the party block electoral system, is a voting method in which voters select a party rather than individual candidates, and the party receiving the majority of votes wins all the seats available. This system is designed to ensure cohesive party representation but can result in the overrepresentation of the majority party." ;
    skos:example "Full Slate Voting: Some municipal elections in the United States",
        "Party Block Voting: U.S. Electoral College system before the 12th Amendment" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Party Block System" .

