<RDuZiTT7eWVTyXTEOgEqM0J> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Guardianship Authority" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R4BbNqGb3HJAUtTar6b1i> ;
    skos:altLabel "Conservatorship Authority"^^xsd:string,
        "Custodial Authority"^^xsd:string,
        "Protective Stewardship"^^xsd:string,
        "Tutelary Authority"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Guardianship Authority is the moral and practical authority entrusted to a guardian to provide care, protection, and prudent direction for a person who cannot fully provide for himself or herself. Guardianship Authority binds the guardian to act for the ward’s true good, respecting the ward’s dignity and, when possible, supporting the ward’s growth toward greater responsibility."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "A court appoints an aunt as a minor child’s guardian after the child’s parents die."^^xsd:string,
        "A guardian consents to medical treatment for an adult ward who cannot make informed decisions."^^xsd:string,
        "A guardian consults the ward’s pastor to support the ward’s spiritual welfare without coercing conscience."^^xsd:string,
        "A temporary guardian makes urgent decisions for a ward during a medical emergency."^^xsd:string .

