<RF7AfcfFA3fae48E20eEAfbc> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "U.S. Consumer Product Safety Commission" ;
    dc:identifier "US-FD-CPSC" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R22815eC3Af3bFF0d002Ca58> ;
    skos:altLabel "US-amerikanische Kommission für Produktsicherheit"@de-de,
        "U.S. Consumer Product Safety Commission"@en-gb,
        "Comisión de Seguridad de Productos de Consumo de EE. UU."@es-es,
        "Comisión de Seguridad de Productos de Consumo de EE. UU."@es-mx,
        "Commission américaine de sécurité des produits de consommation"@fr-fr,
        "הוועד לבטיחות מוצרי הצרכן של ארצות הברית"@he-il,
        "यूएस उपभोक्ता उत्पाद सुरक्षा आयोग"@hi-in,
        "米国消費者製品安全委員会"@ja-jp,
        "Comissão de Segurança de Produtos de Consumo dos EUA"@pt-br,
        "美国消费品安全委员会"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "The United States Consumer Product Safety Commission (CPSC or Commission) is an independent agency of the United States government that seeks to promote the safety of consumer products by addressing \"unreasonable risks\" of injury (through coordinating recalls, evaluating products that are the subject of consumer complaints or industry reports, etc.); developing uniform safety standards (some mandatory, some through a voluntary standards process); and conducting research into product-related illness and injury." ;
