<RFCom7HmbLadGcpGO751NZ> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Guarantee Clause Claim" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RC5bITZZ0taJOXwcwS314VU> ;
    skos:altLabel "Garantieanspruch"@de-de,
        "Guarantee Clause Claim"@en-gb,
        "Reclamación de Cláusula de Garantía"@es-es,
        "Reclamación de Cláusula de Garantía"@es-mx,
        "Réclamation de clause de garantie"@fr-fr,
        "תביעת סעיף הגנה"@he-il,
        "गारंटी शर्त दावा"@hi-in,
        "保証条項請求"@ja-jp,
        "Reivindicação de cláusula de garantia"@pt-br,
        "保证条款索赔"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A Guarantee Clause claim refers to a legal argument based on the Guarantee Clause of the United States Constitution, asserting that the federal government has a duty to guarantee a republican form of government to each state. It aims to ensure that states are protected against domestic insurrection or the imposition of undemocratic forms of government." .

