<RHQZIkjqaamL59jEx6Mhif> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Commandment 01: I am the Lord your God: You shall not have strange Gods before me." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RDJPdWE32ZF0O3QeYJi5uc> ;
    skos:altLabel "I am the Lord your God: You shall not have strange Gods before me."^^xsd:string,
        "Monotheism Commandment"^^xsd:string,
        "No Other Gods"^^xsd:string,
        "No Other Gods Commandment"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "I Am the Lord Your God: You Shall Not Have Strange Gods Before Me represents the first commandment establishing exclusive monotheistic worship and covenant loyalty to Yahweh alone. This foundational decree identifies God as Israel's liberator and demands absolute allegiance, prohibiting worship of any competing deities or divided religious loyalties."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Jewish interpreters throughout history emphasized the first commandment's connection to Exodus liberation, linking theology to social justice."^^xsd:string,
        "Medieval scholastics analyzed the first commandment to define theological virtues of faith, hope, and charity as proper responses."^^xsd:string,
        "Modern Catholic moral theology has employed the first commandment when addressing consumerism, nationalism, and ideological absolutisms as false gods."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:note """Divine Self-Identification Formula (Exodus 20:2)
Liberation Reminder ("who brought you out of Egypt")
Prohibition of Other Gods (Exodus 20:3)
Deuteronomic Restatement (Deuteronomy 5:6-7)
Shema Declaration Connection (Deuteronomy 6:4-5)
Greatest Commandment Linkage (Matthew 22:37-38)
Jealous God Declaration (Exodus 20:5)"""^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel "First Commandment"^^xsd:string .

