    rdfs:subPropertyOf <R8oVqWGVPjAgl133D0pNL7g> ;
    skos:altLabel "direct-examined" ;
    skos:definition "In the legal realm, \"direct examined\" refers to the initial questioning of a witness by the party that called them to testify in a trial or hearing. This process is fundamental for establishing the facts of a case as presented by the witness, and it focuses on eliciting favorable, relevant testimony in a narrative form, typically without leading questions." .

