    skos:altLabel "One-Sided Paralysis" ;
    skos:definition "Hemiplegia is a condition characterized by paralysis or severe weakness on one side of the body, typically resulting from brain injuries such as stroke, traumatic brain injury, or neurological diseases. This condition affects motor function, coordination, and sensation on the affected side, significantly impacting daily activities." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Hemiparetic Condition" .

