<RKqMtq4VODwvUGdxe07Jf6> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Legal Opinion Document" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R99VQVUo93kYqqhla6ZUJTC> ;
    skos:altLabel "Legal Advisory Document",
        "Legal Opinion Letter" ;
    skos:definition "A legal opinion document is a written statement by a legal expert, usually an attorney or a law firm, expressing their professional judgment on the legal aspects of a transaction, agreement, or legal issue. It provides an analysis of the legality, enforceability, or compliance of the matter in question with applicable laws and regulations." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Attorney Opinion Letter" .

<RKrNAlBgKO4pd18K7dGZrU> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Information Ethics" ;
    rdfs:comment "Information Ethics focuses on the truthfulness, accessibility, and dignity of human communication. While Technology Ethics often deals with the tools (the \"hardware\" of action), Information Ethics addresses the content and the right to truth (the \"software\" of communication), rooted in the Vatican II decree Inter Mirifica and the Pontifical Council for Social Communications' document Ethics in Internet."^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R740KsX4ol3KSiJ2DHXcsGL> ;
    skos:altLabel "Informational Justice"^^xsd:string,
        "Media Ethics"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Information Ethics is the branch of applied ethics that evaluates the gathering, storage, and dissemination of data and ideas according to the requirements of justice and charity. It asserts that every person has an inherent right to the truth and that information systems must serve the integral development of the human community rather than the manipulation of the person."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Bridging the Digital Divide and Access to information."^^xsd:string,
        "Ensuring that marginalized communities have equitable access to the digital information necessary for their social participation."^^xsd:string,
        "Ethics of Intellectual Property, including copyrights, trademarks, patents, and trade secrets."^^xsd:string,
        "Respecting the confidentiality of personal data as a reflection of the inherent dignity and privacy of the human person."^^xsd:string,
        "Verifying the accuracy of news reports to prevent the spread of misinformation that could harm the common good."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel "Communications Ethics"^^xsd:string .

<RKsQ8wAiKiOfAtbV7KR6i1> a owl:Class ;
