        "Moral Law Inscribed in Human Nature"^^xsd:string,
        "Lex Naturalis"@la ;
    skos:definition "Natural Law (Lex Naturalis) is the rational creature’s participation in the Eternal Law, whereby human reason discerns moral good and evil. It expresses objective moral principles rooted in human nature and binding on all persons."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "A civil statute contradicts natural law when it authorizes intrinsic evil."^^xsd:string,
        "Catholic teaching appeals to natural law in discussions of human dignity."^^xsd:string,
        "Human reason apprehends natural law through reflection on human nature."^^xsd:string,
        "Natural law grounds universal moral obligations independent of civil law."^^xsd:string .

