    skos:definition "The U.S. Senate is the upper chamber of Congress, responsible for confirming presidential appointments, ratifying treaties, and conducting impeachment trials. Composed of 100 members, with two Senators representing each state, the Senate exercises legislative, executive, and judicial powers as part of the federal government." .

<RQiF2hjodeRJqOHMEKEcHG> a owl:Class ;
