<RQm8rEifuw541HHtvmdfTE> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Glory Be" ;
    dc:source <https://www.xavier.edu/jesuitresource/online-resources/prayer-index/catholic-prayers> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RyTfHxUQPVMUQrtIt1Mycz> ;
    skos:altLabel "Gloria Patri"^^xsd:string,
        "Short Doxology"^^xsd:string,
        "Trinitarian Doxology"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "After Scripture reading, he offered the Glory Be in praise of the Trinity."^^xsd:string,
        "At the end of each decade of the Rosary, the faithful prayed the Glory Be."^^xsd:string,
        "During the Liturgy of the Hours, the psalm concluded with the Glory Be."^^xsd:string,
        "Glory Be is a short Trinitarian doxology that gives praise to the Father, the Son, and the Holy Spirit, affirming God’s eternal glory. It proclaims the unchanging nature of God’s life and majesty from the beginning through all ages."^^xsd:string,
        """Glory be to the Father,
and to the Son,
and to the Holy Spirit.
As it was in the beginning, is now,
and ever shall be,
world without end."""^^xsd:string,
        "In family prayer, the children learned the Glory Be as a foundational prayer."^^xsd:string .

