<RTyOWLTtwSMwIw3JDKhZi8> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Governor" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RBZXbv75cyMrROEWybfqeTJ> ;
    skos:definition "A Governor is the chief executive officer of a state, commonwealth, or territory within a federal system of government. This official is typically elected by the populace and is responsible for implementing state laws, managing the state government, and serving as the state's top representative in dealings with other states and the federal government." .

<RTyoF6vOGn0G3py0iRkxN5> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Number of Employees" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R8nREeU6lB0zs0dt9N339nm> ;
    skos:definition "Number of Employees refers to the total count of individuals employed by a business or organization, either on a full-time or part-time basis. This metric is often used for various purposes including business valuation, eligibility for certain benefits or programs, and as an indicator of company size and capacity." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Workforce Size" .

<RTzCl6pL4nmd45HEBPCRLt> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Breach of Nonsolicitation Agreement" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RDR8hWYIaoudg2qZmCbzto6> ;
    skos:altLabel "Verstoß gegen die Nichtwerbevereinbarung"@de-de,
        "Breach of Nonsolicitation Agreement"@en-gb,
        "Incumplimiento de Acuerdo de No Solicitación"@es-es,
        "Incumplimiento de Acuerdo de No Solicitación"@es-mx,
        "Violation de l'accord de non-sollicitation"@fr-fr,
        "הפרת הסכם אי-סוליציטציה"@he-il,
        "नॉन-सॉलिसिटेशन समझौते का उल्लंघन"@hi-in,
        "ノンソリシテーション契約違反"@ja-jp,
        "Violação do acordo de não solicitação"@pt-br,
        "违反禁止招揽协议"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A breach of nonsolicitation agreement occurs when a party violates the terms of a contract that prohibits them from soliciting or attempting to solicit the employees, clients, or customers of another party, typically their former employer or business partner. Nonsolicitation agreements are often included in employment contracts, partnership agreements, or business sale agreements to protect a company's relationships with its workforce and clientele." .

