<RU1dvjPyTUgMePOcj2YloO> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Contested Divorce" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RDhTbfA9WACnFGtRuw8v57e> ;
    skos:definition "A Contested Divorce is a type of divorce in which the spouses are unable to reach an agreement on key issues such as division of property, child custody, spousal support, or other matters related to the dissolution of their marriage. In a contested divorce, these issues are typically resolved through litigation, with a court making decisions on behalf of the spouses. It often involves a more lengthy and adversarial legal process compared to an uncontested divorce, where the parties agree on the terms of the divorce." .

<RU20xmO7EqpYUmPGUbjt4L> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Contact Name Suffix - III (Third)" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RCOYxInIdB2hOEl2dAlgQQH> ;
    skos:altLabel "The Third" ;
    skos:definition "The suffix \"III\" stands for \"Third\" and is used after a person's full name to distinguish them as the third generation to bear that name in their family. Typically, it follows a grandfather, father, and son who all share the same name, and it helps in differentiating among them in formal, legal, or financial documents." ;
    skos:prefLabel "III" .

<RUAD4q6o0o2WNncfXZ9Bp1> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Management Information Circular" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RmCERXtzdqIJcW9mdbk0Bb> ;
    skos:altLabel "Investor Voting Guide" ;
    skos:definition "A Management Information Circular is a document prepared by a company's management to provide shareholders with material information needed to make informed voting decisions at a shareholders' meeting. It often includes proposals, background information, and recommendations from the board of directors." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Shareholder Meeting Document" .

<RUBi4AYhUtpu5FhXaia36Q> a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "folio:notarized" ;
    rdfs:domain <RDCkFrEclhipkoHPgckuFY6>,
        <RL7sqh8NY6UuTxs6rerO5U> ;
    rdfs:range <RDt4vQCYDfY0R9fZ5FNnTbj> ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf <R9OgtSm35ykpUSi7mgiCW> ;
    skos:altLabel "notarized" ;
    skos:definition "In legal terms, \"notarized\" refers to the process where a document is officially certified by a notary public, a licensed official who verifies the identity of the signatories and their understanding and willingness to sign the document. This process lends authenticity and legal weight to the document, often required for legal formalities such as property deeds, wills, and contracts." .

<RUCs1tfF1J4XdhUkIhPx3R> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Lung Transplantation" ;
    dc:source <https://www.ssa.gov/disability/professionals/bluebook/3.00-Respiratory-Adult.htm#3_11> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RcqrMBmLwAweHAkomaAaNq> ;
    skos:definition "Lung transplantation is a surgical procedure in which one or both diseased lungs are replaced with healthy lungs from a donor. This treatment is typically considered for patients with end-stage lung disease, such as chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) or pulmonary fibrosis, who have not responded to other therapies." .

<RUDVKmMNlScgBVLBkFrgcQ> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Equity Committee" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RCoOnTANPIS6LCYx2SVkLJL> ;
    skos:altLabel "Equity Holders' Committee" ;
    skos:definition "An Equity Committee represents the interests of equity holders (shareholders) in a bankruptcy or restructuring process. This committee ensures that the rights and priorities of shareholders are considered in negotiations, particularly in scenarios where their investments are at risk of being diluted or wiped out." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Shareholders' Committee" .

