    skos:definition "The Universal Church is the totality of the Catholic Church as the one Body of Christ, gathered from all peoples, places, and times. The Universal Church subsists in the communion of faith, sacraments, and governance united under Christ and the successor of Peter."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "The Universal Church embraces diverse rites united in doctrine and sacramental life."^^xsd:string,
        "The Universal Church gathers the faithful across history into one Body of Christ."^^xsd:string,
        "The Universal Church is made present through communion with the pope and the bishops."^^xsd:string,
        "The Universal Church manifests unity through shared creed, sacraments, and apostolic governance."^^xsd:string,
        "The Universal Church professes one faith across all nations and cultures."^^xsd:string .

