<RVhGjQ3xfypuiihrEes52P> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Ritual Cleanliness Law Events" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <ROgocFufRBHZKkFfPDYyYh> ;
    skos:altLabel "Ritual Purity Code Institution"^^xsd:string,
        "Sacred Purity Prescription"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Ritual Cleanliness Law Events encompass the occasions when God established regulations distinguishing ritual purity from impurity, governing access to sacred space and community participation. These events span from Levitical purity codes through prophetic spiritualization to Jesus's radical reinterpretation, defining boundaries between holy and common, clean and unclean."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Catholic biblical scholarship analyzes ritual cleanliness law events to understand ancient Israel's symbolic boundary-making between sacred and profane."^^xsd:string,
        "Liturgical historians trace ritual cleanliness law events to explain baptism's roots in Jewish purification practices."^^xsd:string,
        "Theological commentaries examine ritual cleanliness law events to discern how Jesus internalized external purity requirements."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:note """Clean and Unclean Animals (Leviticus 11)
Childbirth Purification Laws (Leviticus 12)
Skin Disease Regulations (Leviticus 13-14)
Bodily Discharge Laws (Leviticus 15)
Corpse Contact Impurity (Numbers 19)
Menstrual Purity Regulations (Leviticus 15:19-30)
Red Heifer Purification Rite (Numbers 19:1-10)
Water Purification Requirements
Priestly Purity Standards (Leviticus 21-22)
Temple Entry Restrictions
Jesus's Touch Healing of Lepers (Mark 1:40-45)
Jesus's Teaching on Inner Purity (Mark 7:1-23)
Peter's Vision Declaring All Clean (Acts 10:9-16)
Paul's Teaching on Food and Conscience (Romans 14)"""^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel "Purity Law Establishment Events"^^xsd:string .

