        "Farming Ethics"^^xsd:string,
        "Stewardship of the Land"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Agricultural Ethics examines the stewardship of the land, the rights of laborers, and the sustainable production of food in accordance with the dignity of the human person. It applies the principles of the common good and the universal destination of goods to the cultivation, distribution, and consumption of the earth's resources."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Advocating for the equitable distribution of grain to regions suffering from famine."^^xsd:string,
        "Ensuring fair wages and safe working conditions for seasonal harvesters."^^xsd:string,
        "Implementing sustainable farming techniques to protect the soil for future generations."^^xsd:string .

