<RVoE4pdI0NVz0KkTAL6CEj> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Eternal Law" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R8LCVHYfxA8Lri3uDg3TTsF> ;
    skos:altLabel "Divine Eternal Wisdom"^^xsd:string,
        "Eternal Divine Law"^^xsd:string,
        "God’s Eternal Ordinance"^^xsd:string,
        "Lex Aeterna"@la ;
    skos:definition "Eternal Law (Lex Aeterna) is God’s eternal wisdom and rational ordering by which God governs all creation toward its proper end. In Catholic theology, Eternal Law grounds and measures every other true law, and creatures participate in it according to their nature, especially through reason and grace."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "A just human law aligns with eternal law through natural law’s principles."^^xsd:string,
        "Catholic moral theology evaluates positive laws by their conformity to eternal law."^^xsd:string,
        "Eternal law orders creation toward God as its final end."^^xsd:string,
        "Natural law expresses rational creatures’ participation in eternal law."^^xsd:string .

<RVoruROtalNTiniXRiHcxG> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "War Clause Claim" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RDkqXQLaqeFlhG4isnkHJuv> ;
    skos:altLabel "Kriegsklauselanspruch"@de-de,
        "War Clause Claim"@en-gb,
        "Reclamación de cláusula de guerra"@es-es,
        "Reclamación de cláusula de guerra"@es-mx,
        "Réclamation de clause de guerre"@fr-fr,
        "תביעת סעיף מלחמה"@he-il,
        "युद्ध शर्त दावा"@hi-in,
        "戦争条項請求"@ja-jp,
        "Reivindicação de cláusula de guerra"@pt-br,
        "战争条款索赔"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A War Clause claim is a legal argument asserting that a particular action or law exceeds the constitutional authority granted to the government in times of war. This claim is based on the interpretation that the War Clause, which grants Congress the power to declare war, also imposes limitations on the government's actions during war, such as the exercise of certain powers or the infringement of individual rights." .

<RVqw56uVNOkyhXBm2PRjJr> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Successor in Interest Petition" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RKY2B2HNSx5K82dgVN6Qn7> ;
    skos:altLabel "I-140 Successor in Interest Petition" ;
    skos:definition "The I-140 Successor in Interest Petition is a process in the United States through which a new employer or entity assumes the sponsorship of an employment-based immigrant visa (green card) petition that was previously filed by a predecessor employer. This is relevant when the original petitioner goes out of business or undergoes a merger, acquisition, or other organizational change. The new employer or entity can file a Successor in Interest Petition to continue the green card process for the beneficiary (foreign worker) without starting the process anew, provided certain conditions are met." .

