<RWIHny9UXFuBj5mDBhG4A4> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Three-fifths Clause Claim" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RDkqXQLaqeFlhG4isnkHJuv> ;
    skos:altLabel "Anspruch auf den Drei-Fünftel-Klausel"@de-de,
        "Three-fifths Clause Claim"@en-gb,
        "Reclamo de la Cláusula de Tres Quintos"@es-es,
        "Reclamo de la Cláusula de Tres Quintos"@es-mx,
        "Réclamation de la clause des trois cinquièmes"@fr-fr,
        "תביעת סעיף שלוש-חמישים"@he-il,
        "तीन-पांचवां धारा दावा"@hi-in,
        "三分の五条項クレーム"@ja-jp,
        "Reivindicação da Cláusula dos Três Quintos"@pt-br,
        "三分之五条款索赔"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A Three-fifths Clause claim is a legal assertion tied to Article I, Section 2, Clause 3 of the U.S. Constitution, historically known as the Three-fifths Clause. This clause counted enslaved individuals as three-fifths of a person for purposes of representation and taxation, but it was effectively rendered obsolete by the Thirteenth Amendment, which abolished slavery." .

