        "Parte interessada"@pt-br,
        "利益相关者"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "In project management, a person who has an interest in the project's outcome." .

<RWhzz8UrFIWOHpJGZYFfvC> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Spiritual Direction Authority" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R9aY60yvdEVudPss03CM1LF> ;
    skos:altLabel "Authority of Spiritual Direction"^^xsd:string,
        "Direction of Souls"^^xsd:string,
        "Pastoral Discernment Authority"^^xsd:string,
        "Spiritual Guidance Authority"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Spiritual Direction Authority is the moral authority exercised by a spiritual director to guide another person in discerning God’s will and responding faithfully to grace. Spiritual Direction Authority operates through counsel and discernment, not coercion, and it respects conscience while fostering growth in holiness."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "A director advises boundaries that protect freedom while encouraging fidelity to grace."^^xsd:string,
        "A priest helps a layperson discern a possible vocation through ongoing direction."^^xsd:string,
        "A spiritual director helps a directee recognize movements of consolation and desolation."^^xsd:string,
        "A spiritual director suggests prayer practices suited to a directee’s state in life."^^xsd:string .

