        "准合同索赔"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A quasi-contract claim is a legal claim that arises when one party receives a benefit from another party, even though there was no actual contract between them, and the law implies a promise to pay for that benefit." .

<RWyyjFeGJPSetUwHMyCAJK> a owl:Class ;
