<RXJ73emLq5nZqPRdOBKLIj> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Jesus' Walking on Water" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R8eB4tGcIUItbvkSlnjfbOw> ;
    skos:altLabel "Epiphany on the Waters"^^xsd:string,
        "Walking on Water by Jesus"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Jesus’ Walking on Water means the miraculous act by which Jesus Christ walked upon the surface of the Sea of Galilee and approached his disciples’ boat. Jesus’ Walking on Water reveals Christ’s divine authority over the laws of nature and strengthens the disciples’ faith."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Christian theology interprets the walking on water as a revelation of Christ’s divine identity."^^xsd:string,
        "Confession of Faith by the Disciples"^^xsd:string,
        "Rescue of Peter from the Water"^^xsd:string,
        "The Gospels recount Jesus walking on the Sea of Galilee toward the disciples’ boat."^^xsd:string .

<RXNDomJj6civMNyyCWUkz6> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Part-Time Employee" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RBY4j5UKZ7L8gp0q9Wrxyge> ;
    skos:definition "A Part-Time Employee is an individual who works fewer hours per week than what is considered full-time by their employer or by labor laws. While part-time employees may have more flexible schedules, they often have limited or no access to benefits like health insurance, retirement plans, and paid time off." .

