<RZxj9Aij0HZZXlQzbf4bot> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "God's Call to Abram"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RfEesRQkyv0zcnO5ApLLpP> ;
    skos:altLabel "Abram's Divine Summons"^^xsd:string,
        "Abram's Vocational Call"^^xsd:string,
        "Call of Abraham"^^xsd:string,
        "God's call to Abraham"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "God's Call to Abram represents the foundational divine summons when God commanded Abram to leave his country, kindred, and father's house for an unknown land, promising to make him a great nation and source of blessing. This event initiates the Abrahamic covenant narrative, marking the moment when God chose one man through whom all families of the earth would receive blessing."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Catholic vocation directors use God's call to Abram as the archetypal example of responding to divine summons requiring faith and sacrifice."^^xsd:string,
        "Liturgical readings during Lent feature God's call to Abram to encourage believers toward conversion and spiritual pilgrimage."^^xsd:string,
        "Spiritual writers employ God's call to Abram as a paradigm for discerning God's voice amid competing voices and securities."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:note """God's Command to Leave (Genesis 12:1)
Promise of Great Nation (Genesis 12:2)
Promise of Name and Blessing (Genesis 12:2)
Promise to Bless Blessing-Givers, Curse Cursers (Genesis 12:3)
Universal Blessing Promise (Genesis 12:3)
Abram's Obedient Departure (Genesis 12:4)
Journey from Haran to Canaan (Genesis 12:4-5)
Lot's Accompaniment (Genesis 12:4-5)
Arrival at Shechem (Genesis 12:6)
First Altar Building in Canaan (Genesis 12:7)
Divine Appearance and Land Promise (Genesis 12:7)"""^^xsd:string .

