        "归化条款要求"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A Naturalization Clause claim is a legal assertion related to Article I, Section 8, Clause 4 of the United States Constitution, which grants Congress the power \"To establish a uniform Rule of Naturalization.\" This clause provides the federal government with the authority to set the rules for becoming a U.S. citizen. A claim involving the Naturalization Clause may arise in situations where there is a dispute over the application or interpretation of federal immigration and naturalization laws." .

