    skos:definition "A Dominican Priest is a presbyter who belongs to the Order of Preachers and lives according to its rule, dedicated to the ministry of preaching for the salvation of souls. He unites priestly ministry with study, common life, and apostolic preaching rooted in truth."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "A Dominican priest preaches homilies grounded in theological study."^^xsd:string,
        "Dominican priests combine contemplation and preaching in their ministry."^^xsd:string,
        "Dominican priests live a common life ordered toward preaching."^^xsd:string .

