<RdydModaBAfoUy0ld7x8yT> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Circumcision as Covenant Sign"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RfEesRQkyv0zcnO5ApLLpP> ;
    skos:altLabel "Abrahamic Circumcision Institution"^^xsd:string,
        "Brit Milah Establishment"^^xsd:string,
        "Covenant of Circumcision"^^xsd:string,
        "Eighth-Day Circumcision Command"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Circumcision as Covenant Sign represents the divine institution of male circumcision as the permanent physical mark of God's covenant with Abraham and his descendants. This event establishes circumcision as the perpetual sign distinguishing God's covenant people, requiring the removal of the foreskin on the eighth day as an enduring testimony to covenant membership."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Biblical scholars analyze circumcision as covenant sign within ancient Near Eastern contexts where various cultures practiced ritual circumcision differently."^^xsd:string,
        "Homilies employ circumcision as covenant sign when explaining Paul's teachings about circumcision of the heart versus flesh."^^xsd:string,
        "Liturgical tradition celebrates Jesus's circumcision, honoring circumcision as covenant sign while proclaiming Christ's fulfillment."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:note """Circumcision Command to Abraham (Genesis 17:10-14)
Eighth-Day Requirement (Genesis 17:12)
Household Circumcision Mandate (Genesis 17:12-13)
Stranger and Slave Inclusion (Genesis 17:12-13)
Everlasting Covenant Declaration (Genesis 17:13)
Uncircumcised Exclusion Penalty (Genesis 17:14)
Abraham's Immediate Obedience (Genesis 17:23-27)
Ishmael's Circumcision at Thirteen (Genesis 17:25)
Isaac's Eighth-Day Circumcision (Genesis 21:4)
Moses's Son's Circumcision Crisis (Exodus 4:24-26)
Joshua's Mass Circumcision at Gilgal (Joshua 5:2-9)
Paul's Circumcision Theology (Romans 2:25-29)
Jerusalem Council Circumcision Debate (Acts 15:1-29)"""^^xsd:string .

