    skos:definition "These rights pertain to the use of water from sources that exist on the surface of the land, such as lakes, rivers, and streams. The allocation and usage of these rights can be based on factors like historic use, regional laws, and treaties." .

<ReklTm0AtBkDQ0xcUykeaI> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Commendation of Spirit to the Father" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RBIF8SqULlcUju99hpRYHBh> ;
    skos:altLabel "Final Word of Jesus on the Cross"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Commendation of Spirit to the Father means Jesus Christ’s final act of entrusting his spirit to the Father at the moment of his death on the cross. Commendation of Spirit to the Father expresses Christ’s perfect filial obedience and consummates his self-offering within the Paschal sacrifice."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Catholic theology interprets the commendation of Jesus’ spirit as the supreme act of trust and obedience to the Father."^^xsd:string,
        """Jesus uttered a loud cry and said, “Father, into Your hands I commend My spirit.” After He said this, He expired.
(Luke 23:46)"""^^xsd:string,
        "The Gospel of Luke records Jesus saying, “Father, into your hands I commend my spirit,” before he died."^^xsd:string .

