<ReuxkCERjaGTgHW62N0jq1> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Act of Contrition" ;
    dc:source <https://www.xavier.edu/jesuitresource/online-resources/prayer-index/catholic-prayers> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RyTfHxUQPVMUQrtIt1Mycz> ;
    skos:altLabel "Prayer of Contrition"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "A Catholic prayer in which a person expresses sorrow for sin, rejects sin, and resolves to amend life with God’s help. It commonly includes love of God, repentance, a purpose of amendment, and a request for mercy through Jesus Christ."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "A penitent recited an Act of Contrition after confessing sins during the Sacrament of Penance and Reconciliation."^^xsd:string,
        "After realizing he had harmed a friend, he prayed an Act of Contrition and then sought reconciliation through apology and repair."^^xsd:string,
        "During nightly prayer, she prayed an Act of Contrition to repent for the day’s sins and renew her resolve to avoid sin."^^xsd:string,
        """My God, I am sorry for my sins with all my heart.
In choosing to do wrong and failing to do good,
I have sinned against you whom I should love above all things.
I firmly intend, with your help, to do penance, to sin no more,
and to avoid whatever leads me to sin.
Our Savior Jesus Christ suffered and died for us.
In His name. My God have mercy."""^^xsd:string .

<Revs4g1weWrrjVNT9CQSy3> a owl:Class ;
