<RfrrIqKTh9me3Z5tlVD7Fz> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Testicle Cancer" ;
    dc:source <https://www.ssa.gov/disability/professionals/bluebook/13.00-NeoplasticDiseases-Malignant-Adult.htm#13_25> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RDF3VrmH1eapfkrSQstevLs> ;
    skos:altLabel "Male Gonadal Cancer" ;
    skos:definition "Testicle cancer, also known as testicular cancer, is a malignant tumor that originates in the tissues of one or both testicles, the male reproductive glands located in the scrotum. It includes various subtypes, such as seminomas and non-seminomas, and can cause symptoms like testicular lumps, swelling, and discomfort, often requiring treatments like surgery, chemotherapy, and radiation." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Testicular Cancer" .

<RfwjIqLfrhhnCE2TsmLCeR> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Consolidated Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act Claim" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R8TmxqBbWaNgdm0lJQdY6D4> ;
    skos:altLabel "COBRA Claim",
        "Anspruch gemäß dem Gesetz zur Konsolidierung der Haushaltsmittel und zur Rechtschreibung"@de-de,
        "Consolidated Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act Claim"@en-gb,
        "Reclamo de la Ley de Conciliación Consolidada de Presupuesto Omnibus"@es-es,
        "Reclamo de la Ley de Consolidación de Presupuesto Omnibus de Conciliación"@es-mx,
        "Réclamation en vertu de la loi sur la réconciliation budgétaire consolidée Omnibus"@fr-fr,
        "תביעה על פי חוק הסיכום המאוחד לתקציבי אומניבוס"@he-il,
        "संयुक्त ओमनिबस बजट समन्वय अधिनियम दावा"@hi-in,
        "総合予算調整法に基づく請求"@ja-jp,
        "Reivindicação de acordo com a Lei de Reconciliação Orçamentária Consolidada Omnibus"@pt-br,
        "根据《综合预算和协调法案》提出的索赔"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A COBRA claim is a legal action initiated by a former employee against their former employer for not complying with the U.S. law called the Consolidated Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act (COBRA). COBRA requires employers with 20 or more employees to offer certain terminated employees and their eligible dependents the opportunity to continue their group health insurance coverage for a limited time after their employment ends. The claim typically arises when an employer does not comply with applicable COBRA requirements, which can result in the loss of health insurance coverage for the affected individual and their dependents. Employers can face liability for violating COBRA, which can result in significant damages for the affected individual." .

