        "未能及时支付索赔"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A fail-to-pay-timely claim is a legal action initiated by an employee against their employer for not providing timely payment of wages or other compensation. The claim typically arises when an employer does not comply with applicable laws, which require employers to pay employees their earned wages at regular intervals, such as weekly or bi-weekly. The claim can also include allegations of employers not paying earned commissions, bonuses, or other forms of compensation in a timely manner." .

