    skos:definition "Mirror Wills are separate but virtually identical wills made by two people, typically spouses or partners, that reflect each other's wishes. These documents contain reciprocal provisions, usually leaving everything to each other and then to agreed-upon beneficiaries, but remain legally distinct and individually revocable." .

<RnuLwNuTI14dlELybEWuWD> a owl:Class ;
