<Rqw7qSfvFMVfYRlZYoNaad> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Blessed Are the Peacemakers" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RDS4ZvoTuxk7hu7zuyJRyoR> ;
    skos:altLabel "Seventh Beatitude"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Blessed Are the Peacemakers means the beatitude in which Jesus Christ declares blessed those who actively work to reconcile, heal divisions, and establish peace rooted in justice and truth. Blessed Are the Peacemakers promises divine sonship to those who reflect God’s reconciling work in the world."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Christian theology interprets peacemaking as active reconciliation grounded in justice and love."^^xsd:string,
        "The Gospel of Matthew records Jesus proclaiming, “Blessed are the peacemakers, for they shall be called children of God.”"^^xsd:string .

<Rr0s6k9vB5c3kGhFhro0TS> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Blessed Are the Poor in Spirit" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RDS4ZvoTuxk7hu7zuyJRyoR> ;
    skos:altLabel "First Beatitude"^^xsd:string,
        "Poverty of Spirit Beatitude"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Blessed Are the Poor in Spirit means the beatitude in which Jesus Christ declares blessed those who recognize their spiritual dependence on God and place their trust in him. Blessed Are the Poor in Spirit promises the Kingdom of heaven to those who live in humility and detachment from self-sufficiency."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Christian theology interprets poverty of spirit as humility and total reliance on God rather than material or personal security."^^xsd:string,
        "The Gospel of Matthew records Jesus proclaiming, “Blessed are the poor in spirit, for theirs is the Kingdom of heaven.”"^^xsd:string .

