    skos:definition "Weight loss due to any digestive disorder refers to the significant reduction in body weight resulting from conditions affecting the gastrointestinal tract's ability to properly digest and absorb nutrients. This can be caused by disorders such as Crohn's disease, ulcerative colitis, or chronic pancreatitis, leading to symptoms like malnutrition, decreased appetite, and malabsorption." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Nutritional Deficiency Weight Loss" .

