    skos:definition "A Withdrawal of Union Shop Authority (UD) Claim is a legal action initiated by an employer or labor organization to terminate or modify a union shop arrangement, which requires all employees in a bargaining unit to become union members as a condition of employment. This claim often arises in the context of changes in labor relations or challenges to the legality of union security clauses." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Union Deauthorization Claim" .

