<RsZqYmFpa29ujUnSiVifIp> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Organizational Chart" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RBJ4HPUl2DrL4G30lmoFKJN> ;
    skos:altLabel "Entity Chart",
        "Hierarchy Chart",
        "Structural Flowchart",
        "Structure Chart" ;
    skos:definition "An Organizational Chart is a visual diagram that outlines the structure of an organization. For example, it can show the roles, responsibilities, and relationships between employees, divisions, and other stakeholders. It can also demonstrate ownership and control of organizations, entities, and subsidiaries. Organizational Charts are commonly used for planning, managing, and communicating within organizations." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Org Chart" .

<RsbKdqD4dqt39rniZX5MM5> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Promise of Land and Descendants"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RfEesRQkyv0zcnO5ApLLpP> ;
    skos:altLabel "Inheritance and Offspring Assurance"^^xsd:string,
        "Land and Progeny Promise"^^xsd:string,
        "Territorial and Generational Covenant"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Promise of Land and Descendants encompasses God's repeated assurances to Abraham that his offspring would become numerous as stars and sand, inheriting the land of Canaan as an everlasting possession. This dual promise forms the covenant's material core, establishing both the people's identity and their territorial destiny as central to God's salvific plan."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Liturgical prayers invoked promise of land and descendants when blessing marriages, asking God to grant fruitfulness like Abraham and Sarah."^^xsd:string,
        "Some Catholic biblical theology interprets promise of land and descendants as finding ultimate fulfillment in the Church as Abraham's spiritual offspring inheriting eternal life."^^xsd:string,
        "The homily connected promise of land and descendants to New Testament teachings about believers becoming Abraham's children through faith."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:note """Initial Land Promise at Shechem (Genesis 12:7)
Stars of Heaven Comparison (Genesis 15:5)
Land Boundaries Definition (Genesis 15:18-21)
Sand of Seashore Metaphor (Genesis 22:17)
Four-Generation Exile Prediction (Genesis 15:13-16)
Everlasting Possession Declaration (Genesis 17:8)
Nations from Abraham Promise (Genesis 17:4-6)
Sarah's Son Promise (Genesis 17:15-19)
Post-Isaac Sacrifice Reaffirmation (Genesis 22:15-18)
Isaac Inheritance Confirmation (Genesis 26:3-4)
Jacob Inheritance Extension (Genesis 28:13-14)
Joseph's Egyptian Fulfillment Beginning (Genesis 50:24)"""^^xsd:string .

<Rsd5DlkpsVyqos0zrO3KYc> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Debt Security Agreement" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RVoyN9hN3m5gy3So01ZEZ8> ;
    skos:definition "A Debt Security Agreement is a legal contract that outlines the terms under which a company or government entity issues debt securities, such as bonds or notes, to investors. The agreement specifies the interest rate, maturity date, and other covenants that govern the relationship between the issuer and the holders of the debt securities." .

<RsdDEmJbxIZliJRCdd2cUf> a owl:Class ;
