    skos:altLabel "Post-Trauma Condition",
        "Trauma-Induced Anxiety Disorder",
        "Traumatic Stress Disorder" ;
    skos:definition "Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder (PTSD) is a mental health condition triggered by experiencing or witnessing a traumatic event, such as a natural disaster, serious accident, terrorist act, war/combat, rape, or other violent personal assault. Individuals with PTSD may experience intense, disturbing thoughts and feelings related to their experience long after the traumatic event has ended." ;
    skos:prefLabel "PTSD" .

