<RylyViN7f9W76RQFbZjFqU> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Autism Spectrum Disorder with Intellectual Impairment" ;
    dc:source <https://www.ssa.gov/disability/professionals/bluebook/12.00-MentalDisorders-Adult.htm#12_00B1> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RBLAHsgfwEzyP8N8VTMdgmM> ;
    skos:definition "Autism Spectrum Disorder with Intellectual Impairment is characterized by the core symptoms of autism, including deficits in social communication and interaction, and restricted, repetitive behaviors or interests. This condition is accompanied by significant limitations in intellectual functioning, affecting cognitive abilities and adaptive functioning." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Autism Spectrum Disorder with Cognitive Impairment" .

<RyqPbsFi2EtvJVJI5fVgPs> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Military Ethics" ;
    rdfs:comment "In a global Catholic ontology, Military Ethics focuses on the moral governance of force and the preservation of peace. It draws heavily from the Just War tradition (Bellum Justum), which established criteria for the legitimate use of authority, the protection of non-combatants, and the restoration of justice in the aftermath of conflict."^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <R9mTGKaFostHJfLRPz7vsst> ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <R8zVfJ5cgX7pYsgGOQESam7> ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RBY6ZBEYa2Y7NOxChUaInA2> ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <R7iSh4AXN4oJuPPGv1KQDnD> ],
        <R740KsX4ol3KSiJ2DHXcsGL> ;
    skos:altLabel "Ethics of Armed Conflict"^^xsd:string,
        "Martial Ethics"^^xsd:string,
        "Morality of Warfare"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Military Ethics evaluates the conditions under which the use of lethal force is permissible and the conduct required of those engaged in armed conflict. It ensures that military action remains subordinate to the moral law, prioritizing the defense of the innocent and the establishment of a lasting peace."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Ensuring that the response to an unjust aggression remains proportionate to the original injury."^^xsd:string,
        "Prohibiting the use of weapons that cause indiscriminate destruction to civilian populations."^^xsd:string,
        "Providing spiritual and psychological care to soldiers to help them maintain their humanity during combat."^^xsd:string .

<Ryrfm8CLm2S7WB2iF0ODhU> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "DUPLICATE: The Angelus"^^xsd:string ;
    dc:source <https://www.xavier.edu/jesuitresource/online-resources/prayer-index/catholic-prayers> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R7wBHDda7bW9qL2BawI6mDA> ;
    skos:example """The Angel of the Lord declared to Mary:
And she conceived of the Holy Spirit.

Hail Mary, full of grace, the Lord is with thee; blessed art thou among women and blessed is the fruit of thy womb, Jesus. Holy Mary, Mother of God, pray for us sinners, now and at the hour of
our death. Amen.

Behold the handmaid of the Lord: Be it done unto me according to Thy word.

Hail Mary . . .

And the Word was made Flesh: And dwelt among us.

Hail Mary . . .

Pray for us, O Holy Mother of God, that we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.

Let us pray:

Pour forth, we beseech Thee, O Lord, Thy grace into our hearts; that we, to whom the incarnation of Christ, Thy Son, was made known by the message of an angel, may by His Passion and Cross be brought to the glory of His Resurrection, through the same Christ Our Lord."""^^xsd:string ;
    skos:note "DEPRECATED in favor of Angelicus"^^xsd:string .

