    skos:definition "Co-Sureties Contributing on Debt Default: A legal concept where multiple parties agree to be jointly responsible for a debt, and if one party defaults, the other parties are responsible for contributing to the payment of the debt." .

<R75OjKiIyaZ7UKYKYmCvFRL> a owl:Class ;
