    skos:definition "The U.S. Agency for Global Media, formerly the Broadcasting Board of Governors (BBG), is an independent agency of the United States government. The BBG supervises Voice of America (VOA), Radio Free Europe/Radio Liberty, Radio y Television Marti, Radio Free Asia, and the Middle East Broadcast Networks." ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "USAGM" ;
    skos:prefLabel "U.S. Agency for Global Media" .

<R787C07azf3BxNqxCxSvBxc> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "County Governmental Body" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RBQGborh1CfXanGZipDL0Qo> ;
    skos:definition "A county governmental body oversees governance at the county level, which is typically a subdivision of a state or province, but above local city or town governments. County governments handle administrative and regulatory responsibilities that span multiple municipalities within their boundaries. These responsibilities can include law enforcement (through county sheriff's departments), maintaining county roads and infrastructure, overseeing public health and welfare programs, managing property records, and conducting elections." .

<R78bV0IQasgnKfZBYYexReQ> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Dormant Commerce Clause Claim" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RwipRpN2mP7u4u1N74MVzK> ],
        <RwipRpN2mP7u4u1N74MVzK> ;
    skos:altLabel "Klage wegen Verstoßes gegen die Handelsklausel im Ruhezustand"@de-de,
        "Dormant Commerce Clause Claim"@en-gb,
        "Reclamo de la Cláusula de Comercio Inactivo"@es-es,
        "Reclamo de la Cláusula de Comercio Inactivo"@es-mx,
        "Réclamation de la clause de commerce dormant"@fr-fr,
        "תביעת סעיף המסחר המיושן"@he-il,
        "निष्क्रिय वाणिज्य अनुबंध दावा"@hi-in,
        "休眠商業条項クレーム"@ja-jp,
        "Reivindicação da cláusula de comércio inativo"@pt-br,
        "休眠商业条款索赔"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A Dormant Commerce Clause claim is a legal argument asserting that a state law or regulation violates the United States Constitution by burdening or discriminating against interstate commerce. This claim is based on the interpretation that the Commerce Clause not only grants Congress the power to regulate commerce but also implies a limitation on state interference with interstate commerce." .

<R795I9ybqUdayMEcSmyDrG6> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Behavioral Market Segment" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R8UG79BtYP2uqnKNklLYXB8> ;
    skos:altLabel "Usage-Based Market Segment" ;
    skos:definition "A behavioral market segment is a group of consumers classified based on their behavior patterns, including their benefits sought, as well as their usage (of products or services). This segmentation relates to how groups of consumers seek out and interact with products or services." ;
    skos:note "Non-copyrightable idea and fact inspiration drawn from IAB 2.0. https://www.meaningcloud.com/developer/documentation/predefined/deep-categorization-models/iab-2-0" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Consumer Behavior Market Segment" .

