    skos:definition "The Termination of Parental Rights (TPR) is a legal process that permanently ends the legal relationship between a parent and their child, typically due to abuse, neglect, or abandonment, and allows for the child to be adopted or placed in a permanent home." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Termination of Parental Rights" .

<R8A4jLWkG2KpI6wfAznsSCx> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Remittitur" ;
