    skos:altLabel "Court-Ordered Damages Decrease",
        "Decreased Damages Award",
        "Judicial Reduction In Damages" ;
    skos:definition "Remittitur refers to a court's power to reduce the amount of damages awarded by a jury if the judge finds the award excessive. This practice is used to prevent the need for a new trial by offering the plaintiff the option to accept a lower amount." .

