        <RCZyrH2dIAtpDh2AzPTekph> ;
    skos:definition "A substance abuse policy is a formal document established by an organization to outline its stance on the use, possession, and distribution of drugs and alcohol in the workplace. It aims to ensure a safe and productive work environment by defining prohibited behaviors, setting forth procedures for testing and handling violations, and providing resources for prevention and treatment." .

<R9UVUxFvefgSg70axsgw01S> a owl:Class ;
