        "Révocation de la libération provisoire"@fr-fr,
        "ביטול שחרור עדיין לפני המשפט"@he-il,
        "प्रीट्रायल रिलीज रिवोकेशन"@hi-in,
        "保釈取り消し"@ja-jp,
        "Revogação da liberdade provisória"@pt-br,
        "取保候审撤销"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "The concept of Pretrial Release Revocation refers to the legal event of revoking a defendant's release from custody before trial, typically due to a violation of the conditions of their release." .

<RBoDiMryDOIE3XWHl6qgL3y> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Beyond a Reasonable Doubt" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RDV74m3ydS2I72hZ88Mf1RX> ;
    skos:altLabel "Jenseits jeden vernünftigen Zweifels"@de-de,
        "Beyond a Reasonable Doubt"@en-gb,
        "Fuera de toda duda razonable"@es-es,
        "Más allá de toda duda razonable"@es-mx,
        "Hors de tout doute raisonnable"@fr-fr,
        "מעבר לספק סביר"@he-il,
        "एक वजहबल शक से परे"@hi-in,
        "合理的疑いを超えて"@ja-jp,
        "Além de qualquer dúvida razoável"@pt-br,
        "合理怀疑的界限之外"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "The concept of \"Beyond a Reasonable Doubt\" refers to the highest standard of proof required in a criminal trial, where the evidence presented must be so convincing that there is no reasonable doubt in the mind of a reasonable person that the defendant committed the crime." .

<RBolyVfuhcZU8kIUvbQxahu> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Cahuilla" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RC1ceWXE3emNHpYlrOvvmxG> .

<RBpSutJH1FlqWIYeHLVSxhF> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Postal Service Industry" ;
    dc:identifier "TRA-POST" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.naics.com/six-digit-naics/?code=491> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RUE4fCCSnGX1wIK324EyiL> ;
    skos:altLabel "Postal and Messenger",
        "Post- und Kurierdienstbranche"@de-de,
        "Postal and Messenger Industry"@en-gb,
        "Industria Postal y de Mensajería"@es-es,
        "Industria Postal y de Mensajería"@es-mx,
        "Industrie postale et de messagerie"@fr-fr,
        "תעשיית דואר ושליחויות"@he-il,
        "डाक और मेसेंजर उद्योग"@hi-in,
        "郵便およびメッセンジャー業界"@ja-jp,
        "Indústria postal e de mensageiros"@pt-br,
        "邮政和信使行业"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition """The Postal Service subsector includes the activities of the National Post Office and its subcontractors operating under a universal service obligation to provide mail services, and using the infrastructure required to fulfill that obligation.  These services include delivering letters and small parcels.  These articles can be described as those that can be handled by one person without using special equipment.  This allows the collection, pick-up, and delivery operations to be done with limited labor costs and minimal equipment.  Sorting and transportation activities, where necessary, are generally mechanized.  The restriction to small parcels distinguishes these establishments from those in the transportation industries.  These establishments may also provide express delivery services using the infrastructure established for provision of basic mail services.

The traditional activity of the National Postal Service is described in this subsector.  Subcontractors include rural post offices on contract to the Postal Service.

Bulk transportation of mail on contract to the Postal Service is not included here, because it is usually done by transportation establishments that carry other customers' cargo as well.  Establishments that provide courier and express delivery services without operating under a universal service obligation are classified in Subsector 492, Couriers and Messengers.""" ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "POST" .

<RBpkU6cTDASAm3MhUcsNUAL> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Société à Responsabilité Limitée" ;
    dc:identifier "ENTITY-SARL" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <R87QDkTCmXall8ieqmRAsy> ],
        <R7oBWHStfmqTLn2MypkW3Pj> ;
    skos:altLabel "SARL",
        "Society with Limited Responsibility",
        "Gesellschaft mit beschränkter Haftung"@de-de,
        "Société à Responsabilité Limitée"@fr,
        "Société à Responsabilité Limitée"@fr-fr,
        "有限責任事業組合"@ja-jp,
        "Sociedade de Responsabilidade Limitada"@pt-br,
        "有限责任公司"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A Société à responsabilité limitée (short SARL and variations thereof; lit. \"society with limited responsibility\") is a form of private company that exists mainly in French-speaking countries, such as France, Luxembourg, Monaco, Algeria, Morocco, Tunisia, Madagascar, Lebanon, and Switzerland (where it is also designated by GmbH or Sagl)." ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "SARL" .

<RBq37J194MpjXkKw99pB3E0> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Employer-Sponsored Health Plan" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RClKvZvieudjUMtKTcCsMAn> ;
    skos:definition "This is a health insurance plan selected and partially funded by an employer as part of the benefits package for employees. The employer usually pays a portion of the premium, and the employee's share is often deducted from their paycheck." .

<RBqieZofpX6g9xN2RuFUCIp> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Guam Territory Courts" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RyItksdT5vInqyBuoGgoDr> ;
    skos:definition "The Guam Territory Courts are a subset of the U.S. Territory Courts and include the Guam Supreme Court." .

<RBrs0FH5hpFyVnTb3mbSz60> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Political Risk" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.canada.ca/en/treasury-board-secretariat/corporate/risk-management/taxonomies.html> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <R7nCzcmx7E2irmj7iF0N1Uk> ],
        <RxTxaN981tLTsN82qPBcp> ;
    skos:definition "The threats and opportunities associated with the political climate and operating context of an organization — such as the potential for negative consequences arising from political events, decisions, or changes in the regulatory environment that may affect an organization's operations, investments, or overall business climate. These risks can include policy shifts, government instability, geopolitical tensions, or trade restrictions, potentially leading to financial losses, operational disruptions, or reduced market opportunities" .

<RBsFqa5TMQWMQHxVngr0isg> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Social Security Contribution" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RWNHtgqXOWSnS2m1dFK5L0> ;
    skos:altLabel "Social Insurance Contribution",
        "Social Insurance Payment",
        "FICA Payment"@en-us ;
    skos:definition "A Social Security Contribution refers to the payment made by employees and employers to fund the social security system, which provides benefits for retirement, disability, and survivorship. These contributions are typically deducted from wages and matched by employers, ensuring financial support for eligible beneficiaries." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Social Security Tax Payment" .

<RBsiX2FSnOKhxvLGKoU9x1> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Cross-Border Objective" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RBjHwNNG2ASVmasLFU42otk> ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <R9aSzp9cEiBCzObnP92jYFX> ],
        <RlNFgB3TQfMzV26V4V7u4E> ;
    skos:altLabel "Comparative Law Practice",
        "Cross-Border Practice",
        "International",
        "International Practice",
        "Multijurisdictional Practice",
        "Transnational Practice" ;
    skos:definition "Cross-Border Practice, also known as comparative law practice and international practice,  involves lawyers providing legal services concerning legal matters that span the laws of two or more jurisdictions. This practice requires a deep understanding of the legal systems, regulations, and cultural considerations of the relevant jurisdictions." ;
    skos:example "Advising On International Trade Agreements: Providing legal advice on compliance with trade agreements between countries.",
        "Drafting And Reviewing International Contracts: Creating contracts that must comply with the legal requirements of multiple jurisdictions.",
        "Facilitating Cross-Border Corporate Transactions: Assisting in mergers and acquisitions where the entities involved are located in different countries.",
        "Handling Cross-Border Dispute Resolution: Representing clients in litigation or arbitration that involves parties from different jurisdictions.",
        "Navigating Cross-Border Regulatory Compliance: Ensuring that clients adhere to the regulatory standards of all relevant jurisdictions in their operations." ;
    skos:prefLabel "International Objective" .

<RBsvz4pgTzoSsHozyIMUdrv> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Hidden Life at Nazareth" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R7oT3qg4wZmB5K3qC79EVID> ;
    skos:altLabel "Growth in Wisdom and Grace"^^xsd:string,
        "Hidden Life of Jesus"^^xsd:string,
        "Hidden Years of Christ"^^xsd:string,
        "Life in the Holy Family"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Hidden Life at Nazareth means the period of Jesus Christ’s early life spent in Nazareth in obedience to Mary and Joseph, largely unrecorded in Scripture. Hidden Life at Nazareth reveals the sanctification of ordinary human life through Christ’s quiet growth in wisdom, age, and grace."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Christian theology reflects on the hidden life at Nazareth as a model of holiness in ordinary family life."^^xsd:string,
        "The Gospel of Luke notes that Jesus lived in Nazareth and was obedient to Mary and Joseph."^^xsd:string .

<RBuHmAe6jQq5gQSLIXZI1oN> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Citation to Legislation" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty <RdpSPh3bFHYrQ3vYPDwJYB> ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RDEUUJX38pZaHpn7lXM0GIV> ],
        <R7fEpxSrDSl1VojeYSxppg> ;
    skos:altLabel "Zitierung von Gesetzestexten"@de-de,
        "Citation to Legislation"@en-gb,
        "Cita a la legislación"@es-es,
        "Cita a la legislación"@es-mx,
        "Citation de la législation"@fr-fr,
        "ציטוט לחקיקה"@he-il,
        "विधान को उद्धरण"@hi-in,
        "法令の引用"@ja-jp,
        "Citação à legislação"@pt-br,
        "引用法律"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A document's citations to bills and other legislation (e.g., bills before a legislature, bills before congress)." .

<RBuPVAcB52MFzxOD0Ov56jq> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Bankruptcy Exemptions" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty <RB9WPZAmqztZGzX1qXk6gXv> ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <R7vBjMmDitSBmBKZvNugCLG> ],
        <RCzs34uEQI9f4cuWp3bQO0P> ;
    skos:altLabel "Insolvenzfreistellungen"@de-de,
        "Bankruptcy Exemptions"@en-gb,
        "Exenciones de bancarrota"@es-es,
        "Exenciones de quiebra"@es-mx,
        "Exemptions de faillite"@fr-fr,
        "עמלות פשיטת רגל פשיטת רגל"@he-il,
        "दिवालियापन छूट"@hi-in,
        "破産免責"@ja-jp,
        "Isenções de falência"@pt-br,
        "破产豁免"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "Bankruptcy Exemptions are legal protections that allow individuals filing for bankruptcy to keep certain assets, such as a primary residence or personal property, from being seized by creditors to satisfy outstanding debts." .

<RBvvWK0xG1iusmC0NoE8dEo> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Soldier" ;
    rdfs:comment "In a global Catholic ontology, the Soldier or Combatant is defined not merely by the capacity to use force, but by the heavy moral burden of protecting the common good. The Church distinguishes the person’s inherent dignity from their functional role as a \"minister of security and liberty,\" a role that remains strictly bound by the ethical limits of just warfare."^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RBY6ZBEYa2Y7NOxChUaInA2> ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <R79CBFMSwUZjwKG9qV6AfQb> ],
        <R7qVMTAfVUMCpr6LhRZ23eF>,
        <R9e1bYJPmM4lWEdGvWIxf6t> ;
    skos:altLabel "A Soldier is a member of the armed forces or an authorized belligerent group who engages directly in hostilities during an armed conflict. This status carries the grave obligation to act only under legitimate authority and to maintain a conscience formed by the principles of justice and the protection of the innocent."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "A soldier may exercise the right of conscientious objection when a specific conflict is deemed profoundly unjust by a well-formed conscience."^^xsd:string,
        "A soldier must refuse to carry out an order that violates the moral law or involves the deliberate killing of non-combatants."^^xsd:string,
        "Soldiers must obey a lawful order to defend a civilian population from an unprovoked aggression."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel "Armed Services Member"^^xsd:string .

<RBwZjjQmoJgjgi1yx1YBOm7> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Unpaid Wages Claim" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <R8Eoebh7pvPtkWrkUTgecmu> ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RCwT0yMShmi5V0Q2Y9Yn070> ],
        <R9UYGSnWQz2MvNsWUofGb6J> ;
    skos:altLabel "Anspruch auf unbezahlten Lohn"@de-de,
        "Unpaid Wages Claim"@en-gb,
        "Reclamación de salarios impagados"@es-es,
        "Reclamo de salarios no pagados"@es-mx,
        "Réclamation de salaires impayés"@fr-fr,
        "תביעה על שכר לא משולם"@he-il,
        "अवैतनिक वेतन दावा"@hi-in,
        "未払い賃金請求"@ja-jp,
        "Reclamação de salários não pagos"@pt-br,
        "未付工资索赔"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "An unpaid wages claim is a legal action initiated by an employee against their employer for not paying the employee their earned wages. The claim typically arises when an employer does not comply with applicable laws, which require employers to pay employees for all hours worked and to pay at least the minimum wage rate. The claim can include allegations of employers failing to pay the employee their regular pay, overtime pay, earned commissions, or other forms of compensation. Employees may also bring unpaid wages claims for non-payment of bonuses or other benefits owed to them." .

<RBxrjeXCt4RmLEDdf412Ao1> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Partnership Agreement" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <R9JkfZIjkVSa5ud1tJ14w3i> ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RCXorl2fj2P6I15SoL42ybA> ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <R9fslqJlcJW7E5ey4lzHMF5> ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <R95dH92zrdqxZYn7erKlwpU> ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RC3I2GwWuuKWmRJVXgxXeb> ],
        <RCNdhIWpodXkmuDPUE0YLKX> ;
    skos:definition "A Partnership Agreement is a contract between partners in a partnership that specifies their mutual obligations, responsibilities, profit-sharing ratios, and other operational terms." .

<RBxsGEnNaCuScNMawpvTjF3> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Directory" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RTPFix1eiYqgdushRunICo> ;
    skos:altLabel "Verzeichnis"@de-de,
        "Directory"@en-gb,
        "Directorio"@es-es,
        "Directorio"@es-mx,
        "Répertoire"@fr-fr,
        "ספריה"@he-il,
        "डायरेक्टरी"@hi-in,
        "ディレクトリ"@ja-jp,
