    skos:definition "The reputation evidence objective is the legal principle that allows the use of a person's or entity's reputation as evidence in court to prove character or conduct in specific circumstances. This type of evidence is typically used to establish a pattern of behavior or to refute allegations, and is subject to strict rules to prevent unfair prejudice." .

<RC9hKRPbfUdQjXfAQBLwpGO> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Skeletal System Cancer" ;
    dc:source <https://www.ssa.gov/disability/professionals/bluebook/13.00-NeoplasticDiseases-Malignant-Adult.htm#13_11> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RDF3VrmH1eapfkrSQstevLs> ;
    skos:altLabel "Bone Malignancy",
        "Osseous Neoplasm" ;
    skos:definition "Skeletal system cancer, also known as bone cancer, refers to malignant tumors that originate in the bones, including both primary bone cancers like osteosarcoma and secondary cancers that have metastasized from other body parts. These cancers can cause severe pain, fractures, and impaired mobility, necessitating comprehensive treatment and management." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Bone Cancer" .

