<RDAQMAQLYgoUdaKQquAhteq> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Background Check" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RdfKnWpXsG2eBmnS3oJNTF> ;
    skos:altLabel "Hintergrundüberprüfung"@de-de,
        "Background Check"@en-gb,
        "Verificación de Antecedentes"@es-es,
        "Revisión de Antecedentes"@es-mx,
        "Vérification des antécédents"@fr-fr,
        "בדיקת רקע"@he-il,
        "पृष्ठभूमि जाँच"@hi-in,
        "バックグラウンドチェック"@ja-jp,
        "Verificação de antecedentes"@pt-br,
        "背景调查"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A background check is a process through which an individual's personal, criminal, credit, and/or employment history is investigated and verified, typically by an employer, landlord, or other decision-maker. Background checks are often conducted to assess an individual's suitability for employment, housing, or other opportunities, as well as to ensure the safety and security of a workplace or community. Common elements of a background check may include verifying identity, checking criminal records, reviewing credit history, confirming education and employment history, and examining professional licenses or certifications. In many jurisdictions, background checks are regulated by laws such as the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA) to protect individual privacy and prevent discrimination." .

<RDB03224BF1b7177ab986d54> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "United States Marshals Service" ;
    dc:identifier "US-FD-DOJ-USMS" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R0DB70442Cf8b73D9275F14a> ;
    skos:altLabel "United States Marshals Service"@de-de,
        "United States Marshals Service"@en-gb,
        "Servicio de Alguaciles de los Estados Unidos"@es-es,
        "Servicio de Alguaciles de los Estados Unidos"@es-mx,
        "Service des marshals des États-Unis"@fr-fr,
        "שירות מרשלי ארצות הברית"@he-il,
        "यूनाइटेड स्टेट्स मार्शल सेवा"@hi-in,
        "アメリカ合衆国保安官局"@ja-jp,
        "Serviço de Delegados dos Estados Unidos"@pt-br,
        "美国司法部警卫局"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "The United States Marshals Service (USMS) is a federal law enforcement agency within the U.S. Department of Justice. It is the oldest American federal law enforcement agency and was created by the Judiciary Act of 1789 during the presidency of George Washington as the Office of the United States Marshal. The USMS as it stands today was established in 1969 to provide guidance and assistance to Marshals throughout the federal judicial districts. USMS is an agency of the United States executive branch reporting to the United States Attorney General, but serves as the enforcement arm of the United States federal courts to ensure the effective operation of the judiciary and integrity of the Constitution." ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "USMS" ;
    skos:prefLabel "United States Marshals Service" .

