        "Reclamaciones por discriminación laboral"@es-es,
        "Reclamaciones por discriminación laboral"@es-mx,
        "Actions en discrimination en matière d'emploi"@fr-fr,
        "תביעות על הפרת זכויות עובדים"@he-il,
        "रोजगार भेदभाव दावे"@hi-in,
        "雇用差別主張"@ja-jp,
        "Reivindicações de discriminação no emprego"@pt-br,
        "就业歧视索赔"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A claim made by an employee alleging unfair treatment or disparate impact based on a protected characteristic such as race, gender, age, or disability in the workplace." .

<RDQxFX5gW03WCTdtQbAvABt> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Joint Venture Agreement" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RC0ycQb3ti4yr7qDxhAD1Gl> ],
        <RCNdhIWpodXkmuDPUE0YLKX> ;
    skos:altLabel "Joint-Venture-Vereinbarung"@de-de,
        "Joint Venture Agreement"@en-gb,
        "Acuerdo de Joint Venture"@es-es,
        "Acuerdo de Joint Venture"@es-mx,
        "Accord de coentreprise"@fr-fr,
        "הסכם שותפות משותפת"@he-il,
        "संयुक्त उद्यम समझौता"@hi-in,
        "合弁契約"@ja-jp,
        "Acordo de Joint Venture"@pt-br,
        "合资协议"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A Joint Venture Agreement is a legal document that outlines the terms and conditions of a business arrangement between two or more parties who agree to pool their resources and expertise to achieve a specific goal or project. It defines the terms under which multiple parties collaborate on a specific project or business venture, delineating responsibilities, profit-sharing, and decision-making processes." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Joint Operating Agreement" .

<RDRpJk0pctY0wgArzOcbc3q> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Hoarseness" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R7RTOi3HJBujhrMQbvqgmBZ> ;
    skos:altLabel "Raspy Voice" ;
    skos:definition "Hoarseness is a voice disorder characterized by a rough, raspy, or strained vocal quality, often resulting from inflammation, overuse, or irritation of the vocal cords. This condition can cause difficulties in speaking clearly and may be associated with underlying medical issues such as laryngitis, vocal cord nodules, or gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD)." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Dysphonia" .

<RDSTWxMJK0mcdxB1oQtK7jC> a owl:Class ;
