<RDkZBjHchWXuRh8dwpGuJwX> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Demolition" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R9pQxz2fUIrk1LjvVP8hikg> ;
    skos:definition "Demolition is the process of tearing down or dismantling a building or structure, often to clear land for new construction or to remove unsafe or obsolete buildings. This process involves various techniques and machinery, including manual labor, wrecking balls, and controlled explosives, to safely and efficiently bring down the structure. The demolition may be the result of a legal proceeding (e.g., condemnation)." .

