        "Disturbing the Peace"@en-gb,
        "Alteración del Orden Público"@es-es,
        "Alteración del Orden Público"@es-mx,
        "Trouble à l'ordre public"@fr-fr,
        "הפרת שקט ציבור"@he-il,
        "शांति को व्यवधान"@hi-in,
        "公共の秩序を乱す行為"@ja-jp,
        "Perturbação da ordem pública"@pt-br,
        "扰乱公共秩序"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "The act of disturbing the peace refers to behavior that disrupts public order and tranquility, and is classified as a criminal misdemeanor offense." .

<RDwKZmUGcjAuR74XG4wWAPP> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Tic Disorders" ;
    dc:source <https://www.ssa.gov/disability/professionals/bluebook/12.00-MentalDisorders-Adult.htm#12_00B1> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RBU9zZzHpiivyY3EFmul3Ja> ;
    skos:definition "Tic Disorders involve the presence of repetitive, involuntary movements or vocalizations. They may include simple motor tics, such as blinking or head jerking, and complex tics, such as jumping or uttering words or phrases." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Motor and Vocal Tic Disorders" .

