    rdfs:subClassOf <R97svnIdQhrkKZw6i3Nn88z> ;
    skos:altLabel "Rent Control" ;
    skos:definition "A rent control claim typically involves a dispute or legal action related to rent control regulations imposed by local or state governments. These claims can arise when landlords or tenants believe that the rent control policies have been violated, whether through excessive rent increases, failure to provide required services, or other alleged breaches of rent control laws. The resolution of such claims often involves legal proceedings, where the rights and responsibilities of landlords and tenants are assessed in light of applicable rent control regulations." .

