<RuuXgrWsjANd7N8EBCrGeO> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Dietary Law Establishment Events" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <ROgocFufRBHZKkFfPDYyYh> ;
    skos:altLabel "Food Law Institution Events"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Dietary Law Establishment Events comprise the occasions when God instituted regulations governing what humans may consume, marking transitions in the covenant relationship between Creator and creation. These events include the original vegetarian diet in Eden, the post-flood permission to eat meat with restrictions, the Mosaic kosher laws, and Christ's declaration that all foods are clean."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Biblical scholars analyze dietary law establishment events to discern patterns in how God progressively reveals moral and ceremonial distinctions."^^xsd:string,
        "Catholic moral theology studies dietary law establishment events to understand how divine law adapts across different covenant dispensations."^^xsd:string,
        "Liturgical fasting practices trace their theological roots to dietary law establishment events throughout Scripture."^^xsd:string .

<RvITJ74ynBH2zCNG0vfksY> a owl:Class ;
