    rdfs:subClassOf <RBila9ckW95W84Tk54tGfZO> ;
    skos:altLabel "Job Training",
        "Vocational Training" ;
    skos:definition "\"Employment Training\" refers to the process of acquiring or enhancing the skills, knowledge, and competencies necessary for a specific job or career. It often involves formal or informal education, on-the-job training, workshops, or courses designed to prepare individuals for employment or improve their performance in a current job." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Workforce Development" .

<RvxWl1GyQyoCflTi4EtvXV> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Indian Commerce Clause Claim" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RwipRpN2mP7u4u1N74MVzK> ;
    skos:altLabel "Native American Commerce Clause Claim",
        "Anspruch auf die indische Handelsklausel"@de-de,
        "Indian Commerce Clause Claim"@en-gb,
        "Reclamo de la Cláusula de Comercio Indio"@es-es,
        "Reclamo de la Cláusula de Comercio Indio"@es-mx,
        "Réclamation de la clause de commerce indien"@fr-fr,
        "תביעת סעיף המסחר הודי"@he-il,
        "भारतीय वाणिज्य धारा दावा"@hi-in,
        "インド商業条項請求"@ja-jp,
        "Reivindicação da Cláusula de Comércio Indiano"@pt-br,
        "印度商务条款索赔"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "An Indian Commerce Clause claim is a legal argument asserting that a state law or regulation infringes upon the exclusive authority of the federal government to regulate commerce with Native American tribes. This claim is based on the interpretation that the Indian Commerce Clause grants Congress the power to regulate trade and commerce involving tribal nations, thereby limiting state interference in this sphere." .

