    skos:altLabel "A Cultural/Educational Exchange Visa is a non-immigrant visa issued to participants in programs that promote cultural exchange, primarily for studying, teaching, research, or training. In the United States, it's called a J-1 Visa, allowing the holder to stay temporarily in the host country, and they may be subject to a two-year home-country physical presence requirement upon completion of their program.",
        "Cultural Exchange Visa",
        "Cultural/Educational Exchange Visa",
        "Educational Exchange Visa",
        "J-1" .

<R0HJ4Pb6Bo9RmE3gbl7Wqh> a owl:Class ;
