    rdfs:subClassOf <RlZdd14uUrCvqa8YJ7RzNd> ;
    skos:definition "Non-Human Authorship in copyright law pertains to works created by entities other than human beings, such as artificial intelligence or animals. This concept challenges traditional copyright frameworks by raising questions about the eligibility for protection of works created without direct human intellectual input." .

