        "Departamento de Educação dos EUA"@pt-br,
        "美国教育部"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "The United States Department of Education (ED or DoED) is a Cabinet-level department of the United States government. The primary functions of the Department of Education are to \"establish policy for, administer and coordinate most federal assistance to education, collect data on US schools, and to enforce federal educational laws regarding privacy and civil rights.\"" ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "ED" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Department of Education" .

<R890rqgnX4R6holH0er0DWQ> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Place" ;
    skos:definition "Place is a locatable context — physical, institutional, or conceptual — where actions occur, authority is exercised, or activity is situated. It frames jurisdiction, applicability, and meaning for events, texts, and decisions."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "A diocesan tribunal."^^xsd:string,
        "A national legislature."^^xsd:string,
        "The Vatican City."^^xsd:string,
        "The global energy market."^^xsd:string .

<R8ASw8Dgh6TE62ku8oMci5u> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Incapacity Event" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RDETD6YVYGhLGZbM1fBnsfj> ],
        <R8lhhP1c4Hm9RruhEpWMrJW>,
        <RuDAbRiNW105SQoqb1XZ4c> ;
    skos:definition "An Incapacity Event refers to a situation where an individual becomes unable to make or communicate specific decisions, typically due to illness, injury, or cognitive decline. In such cases, legal instruments like durable powers of attorney or advance directives can guide decision-making on behalf of the incapacitated individual." .

<R8AUKvbXRK8jOHSQaqxcAtD> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Legal Determination" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RDnLOdTNWmEc4EhZ0SZXDm7> ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <R9pwejG33H0Y9mi74WzE2nb> ],
        <RBDhSx7fl9qS0ezDVJuZHX4> ;
    skos:definition "\"Litigation determination\" refers to the final outcome or verdict reached in a legal dispute or trial. It can include findings such as \"guilty\" in a criminal case or \"liable\" in a civil case when a party is held responsible, or \"acquitted\" when a defendant is found not guilty in a criminal trial. A single matter's legal determination can be split between claims (e.g., liable for one claim; not liable for another claim)." .

