        "Parables of Commitment"^^xsd:string,
        "Parables on Following Christ"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Parables of Discipleship means the parables taught by Jesus Christ that instruct followers on the demands, responsibilities, and cost of following him. Parables of Discipleship call hearers to vigilance, detachment, faithfulness, and concrete obedience."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Christian theology interprets the parables of discipleship as calls to radical commitment and trust in God."^^xsd:string,
        "Jesus teaches through parables that disciples must place loyalty to God above earthly wealth."^^xsd:string .

<RBvfJW4HbL3Y7Guu9ENS7w2> a owl:Class ;
