        "Woman Religious"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "A Female Religious is a woman who belongs to an institute of consecrated life and publicly professes the evangelical counsels according to the Church’s law. She lives a vowed life of prayer and apostolic service or contemplation within a recognized community."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "A female religious lives in community according to a rule or constitutions."^^xsd:string,
        "A female religious professes vows in a recognized institute."^^xsd:string,
        "The Church depends on female religious for prayer and apostolic service."^^xsd:string .

