    skos:altLabel "Tax Benefit" ;
    skos:definition "A Tax Incentive is a provision in tax law designed to encourage specific behaviors or activities by reducing a taxpayer's tax burden. It encompasses various mechanisms such as tax credits, deductions, exemptions, and preferential rates aimed at promoting certain economic or social objectives." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Tax Relief Mechanism" .

<RJoZMthwG4TT4ztkfGb9Hm> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Unreasonable Search and Seizure Claim" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R8GqVQ7wf48MBB7IuqjSfOk> ;
    skos:altLabel "Search and Seizure Claim",
        "Anspruch auf unangemessene Durchsuchung und Beschlagnahme"@de-de,
        "Unreasonable Search and Seizure Claim"@en-gb,
        "Reclamo de Búsqueda e Incautación Irrelevante"@es-es,
        "Reclamo de Búsqueda e Incautación Irrelevante"@es-mx,
        "Réclamation de recherche et saisie déraisonnable"@fr-fr,
        "תביעה על חיפוש ומעצר בלתי סביר"@he-il,
        "अनुचित तलाश और जब्ती का दावा"@hi-in,
        "違法な捜索および押収の主張"@ja-jp,
        "Reivindicação de busca e apreensão irrazoável"@pt-br,
        "不合理的搜查和扣押索赔"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "Unreasonable search and seizure refers to a violation of an individual's rights under the constitution, protecting individuals from unwarranted government intrusions into their privacy by requiring that searches and seizures conducted by law enforcement or government agents must be reasonable and, in most cases, based on probable cause supported by a warrant. An unreasonable search and seizure may occur when law enforcement officers or government agents conduct a search or seizure without a warrant, without probable cause, or when the scope of the search or seizure exceeds the limits of the warrant. Examples of unreasonable searches and seizures include warrantless searches of a person's home, an arrest without probable cause, or an overly invasive search of a person or their belongings." .

<RJwPJFKAy0EJgBB6jTyhhk> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Organizational Actor" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R8CdMpOM0RmyrgCCvbpiLS0>,
        <RDXLO9MacR7nBfLLV0hskma> ;
    skos:altLabel "Institutional Actor"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "An Organizational Actor is a structured, collective entity that acts, governs, regulates, or participates within ecclesial, civil, or institutional contexts. Such actors exercise authority, responsibility, or influence through defined roles, offices, or legal personality rather than as individual persons."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "A diocese governs pastoral life within a defined territory."^^xsd:string,
        "A state governmental body regulates education and healthcare."^^xsd:string,
        "Armed services operate as organizational actors with defined authority and structure."^^xsd:string,
        "The Holy See acts as a sovereign organizational actor in international law."^^xsd:string .

