            owl:someValuesFrom <R6406aeA21ddaECA8f6EEf9b> ],
        <R1F4dbe4CD17b3B2a7f15b97> ;
    skos:definition "Illinois State Courts are the judicial branches of the Illinois government responsible for interpreting and enforcing the law within the state's jurisdiction." ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "IL" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Illinois State Courts" .

<R788056HRwxGpba6Of0gGM> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Business Schools and Computer and Management Training Industry" ;
    dc:identifier "EDU-BSCH" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.naics.com/six-digit-naics/?code=6114> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RB7IaNyshrHiqug0LlmK6J2> ;
    skos:altLabel "Business Schools and Management Training",
        "Business Schools und Management-Trainingsbranche"@de-de,
        "Business Schools and Management Training Industry"@en-gb,
        "Escuelas de Negocios e Industria de Formación en Gestión"@es-es,
        "Escuelas de Negocios e Industria de Capacitación en Administración"@es-mx,
        "Écoles de commerce et industrie de la formation en management"@fr-fr,
        "בתי ספר לעסקים ותעשיית הדרכה בניהול"@he-il,
        "बिजनेस स्कूल और प्रबंधन प्रशिक्षण उद्योग"@hi-in,
        "ビジネススクールと経営トレーニング業界"@ja-jp,
        "Escolas de negócios e indústria de treinamento em gestão"@pt-br,
        "商学院和管理培训行业"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "This industry group comprises establishments primarily engaged in one of the following: (1) offering courses in office procedures and secretarial and stenographic skills and may offer courses in basic office skills, such as word processing; (2) conducting computer training (except computer repair); or (3) offering an array of short duration courses and seminars for management and professional development.  Instruction may be provided in diverse settings, such as the establishment's or client's training facilities, educational institutions, the workplace, or the home, and through diverse means, such as correspondence, television, the Internet, or other electronic and distance-learning methods.  The training provided by these establishments may include the use of simulators and simulation methods." ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "BSCH" .

<R7BZzP16LxkLJjYqRNwWXP> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Arts, Entertainment and Recreation Industry" ;
    dc:identifier "AER" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.naics.com/six-digit-naics/?code=71> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RCO5FBZfgN8P43sMsRpTesd> ],
        <RDIwFaFcH4KY0gwEY0QlMTp> ;
    skos:altLabel "Arts, Entertainment and Recreation",
        "Kunst-, Unterhaltungs- und Erholungsbranche"@de-de,
        "Arts, Entertainment and Recreation Industry"@en-gb,
        "Industria de las Artes, el Entretenimiento y el Ocio"@es-es,
        "Industria de las Artes, el Entretenimiento y el Ocio"@es-mx,
        "Industrie des arts, du divertissement et des loisirs"@fr-fr,
        "תעשיית האמנות, הבידור והפנאי"@he-il,
        "कला, मनोरंजन और मनोरंजन उद्योग"@hi-in,
        "芸術、エンターテインメント、レクリエーション産業"@ja-jp,
        "Indústria de Artes, Entretenimento e Recreação"@pt-br,
        "艺术、娱乐和休闲产业"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "The Arts, Entertainment and Recreation industry group includes a wide range of establishments that operate facilities or provide services to meet varied cultural, entertainment, and recreational interests of their patrons. This sector includes establishments that are involved in producing, promoting, or participating in live performances, events, or exhibits intended for public viewing, establishments that preserve and exhibit objects and sites of historical, cultural, or educational interest; and establishments that operate facilities or provide services that enable patrons to participate in recreational activities or pursue amusement, hobby, and leisure-time interests." ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "AER" .

<R7F7882E88c14CA0d4aAD629> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Nebraska State Courts" ;
    dc:identifier "USCTS-STCOUS-NE" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:locatedIn ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <R402e77499f953A56a0751ba> ],
        <R1F4dbe4CD17b3B2a7f15b97> ;
    skos:definition "Nebraska State Courts are the judicial branch of the Nebraska state government, responsible for interpreting and enforcing state laws and resolving legal disputes within the state." ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "NE" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Nebraska State Courts" .

<R7KYfSpf0bnFF3LV3RL3YU> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "National Labor Relations Act Claim" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RFBFa05A797a0E88e0a5F580> ],
        <Rfw7NfMHyrhfFQj8ob4M4U> ;
    skos:altLabel "NLRA Claim",
        "National Labour Relations Act Claim"@en-gb,
        "Reclamación de la Ley Nacional de Relaciones Laborales"@es-es,
        "Reclamación de la Ley Nacional de Relaciones Laborales"@es-mx,
        "תביעה על פי חוק הקשרי עבודה לאומי"@he-il,
        "राष्ट्रीय श्रम संबंधी अधिनियम दावा"@hi-in ;
    skos:definition "A National Labor Relations Act (NLRA) claim is a legal action initiated by an employee or group of employees against an employer, alleging that the employer has violated their rights under the NLRA, which is a federal law enacted in 1935 to protect employees' rights to engage in collective bargaining, join or form labor unions, and participate in other concerted activities related to their employment conditions. The NLRA also prohibits employers from interfering with these rights or retaliating against employees for exercising them. An NLRA claim may be filed with the National Labor Relations Board (NLRB), which investigates the allegations and can impose legal remedies, such as reinstatement, back pay, or policy changes, to ensure compliance with the law and the protection of employees' rights." .

<R7KxYUBMSAuzPHdBhWfPSv7> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Demographic Market Segments" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R8UG79BtYP2uqnKNklLYXB8> ;
    skos:definition "Demographic segments refer to divisions of the market that are categorized based on demographic characteristics such as age, gender, income, education level, and family status. These segments help marketers and businesses tailor their products and services to specific groups within the population, based on their unique needs and preferences." ;
    skos:note "Non-copyrightable idea and fact inspiration drawn from IAB 2.0. https://www.meaningcloud.com/developer/documentation/predefined/deep-categorization-models/iab-2-0" .

<R7NkMt6XJKd4fSolKqqOy5B> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "General Sales and Consumption Tax Payment" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R7f6bqEjMQDMYjlvg0WINGf> ;
    skos:altLabel "Comprehensive Sales Tax Payment",
        "General Taxes",
        "General Transaction Tax Payment" ;
    skos:definition "General Sales and Consumption Tax Payment includes all taxes, other than import and export duties, levied on the production, leasing, transfer, delivery, or sale of a wide range of goods and the rendering of a wide range of services. These taxes apply to both domestically produced and imported goods, irrespective of the stage of production or distribution at which they are levied. This category covers value-added taxes, sales taxes, and multi-stage cumulative taxes, including adjustments for border transactions." .

<R7OA1fGV1VIu5tK8bsCx3SE> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Mining Industry (except Oil and Gas)" ;
    dc:identifier "NRS-MING" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RDRa5lUoXHzZDEwMWp3VLh8> ],
        <ROWsW3Tkpc2YQmbHQehntm> ;
    skos:altLabel "Mining (except Oil and Gas)",
        "except Oil and Gas",
        "Bergbauindustrie (außer Öl und Gas)"@de-de,
        "Mining Industry (except Oil and Gas)"@en-gb,
        "Industria minera (excepto petróleo y gas)"@es-es,
        "Industria minera (excepto petróleo y gas)"@es-mx,
        "Industrie minière (sauf pétrole et gaz)"@fr-fr,
        "תעשיית הכריות (למעט נפט וגז)"@he-il,
        "खनन उद्योग (विशेष रूप से तेल और गैस के अलावा)"@hi-in,
        "鉱業（石油・ガスを除く）"@ja-jp,
        "Indústria de mineração (exceto petróleo e gás)"@pt-br,
        "采矿业（不包括石油和天然气）"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "Industries in this group primarily engage in mining, mine site development, and beneficiating (i.e., preparing) metallic minerals and nonmetallic minerals, including coal. The term 'mining' is used in the broad sense to include ore extraction, quarrying, and beneficiating (e.g., crushing, screening, washing, sizing, concentrating, and flotation), customarily done at the mine site." ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "MING" .

<R7OJQHant3Dx172WXuPbWgx> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Garnishment" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <ROjlFsq58MnIV2nxc0IvNu> ],
        <R7Mm9Zf0HlgIvCoXnWbJoMX>,
        <R9pQxz2fUIrk1LjvVP8hikg> ;
    skos:altLabel "Lohnpfändung"@de-de,
        "Attachment of Earnings"@en-gb,
        "Embargo de sueldo"@es-es,
        "Embargo de salario"@es-mx,
        "Saisie de salaire"@fr-fr,
        "מעצר שכר"@he-il,
        "गार्निशमेंट"@hi-in,
        "給与差し押え"@ja-jp,
        "Penhora de salário"@pt-br,
        "工资扣押"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A garnishment is a legal process where a creditor can collect a debt owed by a debtor by seizing a portion of their wages or assets, as authorized by a court order." .

<R7RS1hG7BxbLQktXIrO1Rro> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Applicant/Petitioner" ;
    dc:identifier "APPT" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RCEDL3kMYgjFUEOhOyGp3IE> ;
    skos:altLabel "Applicant",
        "Applicant/Petitioner",
        "Petitioner",
        "Antragsteller/Kläger"@de-de,
        "Applicant/Petitioner"@en-gb,
        "Solicitante/Peticionario"@es-es,
        "Solicitante/Peticionario"@es-mx,
        "Demandeur/Requérant"@fr-fr,
        "מבקש/תביעה"@he-il,
        "आवेदक/प्रार्थी"@hi-in,
        "申請人/原告"@ja-jp,
        "Requerente/Peticionário"@pt-br,
        "申请人/起诉人"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "An applicant or petitioner is a person who files a petition or makes an application or the person who is applying for a legal remedy to a problem." ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "APPT" .

<R7VtpAC807aOYLVtKmPvFRt> a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "folio:argued" ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf owl:topObjectProperty ;
    skos:altLabel "argued",
        "contended",
        "folio:pleaded",
        "pleaded" ;
    skos:definition "In a legal setting, \"argued\" refers to the presentation and advocacy of a legal position or interpretation before a court or tribunal. This process involves a structured discourse, utilizing facts, evidence, and legal principles to persuade the judge or jury of the validity of a party's stance or viewpoint on the matter at hand." ;
    skos:prefLabel "folio:contended" .

<R7XlRtk6WMnbMZULXcg7SnI> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Family Liability" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R9b5fs8QJuliSZYeaJLJU2t> ;
    skos:altLabel "Familienhaftung"@de-de,
        "Family Liability"@en-gb,
        "Responsabilidad familiar"@es-es,
        "Responsabilidad familiar"@es-mx,
        "Responsabilité familiale"@fr-fr,
        "אחריות משפחתית"@he-il,
        "परिवार की ज़िम्मेदारी"@hi-in,
        "家族責任"@ja-jp,
        "Responsabilidade familiar"@pt-br,
        "家庭责任"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "Family Liability refers to the legal responsibility of family members for the actions or debts of other family members, including spousal and parent-child liability, as well as agency and vicarious liability." .

<R7aFBns3Z2d9MuNI5sDEGxF> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Deportation" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R0tJKDoGSixec7FgGKnAAl>,
        <R73Uo5x4VyfiOXt6i4R256t>,
        <RBEXxc9B6kR2p0BMwGjhWGW>,
        <RDbz1PVc6y57oOb9jAIl0eN> ;
    skos:altLabel "Abschiebung"@de-de,
        "Deportation"@en-gb,
        "Deportación"@es-es,
        "Deportación"@es-mx,
        "Déportation"@fr-fr,
        "גירושין"@he-il,
        "निर्वासन"@hi-in,
        "強制送還"@ja-jp,
        "Deportação"@pt-br,
        "驱逐"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "The forced removal of a person from a country by the government as a consequence of violating immigration laws or committing a crime." .

<R7c5BcqV4pI9L9rPupIV17C> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Wildlife Crimes" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R7V9R3w28BDjOd4lLUUrvQ5> ;
    skos:definition "Wildlife Crimes involve illegal activities that harm wildlife species, including poaching, trafficking, and illegal trade. These crimes violate national and international laws aimed at protecting endangered and protected species." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Wildlife Offenses" .

<R7dcZJLuYutSG7vbZRwstAC> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "California Family Rights Act Claim" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RCmAarh6Wj8m6lLe6lJJBmj> ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RCidddiy9X9fqxmBCyYguuE> ],
        <R9LVBKjvGRuzwgtlhuLST36>,
        <R9UYGSnWQz2MvNsWUofGb6J>,
        <RCty0MaQzrLC9KnzjM7nMER> ;
    skos:altLabel "CFRA Claim",
        "Anspruch nach dem kalifornischen Familienrechtsakt"@de-de,
        "California Family Rights Act Claim"@en-gb,
        "Reclamo de la Ley de Derechos Familiares de California"@es-es,
        "Reclamo de la Ley de Derechos Familiares de California"@es-mx,
        "Réclamation en vertu de la loi californienne sur les droits de la famille"@fr-fr,
        "תביעה על פי חוק זכויות המשפחה של קליפורניה"@he-il,
        "कैलिफोर्निया परिवार अधिकार अधिनियम दावा"@hi-in,
        "カリフォルニア家族権利法クレーム"@ja-jp,
        "Reivindicação da Lei de Direitos da Família da Califórnia"@pt-br,
        "加利福尼亚家庭权利法索赔"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A California Family Rights Act (CFRA) claim is a legal action initiated by an employee against their employer for not complying with the CFRA, which provides eligible employees with up to 12 weeks of unpaid leave in a 12-month period for certain family or medical reasons, such as the birth or adoption of a child, the employee's own serious health condition, or to care for a seriously ill family member. The claim typically arises when an employer denies an employee's request for CFRA leave or interferes with an employee's right to take CFRA leave, or retaliates against an employee for exercising their right to CFRA leave. Employers can face liability for violating the CFRA, which can result in significant damages for the affected employee." .

<R7eNtj44HIHIEfl5hdN415d> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Limited Liability Partnership" ;
    dc:identifier "ENTITY-LLP" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RC3I2GwWuuKWmRJVXgxXeb> ;
    skos:altLabel "Gesellschaft mit beschränkter Haftung"@de-de,
        "Société à responsabilité limitée"@fr-fr,
        "有限責任事業組合"@ja-jp,
        "Sociedade de Responsabilidade Limitada"@pt-br,
        "有限责任合伙企业"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A limited liability partnership (LLP) is a partnership in which some or all partners (depending on the jurisdiction) have limited liabilities. It therefore can exhibit elements of partnerships and corporations. In a LLP, each partner is not responsible or liable for another partner's misconduct or negligence." ;
    skos:prefLabel "LLP" .

<R7eVYpVEsDqKqMUL2HL23Zr> a owl:Class ;
