        "Identificadores de sistema"@pt-br,
        "系统标识符"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "Unique identifiers (e.g., IRIs, UUIDs, GUIDs) within the systems of stakeholders (e.g., vendors, sellers, buyers, courts)." .

<R8G6kTX09ac1e8BHuaPSHc3> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Conflict" ;
    rdfs:comment "In a global Catholic ontology, Conflict represents a disruption of the tranquility of order, requiring an ethical response to restore justice. The Church views these events not merely as sociological phenomena but as moral trials that demand the application of charity and the pursuit of peace."^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R73hoH1RXYjBTYiGfolpsAF> ;
    skos:altLabel "Discord"^^xsd:string,
        "Strife"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Conflict is a manifestation of discord between persons, groups, or nations arising from a perceived or actual opposition of interests, rights, or beliefs. It serves as the situational context where the principles of justice and reconciliation must be applied to restore the common good."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Convening a theological council to address doctrinal disagreements within the ecclesial community."^^xsd:string,
        "Engaging in diplomatic negotiations to resolve a territorial disagreement between neighboring nations."^^xsd:string,
        "Mediating a labor dispute to ensure the fair treatment of workers and the viability of the enterprise."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel "Dispute"^^xsd:string .

<R8Gt68Hspze0zsEdYzUS2Fq> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Contingent Financial Obligations" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R9ce0e5pb4hAULGEtqlBCV8> ;
    skos:definition "Contingent Financial Obligations, or Contingent Liabilities, are potential debts that may or may not become actual liabilities, depending on the outcome of a future event. These are not recorded on the balance sheet but may be disclosed in the financial statements' notes if the contingency is considered significant, such as pending lawsuits or financial guarantees." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Contingent Liability" .

<R8IG2xzz6DkWBumc1ZiMyx9> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Sacraments of Initiation" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RB91Ir5bSOsoHyaGccORDpQ> ;
    skos:altLabel "Initiatory Sacraments"^^xsd:string,
        "Sacraments of Christian Initiation"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Sacraments of Initiation are the sacraments by which a person is incorporated into Christ and the Church and receives the fullness of sacramental life. They establish the foundations of Christian existence through rebirth, strengthening, and Eucharistic communion."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Adults ordinarily receive the sacraments of initiation together."^^xsd:string,
        "The sacraments of initiation incorporate a person fully into the Church."^^xsd:string .

<R8KVC7hiMeeT0z2FQauanXT> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Exodus Events" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R9o7849l09skEBQqbxSItaV> .

<R8L6V5AA4I5wcDrZtJjGLRb> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Personal Authority Level" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <http://webprotege.stanford.edu/RBTE2mUxX4WZjAu5EkKF4MA> ;
    skos:definition "Personal Authority Level is a classification that indicates the degree of influence or weight a person’s guidance, judgment, or direction carries in a relational context. It reflects the nature of the relationship and the extent to which reliance, trust, or deference is reasonably expected."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "A friend offers advice on a personal decision."^^xsd:string,
        "A manager advises their employee about the best ethical decision."^^xsd:string,
        "A parent instructs a child on acceptable behavior."^^xsd:string,
        "A trusted mentor advises a student on vocational choices."^^xsd:string,
        "Colleagues rely on a peer’s judgment in a shared project."^^xsd:string .

<R8M0UJWeEVpeK5gMPLTQSl2> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Estate Planning Objectives" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RCDwLiS22z6MzQaQHS08hvk> ;
    skos:definition "Estate Planning Objectives refer to the goals and purposes that individuals aim to achieve when organizing their assets, properties, and financial affairs for the future distribution upon their death. These objectives ensure the proper management and transfer of wealth, fulfillment of personal wishes, and minimization of taxes and legal complications." .

<R8MlNUtcvkICqPmpS1Sm1QD> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Trauma- and Stressor-Related Disorders" ;
    dc:source <https://www.ssa.gov/disability/professionals/bluebook/12.00-MentalDisorders-Adult.htm#12_00B1>,
        <https://www.ssa.gov/disability/professionals/bluebook/12.00-MentalDisorders-Adult.htm#12_15> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RN3TubQIlusDFnPgrNAk8D> ;
    skos:definition "Trauma- and Stressor-Related Disorders are characterized by experiencing or witnessing a traumatic or stressful event, or learning of a traumatic event occurring to a close family member or close friend, and the psychological aftermath of clinically significant effects on functioning. Symptoms and signs may include, but are not limited to, distressing memories, dreams, and flashbacks related to the trauma or stressor; avoidant behavior; diminished interest or participation in significant activities; persistent negative emotional states (for example, fear, anger) or persistent inability to experience positive emotions (for example, satisfaction, affection); anxiety; irritability; aggression; exaggerated startle response; difficulty concentrating; and sleep disturbance." .

<R8N2AJIJYBB3hzZL7OeB0CB> a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "oasis:hasCollection" ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf owl:topObjectProperty .

