<R783351768f732C2badC6a0e> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "U.S. Dept. of Housing and Urban Development" ;
    dc:identifier "US-FD-HUD" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R22815eC3Af3bFF0d002Ca58> ;
    skos:altLabel "US-amerikanisches Ministerium für Wohnungsbau und Stadtentwicklung"@de-de,
        "U.S. Dept. of Housing and Urban Development"@en-gb,
        "Departamento de Vivienda y Desarrollo Urbano de EE. UU."@es-es,
        "Departamento de Vivienda y Desarrollo Urbano de EE. UU."@es-mx,
        "Département du logement et du développement urbain des États-Unis"@fr-fr,
        "משרד המגורים ופיתוח העירוני של ארצות הברית"@he-il,
        "यूएस आवास और शहरी विकास विभाग"@hi-in,
        "米国住宅都市開発省"@ja-jp,
        "Departamento de Habitação e Desenvolvimento Urbano dos EUA"@pt-br,
        "美国住房和城市发展部"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "The United States Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD) is a Cabinet department in the Executive branch of the United States federal government. HUD's mission is to create strong, sustainable, inclusive communities and quality affordable homes for all. HUD is working to strengthen the housing market to bolster the economy and protect consumers; meet the need for quality affordable rental homes; utilize housing as a platform for improving quality of life; build inclusive and sustainable communities free from discrimination, and transform the way HUD does business." ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "HUD" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Department of Housing and Urban Development" .

<R78app5YW8khDGWTy53LbZ4> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Religious House" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R8t0srL2xeL3TDoobUUFnvC> ;
    skos:altLabel "Consecrated Community House"^^xsd:string,
        "House of Religious Life"^^xsd:string,
        "Religious Community House"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Religious House is a sacred place where members of a religious institute live in common according to an approved rule or constitutions. A Religious House is ordered toward prayer, community life, and the apostolic or contemplative mission proper to the institute."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "A convent serves as a religious house for a community of consecrated women."^^xsd:string,
        "A friary houses members of a mendicant religious order in common life."^^xsd:string,
        "A monastery functions as a religious house dedicated primarily to contemplative life."^^xsd:string,
        "A seminary operates as a religious house focused on formation for ordained ministry."^^xsd:string .

<R79CBFMSwUZjwKG9qV6AfQb> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "War" ;
    rdfs:comment "In a global Catholic ontology, War is the most extreme form of conflict, characterized by a state of organized, lethal hostility. The Church views it as a \"scourge\" that always represents a defeat for humanity, yet she maintains a rigorous ethical framework to judge its necessity and conduct when all peaceful means fail."^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R9mTGKaFostHJfLRPz7vsst>,
        <RDFhtJuTWcY7UZGV9F5yOoA> ;
    skos:altLabel "Bellum"^^xsd:string,
        "Military Engagement" ;
    skos:definition "War is a state of active, prolonged armed conflict between sovereign states or large organized groups. It necessitates the strict application of moral criteria to determine if the initiation of force is permissible and if the conduct during the struggle remains within the bounds of justice."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Declaring a formal state of hostilities following a direct violation of national sovereignty."^^xsd:string,
        "Engaging in a prolonged campaign to liberate a territory from an unjust occupying power."^^xsd:string,
        "Mobilizing national resources and personnel for the purpose of a multi-year military engagement."^^xsd:string .

