<R7MmeHfXj4xIERqXjFOEHHw> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "National Governmental Body" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RBQGborh1CfXanGZipDL0Qo> ;
    skos:definition "A national governmental body refers to an organization or institution at the highest level of governance in a country, responsible for making, executing, or interpreting laws and regulations. These bodies often include the executive branch (headed by presidents or prime ministers), legislative branches (such as parliaments or congresses), and judicial branches (like supreme or constitutional courts). Their functions and structures vary depending on the specific form and constitution of each nation's government." .

<R7NuHbXZluNRzq9D1bLM716> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Agreement Attributes" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RBJ4HPUl2DrL4G30lmoFKJN> ;
    skos:altLabel "Agreement Characteristics",
        "Contractual Attributes" ;
    skos:definition "Agreement Attributes refer to the characteristics and forms in which agreements can exist, defining how they are communicated and understood between parties (e.g., whether the is agreement is oral or written). These attributes determine the enforceability and clarity of the agreements within legal contexts." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Contract Attributes" .

<R7O9EXc5CO83M0CzT8VzNFT> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Unarmed Conflict" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R8G6kTX09ac1e8BHuaPSHc3> ;
    skos:altLabel "Social Conflict"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Unarmed Conflict means sustained opposition between persons, groups, or institutions that seeks to compel, resist, or control through non-lethal means rather than organized armed force. Unarmed Conflict can still impose grave moral harms — coercion, injustice, scandal, social fracture — and can demand obligations of truth, charity, justice, and peacebuilding."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "A Catholic employer and a workers’ union managed a strike by maintaining dialogue and protecting human dignity."^^xsd:string,
        "A bishops’ conference helped de-escalate an unarmed conflict between rival political parties after disputed election results."^^xsd:string,
        "A parish council addressed a conflict over liturgical music by convening listening sessions and adopting a shared plan."^^xsd:string,
        "A theologian’s published critique sparked conflict within a seminary faculty that required clarification by competent authority."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel "Nonviolent Conflict"^^xsd:string .

<R7QF58SulRGe1zlQ8gCzVSF> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Cardinal Virtues" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <Rgp2p1OFbXqI1lBJieonvK> ;
    skos:altLabel "Foundational Virtues"^^xsd:string,
        "Principal Virtues"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Cardinal Virtues are fundamental virtues that order human action according to right reason and serve as the foundation for a virtuous moral life. Cardinal Virtues shape moral character by directing intellect, will, and passions toward the good."^^xsd:string .

<R7WKt0VAzs1NaH3XvbaWYIZ> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Disorders of Bone Marrow Failure" ;
    dc:source <https://www.ssa.gov/disability/professionals/bluebook/7.00-HematologicalDisorders-Adult.htm#7_10> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R7O2ClQ73HLZZLgFgtNbVTF> ;
    skos:definition "Bone Marrow Dysfunction",
        "Disorders of bone marrow failure refer to a range of conditions where the bone marrow does not produce sufficient blood cells, including red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets. These disorders can lead to anemia, increased susceptibility to infections, and bleeding problems due to the inadequate production of these critical blood components." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Hematopoietic Failure" .

<R7Zwd84vqcynsz8PsQJt7xj> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Entertainment Visa" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RD1oQDMlC6FytjOndhJTMy8> ;
    skos:altLabel "Entertainer Visa",
        "P-1B Visa" ;
    skos:definition "The Entertainment Visa (in the U.S., P-1B Visa), is designed for members of internationally recognized entertainment groups that wish to perform in the destination country (e.g., U.S.). In the United States, this non-immigrant visa allows the entertainers to stay for the duration of the event, competition, or performance, with an initial period of up to one year, which can be extended in increments of up to one year for continued performances or events" .

<R7f8oRno6qr0y6rzgnqVgK0> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Eviction (Event)" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <Rur2GcVfhwGRdEjyt84rMc> ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <R89e7t0wDXgx7mBu9rn271g> ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <R8mhyaytzU3aWKoT5W7nlls> ],
        <RCvV18Mbbb9FYFXbHt1inuL> ;
    skos:definition "Eviction is a legal process by which a landlord forces a tenant to leave a rented property, typically due to nonpayment of rent, lease violations, or other breaches of the rental agreement. The process involves court proceedings, notice requirements, and, if ordered by the court, law enforcement intervention to remove the tenant from the property." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Eviction" .

<R7hUqSzjreR3vfFZVZniVs4> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Mosaic Covenant Events" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R7hvAdBWgqXF4EHGunMyE3W> ;
    skos:definition "Mosaic Covenant Events encompass the pivotal occasions when God established the covenant with Israel through Moses at Mount Sinai, giving the Law and forming Israel into a holy nation and priestly kingdom. These events include the revelation of Torah, covenant ratification ceremonies, the golden calf apostasy, covenant renewal, and the establishment of sacrificial worship systems that defined Israelite identity for centuries."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Catechists in the early Church used Mosaic Covenant events to explain how Christ fulfilled rather than abolished the Law."^^xsd:string,
        "Medieval theologians contrasted Mosaic Covenant events with the New Covenant to distinguish law from grace in salvation history."^^xsd:string,
        "Reformation scholars debated how Mosaic Covenant events related to justification by faith versus works of law."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:note """Decalogue Proclamation (Exodus 20)
Covenant Ratification Ceremony (Exodus 24)
Tabernacle Construction Instructions (Exodus 25-31)
Covenant Tablets Breaking and Rewriting (Exodus 32-34)
Levitical Priesthood Institution (Leviticus 8-9)
Day of Atonement Establishment (Leviticus 16)
Moab Plains Covenant Renewal (Deuteronomy 29-30)
Blessings and Curses Ceremony (Deuteronomy 27-28)"""^^xsd:string .

<R7hvAdBWgqXF4EHGunMyE3W> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Covenant Events" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R9o7849l09skEBQqbxSItaV> ;
    skos:altLabel "Covenantal Occasions"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Covenant Events encompass the pivotal moments in salvation history when God established or renewed formal agreements with humanity, defining the relationship between the divine and God's people. These events mark transformative occasions where God initiated binding commitments, often accompanied by signs, promises, and obligations that shaped the faith community's identity and mission."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Catholic theology teaches that covenant events demonstrate God's faithful initiative in establishing permanent relationships with humanity."^^xsd:string,
        "Covenant events mark the progressive stages through which God revealed the divine plan for humanity's redemption."^^xsd:string,
        "The Catholic Church recognizes multiple covenant events throughout salvation history, each building upon previous divine-human agreements."^^xsd:string .

<R7kD4ePZmjNDaw2a1pWIDds> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Transaction Negotiation Dynamics" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R70jMZb6xYrVCXW6f3EbO1e> ;
    skos:altLabel "Transactional Bargaining Dynamics" ;
    skos:definition "Transaction negotiation dynamics refer to the processes and interactions involved in negotiating the terms and conditions of a business transaction between parties. These dynamics encompass various strategies, styles, and behaviors that influence the negotiation's outcome, including the degree of cooperation, conflict, and communication between the parties involved." .

<R7n6xn6CbnvekygNrB5DsJM> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Consumer Contract Claims" ;
