        "Reclamaciones de Contratos de Consumo"@es-es,
        "Reclamaciones de Contratos de Consumo"@es-mx,
        "Réclamations de contrat de consommation"@fr-fr,
        "תביעות חוזיות לצרכן"@he-il,
        "उपभोक्ता अनुबंध दावे"@hi-in,
        "消費者契約請求"@ja-jp,
        "Reivindicações de contrato do consumidor"@pt-br,
        "消费者合同索赔"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "Consumer Contract Claims are legal claims made by a party in a contract with a consumer, including claims related to billing errors, unlawful provisions, unconscionable circumstances, and improper actions by loan brokers." .

<R7qVMTAfVUMCpr6LhRZ23eF> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Combatant" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <R9mTGKaFostHJfLRPz7vsst> ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <R8Q29bAm8uBwUw5NEpxF7MR> ],
        <RCEDL3kMYgjFUEOhOyGp3IE> ;
    skos:altLabel "Armed Fighter"^^xsd:string,
        "Belligerent"^^xsd:string,
        "Fighter"^^xsd:string,
        "Participant in Hostilities"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "A combatant is a person who takes a direct part in armed hostilities on behalf of a party to an armed conflict. A combatant’s status affects lawful targeting, detention, and — where recognized — combatant immunity for lawful acts of war."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "A guerrilla fighter carried arms openly during an attack and claimed combatant privileges under applicable conflict rules."^^xsd:string,
        "A militia member who met command, distinction, and compliance requirements received combatant status for the conflict’s duration."^^xsd:string,
        "A uniformed infantry member engaged in hostilities qualified as a combatant under the law of armed conflict."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel "Enemy Combatant"^^xsd:string .

<R7sBKqCcmlK1Dw9HBvKenYy> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Operative Dates" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RDSepz944v79Sc4zhy0qy2X> ;
    skos:definition "Operative Dates include various time points that are significant in legal and regulatory contexts. These include the effective date, when a law or regulation becomes active; the expiration date, when a document or status ceases to be valid; and the issuance date, when an official document is provided." .

<R7vlavFi9wyzEzNgp9zjkE> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Visas for Support Staff" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RD1oQDMlC6FytjOndhJTMy8> ;
    skos:altLabel "Visas for support staff often refer to non-immigrant visas that allow individuals to accompany and assist principal visa holders in the United States. For example, O-2 visas are issued to individuals who will accompany O-1 visa holders to assist in their performances or events. These visas are generally tied to the duration and conditions of the principal visa holder's status." .

<R7xrNuVBQ2B3sD1PzbweIcr> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Written Asynchronous Communication" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R8qItBwG2pRMFhUq1HQEMnb> ;
    skos:altLabel "Asynchrone schriftliche Kommunikation"@de-de,
        "Written Asynchronous Communication"@en-gb,
        "Comunicación Asincrónica Escrita"@es-es,
        "Comunicación Asincrónica Escrita"@es-mx,
        "Communication écrite asynchrone"@fr-fr,
        "תקשורת אסינכרונית כתובה"@he-il,
        "लिखित असिंक्रोनस कम्यूनिकेशन"@hi-in,
        "書面による非同期コミュニケーション"@ja-jp,
        "Comunicação escrita assíncrona"@pt-br,
        "书面异步通信"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A communication that occurs in writing and does not require that the users be synchronous (communicating at the same time)." .

<R7yue2mtjzJWKBkXpq5y1Mm> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Negligently Providing Alcohol" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RCfunX4u69LUQ3gbhckE0oI> ;
    skos:altLabel "Fahrlässige Alkoholabgabe"@de-de,
        "Negligently Providing Alcohol"@en-gb,
        "Suministro negligente de alcohol"@es-es,
        "Suministro negligente de alcohol"@es-mx,
        "Fourniture négligente d'alcool"@fr-fr,
        "ספקת אלכוהול באופן שגוי או באופן שלא ישיג את הסטנדרטים הנדרשים"@he-il,
        "लापरवाही से शराब प्रदान करना"@hi-in,
        "過失によるアルコール提供"@ja-jp,
        "Fornecimento negligente de álcool"@pt-br,
        "过失提供酒精"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "The concept of Negligently Providing Alcohol refers to the legal claim that holds a person responsible for providing alcohol to someone who is not legally allowed to consume it or who is already intoxicated, resulting in harm or injury to that person or others." .

<R7z8IPBHMwVOHP53OFYeSZN> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Urinary and Reproductive System Disorders" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RD12xMI38C0qkkx19ISgWWD> ;
    skos:altLabel "Renal and Reproductive Disorders",
        "Urogenital Disorders" ;
    skos:definition "Genitourinary disorders encompass a range of conditions affecting the organs of the reproductive and urinary systems, including the kidneys, bladder, ureters, urethra, and reproductive organs. These disorders can be congenital or acquired and may involve functional impairment, structural abnormalities, or systemic diseases impacting the genitourinary system." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Genitourinary Disorders" .

<R82Yb8u8L6F9E8vrZFOnfw1> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Funds, Trusts, and Other Financial Vehicles Industry" ;
    dc:identifier "FNS-FUND" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.naics.com/six-digit-naics/?code=525> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RCksXAlY9lRN16wERqZZ8Tk> ;
    skos:altLabel "Funds and Trusts",
        "Fonds- und Treuhandbranche"@de-de,
        "Funds and Trusts Industry"@en-gb,
        "Industria de Fondos y Fideicomisos"@es-es,
        "Industria de Fondos y Fideicomisos"@es-mx,
        "Industrie des fonds et des fiducies"@fr-fr,
        "תעשיית קרנות ואמנויות"@he-il,
        "फंड और ट्रस्ट उद्योग"@hi-in,
        "ファンド・信託業界"@ja-jp,
        "Indústria de fundos e trusts"@pt-br,
        "基金和信托业"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition """Industries in the Funds, Trusts, and Other Financial Vehicles subsector group legal entities (i.e., funds, plans, and/or programs) organized to pool securities or other assets on behalf of shareholders or beneficiaries of employee benefit or other trust funds.  The portfolios are customized to achieve specific investment characteristics, such as diversification, risk, rate of return, and price volatility.  These entities earn interest, dividends, and other investment income, but have little or no employment and no revenue from the sale of services.  Establishments with employees devoted to the management of funds are classified in Industry Group 5239, Other Financial Investment Activities.

Establishments primarily engaged in holding the securities of (or other equity interests in) other firms are classified in Sector 55, Management of Companies and Enterprises.  Equity real estate investment trusts (REITs) that are primarily engaged in leasing buildings, dwellings, or other real estate property to others are classified in Subsector 531, Real Estate.""" ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "FUND" .

<R83VhHEeaRnvGWxfksxJUSc> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Electrical Equipment, Appliance, and Component Manufacturing" ;
    dc:identifier "TEC-EEQP" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.naics.com/six-digit-naics/?code=335> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R9L2shTy2cnDMS1sImF2PBy> ;
    skos:altLabel "Electrical Equipment and Components",
        "Elektrogeräte- und Komponentenindustrie"@de-de,
        "Electrical Equipment and Component Industry"@en-gb,
        "Industria de Equipos y Componentes Eléctricos"@es-es,
        "Industria de Equipos y Componentes Eléctricos"@es-mx,
        "Industrie des équipements et composants électriques"@fr-fr,
        "תעשיית ציוד ורכיבי חשמל"@he-il,
        "विद्युत उपकरण और घटक उद्योग"@hi-in,
        "電気機器・部品産業"@ja-jp,
        "Indústria de equipamentos e componentes elétricos"@pt-br,
        "电气设备和元器件行业"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "Industries in the Electrical Equipment, Appliance, and Component Manufacturing subsector manufacture products that generate, distribute, and use electrical power.  Electric Lighting Equipment Manufacturing establishments produce lighting fixtures, electric light bulbs, and parts (except glass parts and light emitting diodes (LEDs)), and other lighting equipment.  Household Appliance Manufacturing establishments make both small and major electrical appliances and parts.  Electrical Equipment Manufacturing establishments make goods, such as electric motors, generators, transformers, and switchgear apparatus.  Other Electrical Equipment and Component Manufacturing establishments make devices for storing electrical power (e.g., batteries), for transmitting electricity (e.g., insulated wire), and wiring devices (e.g., electrical outlets, fuse boxes, and light switches)." ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "EEQP" .

<R8428LJEfCIiJBkESQPpEhQ> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Obligor" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RClFNLrDawcQ4HuRbzm6JJI> ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RDtFkLR3v97fran5zQ3ugao> ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <R8VN5tK4TtD0GqDw2NCbaLr> ],
        <RCEDL3kMYgjFUEOhOyGp3IE> ;
    skos:altLabel "Grantor",
        "Promisor" ;
    skos:definition "An obligor is a person, organization, or entity that is legally bound to perform a specific duty or pay a certain amount to another party, known as the obligee. The term is commonly used in contract law, finance, and other legal contexts to identify the party with the obligation to fulfill the terms of a contract, loan, or other legal arrangement." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Covenantor" .

<R8A3IWnCF4w7p6lvVLLqAQa> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Education Liability" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RBREngQZS9QIgeWCOMPBLIo> ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RC6b9qx6IeaqNoLfaLBJCwU> ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RB7IaNyshrHiqug0LlmK6J2> ],
        <R8jYAnNATrfoBxAtIKpf72X> ;
    skos:altLabel "Haftung im Bildungsbereich"@de-de,
        "Education Liability"@en-gb,
        "Responsabilidad educativa"@es-es,
        "Responsabilidad educativa"@es-mx,
        "Responsabilité en matière d'éducation"@fr-fr,
        "אחריות חינוך"@he-il,
        "शिक्षा दायित्व"@hi-in,
        "教育責任"@ja-jp,
        "Responsabilidade educacional"@pt-br,
        "教育责任"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "Education Liability refers to the legal responsibility and accountability of educational institutions and their staff for any harm or injury caused to students or their families, including civil claims related to privacy of school records, corporal punishment, compulsory education, and prayer in public school." .

<R8DxS7r88L9RGxTlMebfGWw> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Non-Profit Organization" ;
    dc:identifier "ENTITY-NPO" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R7oBWHStfmqTLn2MypkW3Pj> ;
    skos:altLabel "Charity Organization",
        "Non-Business Entity",
        "Non-Profit Organization",
        "Nonprofit Organization",
        "Not-for-Profit Organization",
        "Non-Profit-Organisation"@de-de,
        "Organisation à but non lucratif"@fr-fr,
        "非営利団体"@ja-jp,
        "Organização sem fins lucrativos"@pt-br,
        "非营利组织"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "A non-profit organization (NPO) is dedicated to furthering a particular social cause or advocating for a shared point of view. In economic terms, it is an organization that uses its surplus of the revenues to further achieve its ultimate objective, rather than distributing its income to the organization's shareholders, leaders, or members. Non-profits are tax-exempt or charitable, meaning they do not pay income tax on the money that they receive for their organization." ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "NPO" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Nonprofit Institution" .

<R8E26e2B7Aa687AFe167203f> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Comoros" ;
    dc:identifier "AFR-KM" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R712935EF6d6a33B83e501b7> ;
    skos:altLabel "the" ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "KM" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Comoros" .

<R8LCVHYfxA8Lri3uDg3TTsF> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Legal Concepts" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RDQC6BrYjcS3V0gZcYzqc8O> ;
    skos:altLabel "Concepts of Law"^^xsd:string,
        "Juridical Concepts"^^xsd:string,
        "Legal Notions"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Legal Concepts are structured ideas that express how law defines, regulates, and orders rights, duties, powers, and institutions within a legal system. Legal Concepts provide the conceptual framework through which legal norms are created, interpreted, applied, and enforced."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Legal concepts enable comparison across legal systems, jurisdictions, theologies, and ideologies."^^xsd:string .

<R8MAmklNCHWQOvWpLPS5K9G> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Computer Systems Design and Related Services Industry" ;
    dc:identifier "PRS-CPSW" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.naics.com/six-digit-naics/?code=5415> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RBFLYkta0F7DwegW1FnUX52> ;
    skos:altLabel "Computer and Software Services",
        "Computer- und Software-Dienstleistungsbranche"@de-de,
        "Computer and Software Services Industry"@en-gb,
        "Industria de Servicios de Computación y Software"@es-es,
        "Industria de Servicios de Computación y Software"@es-mx,
        "Industrie des services informatiques et logiciels"@fr-fr,
        "תעשיית שירותי מחשוב ותוכנה"@he-il,
        "कंप्यूटर और सॉफ्टवेयर सेवा उद्योग"@hi-in,
        "コンピュータおよびソフトウェアサービス産業"@ja-jp,
        "Indústria de Serviços de Computação e Software"@pt-br,
        "计算机和软件服务行业"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "This sector comprises establishments primarily engaged in activities in which human capital is the major input. These establishments make available the knowledge and skills of their employees, often on an assignment basis. The individual industries of this sector are defined on the basis of the particular expertise and training of the service provider." ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "CPSW" .

<R8TmxqBbWaNgdm0lJQdY6D4> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Pension and Benefits Claims" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <R7gFwngdoBeiYXxslm69WNk> ],
        <RCty0MaQzrLC9KnzjM7nMER> ;
    skos:altLabel "Benefits Claims",
        "Renten- und Leistungsansprüche"@de-de,
        "Pension and Benefits Claims"@en-gb,
        "Reclamaciones de pensiones y beneficios"@es-es,
        "Reclamaciones de pensiones y prestaciones"@es-mx,
        "Réclamations de pensions et d'avantages sociaux"@fr-fr,
        "תביעות פנסיה וטבעות"@he-il,
        "पेंशन और लाभ दावे"@hi-in,
        "年金および給付請求"@ja-jp,
        "Reivindicações de pensão e benefícios"@pt-br,
        "养老金和福利索赔"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "Pension and benefits claims are legal actions initiated by an employee against their employer for not complying with applicable laws or the terms of an employment agreement regarding retirement and other benefits. These claims can involve issues such as the mismanagement or mishandling of employee pension or retirement accounts, denial or reduction of employee benefits, or failure to provide required benefits such as health insurance or disability coverage. Employees may also bring pension and benefits claims if their employer retaliates against them for asserting their rights to these benefits." .

<R8UG79BtYP2uqnKNklLYXB8> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Market Segment Attributes" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RjM80CC0FA0G2sKxmlbaJF> ],
        <R8f4qGdjxuiQary8OBpq8W9> ;
    skos:altLabel "Market Characteristics" ;
    skos:definition "Market Attributes refer to the features and qualities of a market that are shaped by consumer preferences and demand. These characteristics can include the types of products and services sought by consumers. These can include consumers' preferences for luxury or commodity goods, their interest in specific industry sectors such as technology or finance, their preference for regional or national businesses, and similar demand-side attributes." ;
    skos:note "Non-copyrightable idea and fact inspiration drawn from IAB 2.0. https://www.meaningcloud.com/developer/documentation/predefined/deep-categorization-models/iab-2-0",
        "These are the attributes of the Buyer (Demand Side) that may or may not relate to the Industry of the Seller (Supply Side). This classification fills the gaps that the NAICS supply-side industry does not, including Demographic markets (e.g., luxury goods and services, children's goods and services), Geographic markets (e.g., Local, Regional, National, International), and Interest markets (e.g., Tech markets like FinTech, BioTech, LegalTech; Organic Products Market, Fitness and Exercise Market, Dating Market, Wedding Market)" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Demand-Side Industry Attributes" .

<R8WhsyEOse5TvMLfnHDYfTY> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Stone Fruits" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RDx4PuWu7ZznwNEGW6rXll0> ;
    skos:altLabel "Drupes",
        "Hard Stone Fruits",
        "Pitted Fruits" ;
    skos:definition "Stone fruits, also known as drupes, are fruits characterized by a fleshy exterior surrounding a hard pit or \"stone\" that encases the seed. They are typically grown in temperate climates and are valued for their sweet, juicy flesh and nutritional content, which includes vitamins, minerals, and antioxidants." .

<R8YfXog92OHuOj0eFmQBB4> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Skin Cancer" ;
    dc:source <https://www.ssa.gov/disability/professionals/bluebook/13.00-NeoplasticDiseases-Malignant-Adult.htm#13_03> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RDF3VrmH1eapfkrSQstevLs> ;
    skos:altLabel "Cutaneous Carcinoma",
        "Dermal Cancer",
        "Epidermal Carcinoma" ;
    skos:definition "Skin cancer is a type of cancer that begins in the cells of the skin. It includes various forms, such as basal cell carcinoma, squamous cell carcinoma, and melanoma, each requiring specific treatments like surgery, radiation therapy, chemotherapy, and immunotherapy." .

<R8aVRgLAjmuf0OiloIoc9pm> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Semi-Proportional Electoral System" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R7OQ65vKuOBSSGgSVYnoMfx> ;
    skos:definition "A semi-proportional electoral system is a voting method that seeks to balance majority rule with proportional representation, allowing for more accurate reflection of voter preferences while still favoring larger parties. Examples include limited voting, cumulative voting, single non-transferable vote, and modified Borda count, which each employ different mechanisms to achieve this balance." .

<R8cGjHXv3vecVd4ZO6HVjo> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Immigration Processing Types" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R9ODLnhxFt38FQNV4BUbRSD> ;
    skos:definition "\"Immigration processing type\" refers to the specific stage or procedure within the immigration process, such as visa applications, port of entry checks, change of status requests, or extensions, each with its own requirements and documentation. These steps are crucial for determining an individual's eligibility for entry, residency, or other immigration-related benefits in a destination country." .

<R8fSoRbI3U75OLeBvp4PzG2> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Publisher" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R8eT1bTptg5J6ZfnwSUQYpf> ;
    skos:definition "A publisher is an individual, group, or organization responsible for producing and distributing printed or digital content, such as books, newspapers, magazines, or software. Publishers oversee the editorial, production, and marketing processes to bring a work from manuscript or concept to a finished, available product" .

<R8fcGNgScyMlOAFxW5Omw5Y> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Rape" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ucr.fbi.gov/nibrs/2012/resources/nibrs-offense-definitions> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <R8TvbewYypS9Uy4y5JGIwEH> ;
    skos:altLabel "Vergewaltigung"@de-de,
        "Rape"@en-gb,
        "Violación"@es-es,
        "Violación"@es-mx,
        "Viol"@fr-fr,
        "אונס"@he-il,
        "बलात्कार"@hi-in,
        "レイプ"@ja-jp,
        "Estupro"@pt-br,
        "强奸"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "The carnal knowledge of a person, forcibly and/or against that person’s will or not forcibly or against the person’s will in instances where the victim is incapable of giving consent because of his/her temporary or permanent mental or physical incapacity." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Sexual Assault" .

<R8i9ifFKGOUWKWVHDXvxgR1> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Domesticated Animal" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RBbKQavNM8iQqNfPu2byT6X> ;
    skos:altLabel "Domestic Animal",
        "Tame Animal" ;
    skos:definition "A Domesticated Animal is a species that has been bred and adapted over generations to live in close association with humans, often providing companionship, labor, or products such as milk, eggs, and wool. These animals are typically dependent on humans for food, shelter, and care." .

<R8jiyejSsdOkKDAWQ9ZPcjj> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Antitrust - Vertical Claims" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RCFPWMbdFLbplboOqvI77Jh> ;
    skos:altLabel "Wettbewerbsrecht - Vertikale Ansprüche"@de-de,
        "Antitrust - Vertical Claims"@en-gb,
        "Antimonopolio - Reclamaciones Verticales"@es-es,
        "Antimonopolio - Reclamaciones Verticales"@es-mx,
        "Antitrust - Revendications verticales"@fr-fr,
        "אנטיטרוסט - טענות אנכיות"@he-il,
        "एंटीट्रस्ट - लंबवत दावे"@hi-in,
        "独占禁止法 - 垂直クレーム"@ja-jp,
        "Antitruste - Reivindicações verticais"@pt-br,
        "反垄断 - 垂直索赔"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "Antitrust - Vertical Claims refer to legal claims related to antitrust violations that involve vertical relationships between parties, such as price fixing, market allocation, and tying arrangements." .

<R8lpuELvxz47gLtnJQsIzqx> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Health and Personal Care Retailers Industry" ;
    dc:identifier "RET-HPCS" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.naics.com/six-digit-naics/?code=456> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RDfdmGR6iPi4k2t6ecIUBkP> ;
    skos:altLabel "Health and Personal Care Stores",
        "Gesundheits- und Körperpflegeeinzelhandelsbranche"@de-de,
        "Health and Personal Care Store Industry"@en-gb,
        "Industria de tiendas de salud y cuidado personal"@es-es,
        "Industria de tiendas de salud y cuidado personal"@es-mx,
        "Industrie des magasins de santé et de soins personnels"@fr-fr,
        "תעשיית חנויות בריאות וטיפוח אישי"@he-il,
        "स्वास्थ्य और व्यक्तिगत देखभाल स्टोर उद्योग"@hi-in,
        "健康と個人用品店業界"@ja-jp,
        "Indústria de lojas de saúde e cuidados pessoais"@pt-br,
        "健康和个人护理商店行业"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "Industries in the Health and Personal Care Retailers subsector retail health and personal care merchandise.  Establishments in this subsector are characterized principally by the products they retail, and some health and personal care retailers have specialized staff including pharmacists, opticians, and other professionals engaged in retailing, advising customers, and/or fitting the product sold to the customer's needs." ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "HPCS" .

<R8sg6ZiCdJPHi2EUyh7BiZf> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Social Assistance Industry" ;
    dc:identifier "HTC-SOCA" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RCSG4k3ah1Pu5YgPexPgOmL> ;
    skos:altLabel "Social Assistance",
