    skos:definition "Organizational Board Roles refer to the positions and responsibilities assigned to individuals on a board of directors, including governance, oversight, and strategic planning functions. These roles are designed to ensure effective leadership, compliance, and decision-making within an organization." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Board Positions" .

