        <RBCzyIAi2Hjl80hfQr8wAMR> ;
    skos:altLabel "IP Applications",
        "IP Regulatory Document" ;
    skos:definition "An Intellectual Property Regulatory Document, such as a Patent Application, Trademark Application, or Copyright Application, is a formal submission to a governmental body to secure legal protection for a specific piece of intellectual property. It outlines the details of the intellectual property, provides evidence of its originality or distinctiveness, and serves as the basis for granting or denying the intellectual property rights" .

<R7O2ClQ73HLZZLgFgtNbVTF> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Blood Disorders" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RD12xMI38C0qkkx19ISgWWD> ;
    skos:altLabel "Hematopathy" ;
    skos:definition "Hematological Disorders encompass a range of conditions affecting the blood and its components, including red blood cells, white blood cells, platelets, and plasma. These disorders can impact blood production, function, and composition, leading to symptoms such as anemia, bleeding, or increased risk of infection." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Hematological Disorders" .

