<R9UCFdrDU3BruofWcw9xAr5> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Parables of the Kingdom" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RBwnjqdPUZaR0T0pghMXTl6>,
        <RPq5X7NPLuzbWzt3kLIhkw> ;
    skos:altLabel "Parables of the Kingdom of God"^^xsd:string,
        "Proclaiming the Kingdom"^^xsd:string,
        "Reign of God Parables"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Parables of the Kingdom means the parables taught by Jesus Christ that reveal the nature, growth, value, and demands of the Kingdom of God. Parables of the Kingdom disclose divine realities through ordinary images while inviting hearers to conversion and discernment."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example """"And preach as you go, saying, 'The kingdom of heaven is at hand.' Heal the sick, raise the dead, cleanse lepers, cast out demons. You received without pay, give without pay."
(Matthew 10:7-8)"""^^xsd:string,
        "Jesus compares the Kingdom of God to a mustard seed that grows into a great tree."^^xsd:string,
        "The Gospel of Matthew presents the parable of the sower to explain different responses to the word of the Kingdom."^^xsd:string .

<R9X6xDAYYSYwCeCqMHt5G75> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Peace" ;
    rdfs:comment "In a global Catholic ontology, Peace represents the \"tranquillity of order\" (tranquillitas ordinis) as defined by Saint Augustine. The Church views it not merely as a passive absence of war, but as a dynamic and positive state of social harmony achieved through the active practice of justice and charity."^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RB4yg0TUPW2kfmcnhwGTCIV> ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RDVeTFioc9tEXhTGI2gd6Nn> ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
            owl:someValuesFrom <RDwDmcN0z56JIukw0vYcGte> ],
        <R73hoH1RXYjBTYiGfolpsAF> ;
    skos:altLabel "Cessation of Hostilities"^^xsd:string,
        "Shalom"^^xsd:string,
        "Social Harmony"^^xsd:string,
        "Tranquillity of Order"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "Peace is a condition in which conflict or violence has ceased and parties refrain from hostilities. Legal and normative systems treat peace as both a factual state and a status with consequences for rights, duties, and enforcement mechanisms. Peace is the stable and harmonious social order resulting from the practice of justice and the recognition of human dignity. It requires the constant protection of rights, the equitable distribution of goods, and the sincere desire for reconciliation among all members of the human family."^^xsd:string ;
    skos:example "Establishing a community-based mediation program to foster reconciliation after a period of intense civil unrest."^^xsd:string,
        "Implementing a comprehensive peace treaty that addresses the root causes of systemic injustice between two formerly warring nations."^^xsd:string,
        "Promoting an international culture of dialogue that prioritizes the common good over individual or nationalistic interests."^^xsd:string .

