    skos:definition "Legal System Types refer to the various frameworks of laws, rules, and institutions that govern the legal processes and procedures within a jurisdiction. These systems encompass distinct traditions, principles, and methodologies that have evolved over time, influenced by cultural, religious, and historical factors." .

