    skos:definition "Claims Against Real Estate Agents and Brokers refers to legal actions taken against individuals or companies who act as intermediaries in real estate transactions, alleging breach of duty or negligence in their representation of clients." .

<REFNhmFYG6yk3W0RPLFV6g> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Neurocognitive Disorders" ;
    dc:source <https://www.ssa.gov/disability/professionals/bluebook/12.00-MentalDisorders-Adult.htm#12_00B1>,
        <https://www.ssa.gov/disability/professionals/bluebook/12.00-MentalDisorders-Adult.htm#12_02> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RN3TubQIlusDFnPgrNAk8D> ;
    skos:definition "Neurocognitive Disorders are characterized by a clinically significant decline in cognitive functioning that impacts memory, executive functions, language, visual-spatial abilities, and other cognitive domains. Symptoms may include disturbances in memory, planning, perception, and social judgment, with various conditions falling under this category due to medical, neurological, or substance-related causes." .

