<RDXLO9MacR7nBfLLV0hskma> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Operational Concepts"@en ;
    skos:definition "Operational Concepts are standardized concepts that describe how Church-related activities, records, communications, and processes function in practice. They provide implementation-level structure—such as identifiers, statuses, languages, modalities, and transactional attributes—without asserting doctrine or moral teaching."@en .

<RDeZlellOVEkUBkTSbLgxUC> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Student" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RCEDL3kMYgjFUEOhOyGp3IE> ;
    skos:definition "A student is an individual who is enrolled in an educational institution, such as a school, college, or university, for the purpose of acquiring knowledge, skills, and qualifications. Students engage in a structured learning process to pursue academic or vocational goals, typically under the guidance of teachers or instructors." .

<RDfdmGR6iPi4k2t6ecIUBkP> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Retail Trade Industry" ;
    dc:identifier "RET" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.naics.com/six-digit-naics/?code=44>,
        <https://www.naics.com/six-digit-naics/?code=45> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <RDIwFaFcH4KY0gwEY0QlMTp> ;
    skos:altLabel "Retail Trade",
        "Einzelhandelsbranche"@de-de,
        "Retail Trade Industry"@en-gb,
        "Industria del Comercio Minorista"@es-es,
        "Industria del Comercio al por Menor"@es-mx,
        "Industrie du commerce de détail"@fr-fr,
        "תעשיית מסחר בקמעונאות"@he-il,
        "खुदरा व्यापार उद्योग"@hi-in,
        "小売業界"@ja-jp,
        "Indústria do comércio varejista"@pt-br,
        "零售贸易行业"@zh-cn ;
    skos:definition "The Retail Trade industry group comprises establishments engaged in retailing merchandise, generally without transformation, and rendering services incidental to the sale of merchandise. The retailing process is the final step in the distribution of merchandise; retailers are, therefore, organized to sell merchandise in small quantities to the general public. This sector comprises two main types of retailers: store and nonstore retailers." ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "RET" .

