<RCx3rNyJdykIdu45Cr4ajaK> a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "folio:appealsTo" ;
    rdfs:domain <RBjHwNNG2ASVmasLFU42otk>,
        <RCEDL3kMYgjFUEOhOyGp3IE>,
        <RCFgxBbypUKKsDDOJ1iOk36> ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf owl:topObjectProperty ;
    skos:definition "\"Appeals to\" in a legal setting refers to the process of challenging and seeking review of a lower court's decision by a higher court. This action is initiated by the party dissatisfied with the trial court's judgment, aiming for a reassessment of the legal and factual determinations made, based on the assertion of errors in the application of law or procedural missteps. It also relates to where a case heard by a trial court \"appeals to\" the appellate court (e.g., SDNY appeals to Second Circuit)." .

